WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Welcome to
the Huberman Lab podcast,

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.920
where we discuss science
and science-based tools

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.700
for everyday life.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.070
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.930
I'm Andrew Huberman,
and I'm a professor

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.940
of neurobiology
and ophthalmology

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.410
at Stanford School of Medicine.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.570
Today we are
discussing fertility.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.970
We will discuss male fertility
and female fertility.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.140
And I should mention that
today's discussion is not just

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.450
for people who are seeking
to conceive children

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.790
or who want to know how their
children were conceived,

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.470
but it's really for everybody.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.950
And I say that because it
is the story of all of us.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.800
All of us are here
because a specialized set

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.200
of cells, called germ cells--

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.853
that is the sperm and the egg.

00:00:39.853 --> 00:00:41.770
And I'll make it very
clear why they're called

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.020
germ cells a little bit later.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.620
It has nothing to
do with infection.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:50.290
But it's because a sperm cell
and an egg cell arrived at one

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:54.138
another, either in vivo-- inside
of our mother-- or in vitro--

00:00:54.138 --> 00:00:55.930
so-called in vitro
fertilization-- and then

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.590
we're implanted into our
mother and became us.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:02.800
And so understanding
the process of how

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.130
the egg cell and the
sperm cell came to be

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.930
is really the key
to understanding

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.263
how that fertilization
process came to be.

00:01:10.263 --> 00:01:11.680
Now, I know
everyone's thinking, I

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.202
know how fertilization occurs.

00:01:13.202 --> 00:01:15.160
It occurs through sexual
intercourse and so on.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.050
And we'll talk a
little bit about that.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.750
But I promise you
that if you understand

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.280
the menstrual cycle--

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.830
and the menstrual cycle
in today's conversation

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.950
can best be thought of as
a biological cycle that

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:30.940
occurs in females that allows
the potential for fertilization

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.040
by the sperm, because
that's really what it is,

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.080
and it's a beautifully
orchestrated process

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.220
that I'll describe to you.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:39.790
And I should say, all people,
males and females, should

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.950
really understand how the
menstrual cycle works,

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:45.430
how it impacts
fertilization, but also

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.460
how it impacts the brain and
body, behavior, psychology,

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.120
et cetera.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.450
And we'll also talk
about spermatogenesis,

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:56.740
how sperm cells come to
be and how they arrive--

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.450
that is, how they
swim to the egg--

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.810
and the incredible interplay
between the biology

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:05.470
of the sperm and the
biology of the egg

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.770
leads to this incredible thing
that we call embryogenesis

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.930
and the birth of the
child and, of course,

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:16.210
the development of that child
into an infant, a toddler,

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:19.600
an adolescent, a
teen, and an adult.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.790
Today's discussion,
again, is not just

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.550
for those of you that are
seeking to have children.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.420
And I say that because
when you look at the data,

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.870
you look at the literature
on longevity and vitality,

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.550
two themes in biology that
oftentimes people lump together

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.300
but aren't always the
same-- for instance,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.675
there are a lot
of things that we

00:02:38.675 --> 00:02:41.170
can do to increase our
vitality that actually

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:43.450
can harm our longevity.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:47.860
But there are a subset of
biological rules and mechanisms

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.100
that, when aligned,
allow us to maximize both

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.140
our vitality and our longevity.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.430
And I think it's fair to say
that all of those mechanisms

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.650
and tools are housed
in the discussion

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.942
around maximizing fertility.

00:03:01.942 --> 00:03:04.150
And that's true whether or
not you're male or female.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.220
In other words, if
you want children

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.260
or if you don't, if you
already have children

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.850
or if you don't, understanding
how fertility and fertilization

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.670
occurs in the
brain and body will

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.760
allow you to maximize your
vitality and longevity.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.260
And of course,
today's discussion

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.630
will provide an
understanding of the biology

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.420
and many actionable tools that
will also help you conceive

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:26.980
children, if that's your wish.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.020
So of course, as is
characteristic of this podcast,

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.180
we will discuss
science-based tools,

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.860
including behavioral tools, both
the dos and the don'ts, and we

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.250
will discuss nutrition-based
tools and supplementation-based

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.550
tools and some other practices,
including things like

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:46.090
acupuncture, which have quite
good data to support them

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.800
in terms of improving fertility.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.760
And we will discuss why those
certain practices can work.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.890
And we will discuss
prescription drugs

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.820
that your doctor can prescribe
to you if, for instance, you

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.107
have a deficit at the
level of hormone production

00:04:00.107 --> 00:04:02.440
or neurotransmitter production
at the level of the brain

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.520
or the pituitary gland--

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.740
I'll explain what all of
those things are soon--

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:10.030
or the gonads, the ovary and
the testes in females and males

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:12.080
respectively.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.640
Again, by the end
of today's episode,

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.390
you will have a lot of knowledge
and actionable tools related

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.850
to maximizing
fertility, and you will

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.490
have a lot of knowledge and
actionable tools related

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.760
to maximizing vitality
and longevity.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:26.532
Before we begin, I'd
