01:04:18.730 --> 01:04:21.690
So we've covered the
ovulatory cycle in females.

01:04:21.690 --> 01:04:24.240
And I confess, it was
a lot of information

01:04:24.240 --> 01:04:26.370
with a lot of
biological nomenclature.

01:04:26.370 --> 01:04:29.130
But I promise you that
many of those same themes

01:04:29.130 --> 01:04:31.920
and indeed the same
names and nomenclature

01:04:31.920 --> 01:04:33.660
will show up in the
discussion that we're

01:04:33.660 --> 01:04:36.520
going to have now, which is
about the generation of sperm.

01:04:36.520 --> 01:04:40.452
Now, sperm are similar
to eggs in the sense

01:04:40.452 --> 01:04:41.910
that they are part
of the germline.

01:04:41.910 --> 01:04:44.590
They are these protected
cells, protected in the sense

01:04:44.590 --> 01:04:47.620
that the activities
of an individual

01:04:47.620 --> 01:04:52.070
are not going to change the
genetic makeup of those cells.

01:04:52.070 --> 01:04:54.220
Now, again, there are
instances in which

01:04:54.220 --> 01:04:57.730
mutagens, such as
chemicals, could disrupt

01:04:57.730 --> 01:05:00.910
the genomes of the germ
cells in males, just

01:05:00.910 --> 01:05:01.970
as it could in females.

01:05:01.970 --> 01:05:04.510
But in general, the
activities, the things

01:05:04.510 --> 01:05:06.610
that we do, the
experiences we have,

01:05:06.610 --> 01:05:09.410
doesn't tend to change
the genome of those cells.

01:05:09.410 --> 01:05:11.453
However, there are a lot
of lifestyle factors--

01:05:11.453 --> 01:05:13.870
dos and don'ts, nutrition and
supplements and prescription

01:05:13.870 --> 01:05:17.770
drugs, et cetera-- that can
indeed modify the quality

01:05:17.770 --> 01:05:18.850
of the sperm.

01:05:18.850 --> 01:05:20.900
And we'll talk about
what sperm quality means.

01:05:20.900 --> 01:05:27.310
But the point is that the sperm
cell, much like the egg cell,

01:05:27.310 --> 01:05:28.947
are both germline cells.

01:05:28.947 --> 01:05:30.280
They are not like somatic cells.

01:05:30.280 --> 01:05:31.600
They are unique populations.

01:05:31.600 --> 01:05:34.480
And let's just remember what
the job of the sperm cell is.

01:05:34.480 --> 01:05:38.200
The job of the sperm cell is
to deliver the genetic material

01:05:38.200 --> 01:05:42.920
from the father and to do that
in the form of a haploid cell.

01:05:42.920 --> 01:05:47.740
So that means 23
chromosomes, 22 autosomes,

01:05:47.740 --> 01:05:50.445
one so-called sex chromosome--

01:05:50.445 --> 01:05:52.570
again, not sex the verb,
at least not in this case.

01:05:52.570 --> 01:05:54.160
Sex, the verb, is
a discussion we're

01:05:54.160 --> 01:05:57.070
going to have in a few
minutes, but sex the noun.

01:05:57.070 --> 01:06:00.700
The sex chromosome can either
be an X chromosome or a Y

01:06:00.700 --> 01:06:01.970
chromosome.

01:06:01.970 --> 01:06:04.630
So 22 autosomes and
then one sex chromosome

01:06:04.630 --> 01:06:06.910
is going to be contained
within the sperm

01:06:06.910 --> 01:06:09.100
because it's a haploid
cell, not a diploid cell.

01:06:09.100 --> 01:06:11.350
Remember, the egg was diploid,
then it became haploid.

01:06:11.350 --> 01:06:14.617
The sperm cells
are cells that are

01:06:14.617 --> 01:06:16.450
created through the
division of other cells.

01:06:16.450 --> 01:06:18.880
But after that division occurs
through a process called

01:06:18.880 --> 01:06:24.580
meiosis, the sperm cell is
going to contain 23 chromosomes,

01:06:24.580 --> 01:06:27.490
consisting of 22 autosomes
and one sex chromosome.

01:06:27.490 --> 01:06:32.200
And the sperm that manages
to deposit its DNA contents

01:06:32.200 --> 01:06:34.180
into the egg, to
fertilize the egg,

01:06:34.180 --> 01:06:38.470
will either have an X
sex chromosome or a Y sex

01:06:38.470 --> 01:06:39.190
chromosome.

01:06:39.190 --> 01:06:41.560
And the Y sex
chromosome has a number

01:06:41.560 --> 01:06:44.020
of different genes on
that chromosome that

01:06:44.020 --> 01:06:46.870
will suppress, for
instance, the development

01:06:46.870 --> 01:06:49.390
of the female reproductive axis.

01:06:49.390 --> 01:06:52.240
One good example would be the
Müllerian-inhibiting hormone,

01:06:52.240 --> 01:06:53.380
or MIH.

01:06:53.380 --> 01:06:55.790
The gene for
Müllerian-inhibiting hormone,

01:06:55.790 --> 01:06:58.780
which is a hormone that prevents
the formation of the Müllerian

01:06:58.780 --> 01:07:02.410
ducts, which is part of the
female reproductive structure,

01:07:02.410 --> 01:07:07.780
well, that gene controls the
prevention of the development

01:07:07.780 --> 01:07:12.070
of the female genitalia
and in doing so promotes

01:07:12.070 --> 01:07:13.690
the development of
the male genitalia.

01:07:13.690 --> 01:07:15.010
And there are other
examples of genes

01:07:15.010 --> 01:07:16.900
that are on the Y
chromosome that give you

01:07:16.900 --> 01:07:19.227
a what we call male phenotype.

01:07:19.227 --> 01:07:20.560
You have genotype and phenotype.

01:07:20.560 --> 01:07:22.990
By the way, in case you
haven't heard this in a while

01:07:22.990 --> 01:07:24.040
from your high school biology--

01:07:24.040 --> 01:07:25.665
or if you never heard
it, no big deal--

01:07:25.665 --> 01:07:29.260
karyotype is the
complement of chromosome--

01:07:29.260 --> 01:07:30.352
XX or XY.

01:07:30.352 --> 01:07:31.810
And there are
individuals out there

01:07:31.810 --> 01:07:35.530
that are XXY or XYY, a
discussion for our episode

01:07:35.530 --> 01:07:36.760
on sex differentiation.

01:07:36.760 --> 01:07:38.710
That's karyotype with a K.

01:07:38.710 --> 01:07:41.230
Then there's genotype, which
are the genes that you have.

01:07:41.230 --> 01:07:46.840
And then there's phenotype,
spelled P-H-E-N-O-T-Y-P-E,

01:07:46.840 --> 01:07:47.650
phenotype.

01:07:47.650 --> 01:07:51.530
And the phenotype
is how the genes,

01:07:51.530 --> 01:07:54.910
which then code for RNA,
which code for protein,

01:07:54.910 --> 01:07:57.613
how those are expressed in
terms of things like eye color.

01:07:57.613 --> 01:07:58.780
So eye color is a phenotype.

01:07:58.780 --> 01:07:59.800
Height is a phenotype.

01:07:59.800 --> 01:08:00.940
Hair color is a phenotype.

01:08:00.940 --> 01:08:02.930
So you have karyotype,
genotype, and phenotype.

01:08:02.930 --> 01:08:05.650
Well, what we need to do is
we need to bring together

01:08:05.650 --> 01:08:08.710
that sperm, which is
haploidd it contains those 23

01:08:08.710 --> 01:08:10.660
chromosomal strandes--

01:08:10.660 --> 01:08:13.030
with either an X or
a Y. Sex chromosome

01:08:13.030 --> 01:08:14.350
is the 23rd chromosome.

01:08:14.350 --> 01:08:17.899
We need to get that
cell to the egg.

01:08:17.899 --> 01:08:21.170
And so when we talk about
spermatogenesis, of course,

01:08:21.170 --> 01:08:24.069
we are talking about the
generation of sperm cells.

01:08:24.069 --> 01:08:26.410
But what we're really talking
about is the generation

01:08:26.410 --> 01:08:30.310
of cells whose job is to deliver
the genetic material from dad

01:08:30.310 --> 01:08:35.680
to the egg within the female
in a way that increases

01:08:35.680 --> 01:08:38.710
the probability that not only
will that egg be fertilized

01:08:38.710 --> 01:08:42.880
but that it will progress in
a healthy way with each set

01:08:42.880 --> 01:08:44.890
of chromosomes from
mom and from dad--

01:08:44.890 --> 01:08:47.560
each set of 23
chromosomes, that is--

01:08:47.560 --> 01:08:51.850
will progress in a healthy way,
will implant in a healthy way,

01:08:51.850 --> 01:08:56.770
and will maintain and grow in a
healthy way to a healthy embryo

01:08:56.770 --> 01:09:01.180
and child and eventually adult.
That's the job of the sperm.

01:09:01.180 --> 01:09:03.340
So as we talk about
spermatogenesis,

01:09:03.340 --> 01:09:06.067
let's just remember that
and why they're there

01:09:06.067 --> 01:09:06.859
in the first place.

01:09:06.859 --> 01:09:09.550
Now, a few things about
sperm that are interesting,

01:09:09.550 --> 01:09:11.620
besides the fact
that they're haploid

01:09:11.620 --> 01:09:14.213
and besides the fact that,
as you all know, they swim.

01:09:14.213 --> 01:09:15.380
They have a head and a tail.

01:09:15.380 --> 01:09:17.547
They actually have a head,
a mid region, and a tail,

01:09:17.547 --> 01:09:19.729
and that mid region turns
out to be very important.

01:09:19.729 --> 01:09:21.812
It's something we'll come
back to again and again.

01:09:21.812 --> 01:09:24.520
That mid region is really
key for the ability for sperm

01:09:24.520 --> 01:09:27.700
to engage in forward
progression to swim forward.

01:09:27.700 --> 01:09:30.170
It involves the activity
of mitochondria,

01:09:30.170 --> 01:09:33.580
which are involved in
generation of ATP, which

01:09:33.580 --> 01:09:36.340
is involved in all aspects
of energy and all cells.

01:09:36.340 --> 01:09:40.149
But let's just remember that
the sperm are swimming cells.

01:09:40.149 --> 01:09:43.300
And in order to create
a really good swimmer

01:09:43.300 --> 01:09:45.680
or set of swimmers, you
need a couple of things.

01:09:45.680 --> 01:09:49.990
First of all, within the testes
is where the sperm develop.

01:09:49.990 --> 01:09:53.560
And unlike in females
and unlike in the ovary,

01:09:53.560 --> 01:09:55.120
there's no vault of sperm.

01:09:55.120 --> 01:09:57.640
The sperm are continually
being generated.

01:09:57.640 --> 01:10:00.220
It takes about 60
days for sperm to be

01:10:00.220 --> 01:10:02.710
born from their parent cells--

01:10:02.710 --> 01:10:04.760
because cells actually
give rise to other cells,

01:10:04.760 --> 01:10:06.790
that's the it works-- to be
born from their parent cells

01:10:06.790 --> 01:10:08.457
and then matured to
the point where they

01:10:08.457 --> 01:10:09.670
can be a really good swimmer.

01:10:09.670 --> 01:10:13.600
Now, that doesn't mean
that a bunch of sperm

01:10:13.600 --> 01:10:17.560
are made on day one, and then
60 days later, all those sperm

01:10:17.560 --> 01:10:19.390
are deployed in the
form of ejaculate,

01:10:19.390 --> 01:10:21.140
and then the cycle
starts over again.

01:10:21.140 --> 01:10:23.740
So it's a little different than
the ovulatory menstrual cycle.

01:10:23.740 --> 01:10:26.530
Rather, at any given point
in time-- like right now,

01:10:26.530 --> 01:10:29.770
if you have testes, you have
some sperm in your testes that

01:10:29.770 --> 01:10:35.350
are immature and cannot swim,
cannot deliver those contents

01:10:35.350 --> 01:10:35.950
to--

01:10:35.950 --> 01:10:38.770
those genetic contents,
rather-- to the female egg.

01:10:38.770 --> 01:10:40.510
And you have some
sperm that are mature,

01:10:40.510 --> 01:10:43.780
and you very likely have
some sperm that are so mature

01:10:43.780 --> 01:10:46.090
that they are dying off
or that they're dead.

01:10:46.090 --> 01:10:48.730
Almost certainly, also,
regardless of your age,

01:10:48.730 --> 01:10:51.640
you have some sperm that are
healthier than others, that are

01:10:51.640 --> 01:10:53.180
better swimmers than others.

01:10:53.180 --> 01:10:56.150
This is just the way
the system works.

01:10:56.150 --> 01:10:59.212
Now, the process
of spermatogenesis

01:10:59.212 --> 01:11:01.420
involves a couple of things,
but a lot of the players

01:11:01.420 --> 01:11:03.880
are the same as the
process of developing

01:11:03.880 --> 01:11:08.180
the so-called oocyte,
the immature egg.

01:11:08.180 --> 01:11:10.523
We've got GnRH from
the hypothalamus.

01:11:10.523 --> 01:11:11.690
That's going to be a player.

01:11:11.690 --> 01:11:13.888
We have FSH,
follicle-stimulating hormone,

01:11:13.888 --> 01:11:16.430
although the name's a little
bit of a misnomer in the context

01:11:16.430 --> 01:11:19.430
of spermatogenesis, because in
the context of spermatogenesis,

01:11:19.430 --> 01:11:20.563
there is no follicle.

01:11:20.563 --> 01:11:21.980
What we're really
talking about is

01:11:21.980 --> 01:11:26.310
FSH for stimulating the
maturation of the sperm cell,

01:11:26.310 --> 01:11:28.340
so not egg follicle
but sperm cell.

01:11:28.340 --> 01:11:32.390
But we still have GnRH,
FSH, LH, and rather

01:11:32.390 --> 01:11:34.760
than the ovary being the
target of those hormones,

01:11:34.760 --> 01:11:36.480
it's going to be the testes.

01:11:36.480 --> 01:11:40.400
So most everybody should know
that the testes and the ovaries

01:11:40.400 --> 01:11:42.830
are the so-called gonads.

01:11:42.830 --> 01:11:46.250
The testes, of course,
reside outside of the body.

01:11:46.250 --> 01:11:49.160
There are instances
where the testes fail

01:11:49.160 --> 01:11:50.660
to descend during development.

01:11:50.660 --> 01:11:52.570
Certainly, if the
testes don't descend

01:11:52.570 --> 01:11:55.070
on time, that's something that
doctors need to be made aware

01:11:55.070 --> 01:11:56.945
of, the pediatrician
should be made aware of,

01:11:56.945 --> 01:12:00.020
because that can
prevent fertility.

01:12:00.020 --> 01:12:01.020
Why would that be?

01:12:01.020 --> 01:12:03.410
Well, it turns out
that the testes

01:12:03.410 --> 01:12:05.630
reside outside the
body in the scrotum

01:12:05.630 --> 01:12:08.540
because the
temperature conditions

01:12:08.540 --> 01:12:11.030
under which
spermatogenesis can occur

01:12:11.030 --> 01:12:14.420
and under which healthy
sperm can be maintained

01:12:14.420 --> 01:12:20.210
are very restricted and is
approximately 2 degrees cooler

01:12:20.210 --> 01:12:21.990
than the rest of the body.

01:12:21.990 --> 01:12:23.450
This is very important.

01:12:23.450 --> 01:12:26.180
I think this is something that
used to be discussed a lot more

01:12:26.180 --> 01:12:28.880
but isn't discussed
so much these days.

01:12:28.880 --> 01:12:31.053
But keeping the
testes cool enough--

01:12:31.053 --> 01:12:33.470
doesn't necessarily mean keeping
them cold, although there

01:12:33.470 --> 01:12:35.300
is a place for
using cold exposure,

01:12:35.300 --> 01:12:37.700
deliberate cold
exposure, to improve

01:12:37.700 --> 01:12:39.890
sperm quality and
number and perhaps even

01:12:39.890 --> 01:12:40.980
testosterone levels.

01:12:40.980 --> 01:12:42.688
We'll talk about that
a little bit later.

01:12:42.688 --> 01:12:46.190
But keeping the
testes about 2 degrees

01:12:46.190 --> 01:12:49.200
cooler than the rest of
the body is absolutely key.

01:12:49.200 --> 01:12:51.950
If sperm get too hot, they die.

01:12:51.950 --> 01:12:54.590
And if spermatocytes, the
cells that give rise to sperm,

01:12:54.590 --> 01:12:57.620
get too warm, well, then
oftentimes the sperm

01:12:57.620 --> 01:13:00.427
that develop are not
healthy, not healthy

01:13:00.427 --> 01:13:01.260
in a number of ways.

01:13:01.260 --> 01:13:04.370
Either they can't engage in
fast forward progression--

01:13:04.370 --> 01:13:08.450
that is, swimming-- or
they will lack the ability

01:13:08.450 --> 01:13:11.360
to deposit their DNA
contents within the egg.

01:13:11.360 --> 01:13:14.060
So again, whatever is
contained in the ejaculate

01:13:14.060 --> 01:13:16.310
is going to be a mixture of
different sperm qualities.

01:13:16.310 --> 01:13:20.780
And sperm of different ages will
impact the quality, but also

01:13:20.780 --> 01:13:25.130
the temperature under which
those sperm developed is

01:13:25.130 --> 01:13:26.750
going to impact their quality.

01:13:26.750 --> 01:13:29.270
And so we're going to get
into tools a little bit

01:13:29.270 --> 01:13:32.420
later, as I mentioned, but just
to give you a simple takeaway.

01:13:32.420 --> 01:13:36.080
If you are hoping to conceive
in the next 90 days--

01:13:36.080 --> 01:13:38.240
the spermatogenesis
cycle take 60 days,

01:13:38.240 --> 01:13:41.630
but then the sperm actually have
to migrate from the testicle

01:13:41.630 --> 01:13:45.170
into the so-called epididymis,
which is a related structure,

01:13:45.170 --> 01:13:47.330
and then into the
vas deferens and then

01:13:47.330 --> 01:13:49.820
into the urethra, where it
can be part of the ejaculate.

01:13:49.820 --> 01:13:53.210
In order for sperm to
do all that properly,

01:13:53.210 --> 01:13:56.390
undergo that maturation and
then exit in ejaculate in a way

01:13:56.390 --> 01:13:59.930
that's healthy or that
the sperm is healthy,

01:13:59.930 --> 01:14:03.740
if you plan to conceive children
or to try and conceive children

01:14:03.740 --> 01:14:06.980
in the next 90 days, you
definitely want to avoid

01:14:06.980 --> 01:14:10.670
exposing your testicles--
that is, your scrotum--

01:14:10.670 --> 01:14:13.080
to elevated temperatures.

01:14:13.080 --> 01:14:16.190
So that means definitely
avoiding hot tubs,

01:14:16.190 --> 01:14:17.690
definitely avoiding hot baths.

01:14:17.690 --> 01:14:19.910
Now, a brief hot bath
or hot tub or hot shower

01:14:19.910 --> 01:14:22.448
isn't going to be a
problem, although if you're

01:14:22.448 --> 01:14:24.740
really interested in conceiving,
I would avoid hot tubs

01:14:24.740 --> 01:14:27.470
and hot baths as
much as possible.

01:14:27.470 --> 01:14:29.940
Hot showers are probably fine.

01:14:29.940 --> 01:14:32.220
But if you're going to go
into a sauna, for instance,

01:14:32.220 --> 01:14:33.887
you might want to
rethink that decision.

01:14:33.887 --> 01:14:35.900
And if you do decide
to, you almost certainly

01:14:35.900 --> 01:14:39.170
would want to bring a cold
pack in that you could-- well,

01:14:39.170 --> 01:14:41.270
hopefully put some material
between the cold pack

01:14:41.270 --> 01:14:43.460
and the scrotum so you
don't get a cold burn.

01:14:43.460 --> 01:14:48.170
But put something there, but
keep the scrotal tissue cool.

01:14:48.170 --> 01:14:52.760
Keep it cold to cool because
heat exposure can really

01:14:52.760 --> 01:14:55.790
mutate and disrupt
the developing sperm,

01:14:55.790 --> 01:14:57.180
and it can kill sperm.

01:14:57.180 --> 01:15:00.920
And so, again, that would
be for an entire 90 days

01:15:00.920 --> 01:15:03.137
leading up to your
attempts to conceive.

01:15:03.137 --> 01:15:05.720
Again, we'll get into more tools
later, but a number of people

01:15:05.720 --> 01:15:09.530
also have probably heard
of the boxers versus briefs

01:15:09.530 --> 01:15:13.940
controversy, I guess it is,
or whether or not people call

01:15:13.940 --> 01:15:18.320
it going commando with no
underwear of any kind-- boxers,

01:15:18.320 --> 01:15:20.790
briefs, briefs, or
otherwise rather.

01:15:20.790 --> 01:15:23.030
It turns out that the data
on that point to the fact

01:15:23.030 --> 01:15:25.640
that there isn't really a big
difference in terms of sperm

01:15:25.640 --> 01:15:28.910
quality if people
wear boxers or briefs

01:15:28.910 --> 01:15:33.500
or don't wear anything under
their jeans or shorts at all.

01:15:33.500 --> 01:15:37.850
The scrotum has the ability to
move the testicles far enough

01:15:37.850 --> 01:15:39.743
away from the body in
order to achieve lower

01:15:39.743 --> 01:15:40.910
temperatures if it needs to.

01:15:40.910 --> 01:15:42.285
It achieves that
through a muscle

01:15:42.285 --> 01:15:43.940
called the cremaster
muscle, which

01:15:43.940 --> 01:15:46.140
is a really interesting
muscle, believe it or not.

01:15:46.140 --> 01:15:48.140
I was reading up on the
biology of the cremaster

01:15:48.140 --> 01:15:49.160
muscle, something
I never thought

01:15:49.160 --> 01:15:51.890
I'd spend too much time on but
that I ended up spending far

01:15:51.890 --> 01:15:53.393
too much time reading up about.

01:15:53.393 --> 01:15:54.560
And it's really fascinating.

01:15:54.560 --> 01:15:57.710
What you have is a muscle
that is a smooth muscle

01:15:57.710 --> 01:16:01.460
tissue, unlike skeletal muscle,
which is striated muscle,

01:16:01.460 --> 01:16:03.120
that is temperature dependent.

01:16:03.120 --> 01:16:06.920
So it has certain nerve endings,
and it has certain receptors

01:16:06.920 --> 01:16:09.410
on it that allow it to
respond to local temperature

01:16:09.410 --> 01:16:13.280
and then to relax in
order to essentially let

01:16:13.280 --> 01:16:16.210
the testicles to descend further
from the body or to contract

01:16:16.210 --> 01:16:17.960
and bring the testicles
closer to the body

01:16:17.960 --> 01:16:20.720
in order to try and maintain
the optimal temperature range.

01:16:20.720 --> 01:16:23.215
And it turns out the cremaster
muscle can achieve that

01:16:23.215 --> 01:16:25.340
whether or not people are
wearing boxers or briefs.

01:16:25.340 --> 01:16:29.007
Although it stands to
reason that any kind of--

01:16:29.007 --> 01:16:31.340
there's no other name for
it-- undergarments-- you know,

01:16:31.340 --> 01:16:33.757
I don't know why that word
just seems kind of antiquated--

01:16:33.757 --> 01:16:37.550
but undergarment that allows
some movement of the scrotum

01:16:37.550 --> 01:16:39.620
and the testicles should
be sufficient to allow

01:16:39.620 --> 01:16:44.000
these temperature variations to
occur and keep things in range.

01:16:44.000 --> 01:16:47.180
That said, a little bit later,
we'll go into some detail,

01:16:47.180 --> 01:16:47.690
really--

01:16:47.690 --> 01:16:50.090
because it's
important-- as to why,

01:16:50.090 --> 01:16:52.400
for instance, if you are
somebody who has big thighs,

01:16:52.400 --> 01:16:53.875
believe it or not,
that it actually

01:16:53.875 --> 01:16:56.000
can lower sperm count
substantially, whether or not

01:16:56.000 --> 01:16:58.042
the big thighs occur
because you're very muscular

01:16:58.042 --> 01:17:00.830
or the big thighs occur
because you are overweight.

01:17:00.830 --> 01:17:02.520
It can increase the temperature.

01:17:02.520 --> 01:17:04.040
If you're sitting
a lot, increases

01:17:04.040 --> 01:17:05.655
scrotal temperature, for sure.

01:17:05.655 --> 01:17:08.030
And there are some other things
that can increase scrotal

01:17:08.030 --> 01:17:11.180
temperature, seat heaters
in cars, for instance--

01:17:11.180 --> 01:17:14.030
terrible idea, just terrible
idea if you're hoping

01:17:14.030 --> 01:17:16.710
to conceive in the near future--

01:17:16.710 --> 01:17:20.400
and again, hot tub,
things of that sort.

01:17:20.400 --> 01:17:24.950
So temperature modulation
of spermatogenesis and sperm

01:17:24.950 --> 01:17:26.283
quality and function is key.

01:17:26.283 --> 01:17:27.950
That relates a little
bit more to tools.

01:17:27.950 --> 01:17:28.760
But what happens?

01:17:28.760 --> 01:17:31.220
How does the actual
sperm develop?

01:17:31.220 --> 01:17:33.470
Well, contained
within the testicle,

01:17:33.470 --> 01:17:36.830
you have the cells, the
so-called spermatogonia,

01:17:36.830 --> 01:17:38.990
which differentiate into
so-called spermatocytes.

01:17:38.990 --> 01:17:40.490
You don't have to
remember all this.

01:17:40.490 --> 01:17:43.110
And the spermatocytes undergo
this process of meiosis.

01:17:43.110 --> 01:17:45.410
Meiosis is a form of
cell division, which

01:17:45.410 --> 01:17:49.970
reduces the chromosome number to
those 23 individual strands as

01:17:49.970 --> 01:17:51.080
opposed to pairs.

01:17:51.080 --> 01:17:53.447
So it makes them haploid
as opposed to diploid.

01:17:53.447 --> 01:17:56.030
Very, very important for reasons
that we talked about earlier.

01:17:56.030 --> 01:18:00.680
And the meiosis process in
these primordial sperm cells,

01:18:00.680 --> 01:18:04.700
these immature sperm cells, is
similar to the meiosis process

01:18:04.700 --> 01:18:07.760
that occurs in eggs when
the chromosomes segregate in

01:18:07.760 --> 01:18:10.910
that it involves these
spindle-like structures

01:18:10.910 --> 01:18:11.610
within the cell.

01:18:11.610 --> 01:18:12.980
Now, why do I keep
bringing up the spindles?

01:18:12.980 --> 01:18:14.240
Well, it turns out
that the function

01:18:14.240 --> 01:18:16.100
of the spindle in
the egg and the sperm

01:18:16.100 --> 01:18:19.410
is heavily dependent on
mitochondrial function.

01:18:19.410 --> 01:18:22.040
And later when we get into tools
for improving egg and sperm

01:18:22.040 --> 01:18:24.123
quality, you're going to
hear about a lot of tools

01:18:24.123 --> 01:18:25.280
for improving mitochondria.

01:18:25.280 --> 01:18:27.080
And it's not just
because the mitochondria

01:18:27.080 --> 01:18:31.190
are involved in energy-demanding
aspects of cell biology.

01:18:31.190 --> 01:18:34.190
But it's also because the
mitochondria in this context

01:18:34.190 --> 01:18:39.650
are very, very important for
the removal of or the separation

01:18:39.650 --> 01:18:41.300
of one set of
chromosomes to give you

01:18:41.300 --> 01:18:44.430
these two sets of haploid
cells, the egg and the sperm.

01:18:44.430 --> 01:18:49.730
And this is so important because
many failures at fertilization,

01:18:49.730 --> 01:18:53.630
many failures at implantation,
many, many miscarriages,

01:18:53.630 --> 01:18:57.050
and many birth defects that
do survive after birth that

01:18:57.050 --> 01:19:01.430
are very detrimental, such as
trisomies and things like that,

01:19:01.430 --> 01:19:05.180
occur because the spindles
don't effectively pull apart

01:19:05.180 --> 01:19:08.120
the chromosomes in
typically the egg,

01:19:08.120 --> 01:19:10.710
but it can also
occur in the sperm.

01:19:10.710 --> 01:19:12.950
So the spindles and the
fact that mitochondria

01:19:12.950 --> 01:19:15.470
are rich on the spindle are
very important for generating

01:19:15.470 --> 01:19:17.750
these haploid sperm--
again, 23 individual strands

01:19:17.750 --> 01:19:19.400
of chromosomes.

01:19:19.400 --> 01:19:23.040
That's occurring
inside of the testes.

01:19:23.040 --> 01:19:25.880
So there's not as much
long-distance migration

01:19:25.880 --> 01:19:29.870
of the spermatocytes
and the sperm cells

01:19:29.870 --> 01:19:31.837
as there is the
egg just when you

01:19:31.837 --> 01:19:33.920
think about the overall
architecture of the uterus

01:19:33.920 --> 01:19:35.540
and the Fallopian tubes
compared to the testicles,

01:19:35.540 --> 01:19:36.690
but there's still
a lot of movement.

01:19:36.690 --> 01:19:38.270
So within the
testicle, if you were

01:19:38.270 --> 01:19:40.427
to look at the testicle
in cross-section--

01:19:40.427 --> 01:19:42.260
and I prefer to call
it that rather than cut

01:19:42.260 --> 01:19:43.100
the testicle in half.

01:19:43.100 --> 01:19:44.450
Any time you talk about
anatomy, you actually

01:19:44.450 --> 01:19:45.533
talk about slicing things.

01:19:45.533 --> 01:19:48.530
That's what you would do with
a cadaver is what I teach

01:19:48.530 --> 01:19:52.010
and we do in my
laboratory and, frankly,

01:19:52.010 --> 01:19:54.300
in biological laboratories
all over the place.

01:19:54.300 --> 01:19:56.883
But when you talk about it, you
talk about if you were to take

01:19:56.883 --> 01:19:58.917
a visual cross-section
through the testicle,

01:19:58.917 --> 01:20:01.250
what you would find is that
there are a lot of different

01:20:01.250 --> 01:20:05.720
little tubes, a lot of
ducts, D-U-C-T-S, ducts.

01:20:05.720 --> 01:20:06.770
Those are pathways.

01:20:06.770 --> 01:20:10.550
And the main ducts that are
important for this discussion

01:20:10.550 --> 01:20:13.490
are called the
seminiferous tubules.

01:20:13.490 --> 01:20:16.910
So it's a mesh-like
or network structure

01:20:16.910 --> 01:20:18.530
of tubes in the testicle.

01:20:18.530 --> 01:20:23.180
And the immature sperm sit
on a little compartment

01:20:23.180 --> 01:20:24.810
along the edge of those tubes.

01:20:24.810 --> 01:20:27.140
And as they mature, they
move towards the center

01:20:27.140 --> 01:20:27.848
of those tubes.

01:20:27.848 --> 01:20:29.390
And then when they
are mature enough,

01:20:29.390 --> 01:20:33.380
those sperm cells actually drop
into the hollow of the tube,

01:20:33.380 --> 01:20:35.780
and then can travel
through those tubes

01:20:35.780 --> 01:20:40.400
to a structure that's along
the side of the testicle called

01:20:40.400 --> 01:20:42.200
the epididymis.

01:20:42.200 --> 01:20:45.020
The epididymis, again,
is a series of ducts.

01:20:45.020 --> 01:20:47.870
And then the epididymis
converges with something

01:20:47.870 --> 01:20:49.937
called the vas deferens.

01:20:49.937 --> 01:20:51.770
I think in high school,
we all remember this

01:20:51.770 --> 01:20:53.600
by thinking about it's
the vast difference.

01:20:53.600 --> 01:20:55.370
I don't know who
came up with that.

01:20:55.370 --> 01:20:57.182
I think it was a
young girl sitting

01:20:57.182 --> 01:20:58.890
to the left of me that
was like, oh, it's

01:20:58.890 --> 01:20:59.630
like the vast difference.

01:20:59.630 --> 01:21:00.450
I never forgot that.

01:21:00.450 --> 01:21:00.590
I don't know.

01:21:00.590 --> 01:21:01.520
Maybe it was the topic matter.

01:21:01.520 --> 01:21:02.030
Maybe it was her.

01:21:02.030 --> 01:21:03.738
Maybe it was some
combination of the two.

01:21:03.738 --> 01:21:05.900
But in any case, the sperm
go from the seminiferous

01:21:05.900 --> 01:21:09.150
tubules to the
epididymis and then

01:21:09.150 --> 01:21:12.720
to the vas deferens and then
are contained in the ejaculate,

01:21:12.720 --> 01:21:14.700
along with seminal fluid.

01:21:14.700 --> 01:21:18.630
Now, the seminal fluid
is the carrier fluid

01:21:18.630 --> 01:21:21.427
for the sperm themselves.

01:21:21.427 --> 01:21:23.010
This is important
because it turns out

01:21:23.010 --> 01:21:26.160
that a lot of things that can
both negatively or positively

01:21:26.160 --> 01:21:29.460
impact the quality of the
sperm relates not just

01:21:29.460 --> 01:21:31.890
to the sperm cells themselves
and the temperature

01:21:31.890 --> 01:21:35.310
of the environment that
they were matured in,

01:21:35.310 --> 01:21:38.370
but also to the semen quality.

01:21:38.370 --> 01:21:43.890
For instance, if you are a heavy
drinker, if you are a smoker,

01:21:43.890 --> 01:21:47.700
or if you are a regular
user of cannabis,

01:21:47.700 --> 01:21:51.330
especially if you smoke
cannabis or vape cannabis,

01:21:51.330 --> 01:21:54.660
you create a lot of
reactive oxygen species

01:21:54.660 --> 01:21:57.810
that disrupt the chemistry
of the seminal fluid, which

01:21:57.810 --> 01:21:59.140
disrupts the sperm cells.

01:21:59.140 --> 01:22:01.530
So it's not a direct action
always on the sperm cell

01:22:01.530 --> 01:22:02.770
itself, although it can be.

01:22:02.770 --> 01:22:07.418
So for instance, in the form
of smoked tobacco or cannabis,

01:22:07.418 --> 01:22:09.210
there are a lot of
carcinogens and mutagens

01:22:09.210 --> 01:22:12.330
that actually mutate the DNA,
can cause DNA fragmentation,

01:22:12.330 --> 01:22:13.530
and debilitate sperm.

01:22:13.530 --> 01:22:17.940
But there are also a lot of
things created by smoking

01:22:17.940 --> 01:22:20.910
in particular, regardless
of what's being smoked,

01:22:20.910 --> 01:22:24.150
that can create elevated
reactive oxygen species

01:22:24.150 --> 01:22:28.770
and disrupt the seminal fluid
that the sperm are contained

01:22:28.770 --> 01:22:31.230
in in the so-called
ejaculate, the semen.

01:22:31.230 --> 01:22:35.010
Now, this will also become a
relevant conversation later

01:22:35.010 --> 01:22:37.560
when we briefly talk
about vasectomies.

01:22:37.560 --> 01:22:41.400
Vasectomies are
literally a cutting

01:22:41.400 --> 01:22:45.060
of the vas deferens, which
leads to a situation,

01:22:45.060 --> 01:22:46.890
provided the surgery
was done correctly,

01:22:46.890 --> 01:22:50.435
where men can still achieve
all the other aspects

01:22:50.435 --> 01:22:51.060
of intercourse.

01:22:51.060 --> 01:22:53.070
They can still achieve erection.

01:22:53.070 --> 01:22:54.930
They can still achieve orgasm.

01:22:54.930 --> 01:22:57.180
They can still ejaculate.

01:22:57.180 --> 01:23:00.280
But when they ejaculate, the
seminal fluid is released,

01:23:00.280 --> 01:23:02.820
but there are no sperm contained
within the seminal fluid.

01:23:02.820 --> 01:23:04.770
And it turns out
that vasectomies

01:23:04.770 --> 01:23:07.410
are a very effective
form of birth control.

01:23:07.410 --> 01:23:09.900
And they always check
to see if zero sperm

01:23:09.900 --> 01:23:11.457
and confirm that
zero sperm are being

01:23:11.457 --> 01:23:12.540
released in the ejaculate.

01:23:12.540 --> 01:23:13.985
They are reversible.

01:23:13.985 --> 01:23:17.730
And that is, vasectomies are
reversible, but not always.

01:23:17.730 --> 01:23:19.980
There are a subset of cases
where it's not reversible,

01:23:19.980 --> 01:23:22.147
in which case if people
still want to have children,

01:23:22.147 --> 01:23:25.350
you have to go in and actually
surgically extract sperm

01:23:25.350 --> 01:23:26.610
from the testicles.

01:23:26.610 --> 01:23:32.010
But it's a process in which
the vas deferens is altered

01:23:32.010 --> 01:23:34.290
or severed in a way that
the sperm can't actually

01:23:34.290 --> 01:23:35.960
exit the testicle.

01:23:35.960 --> 01:23:37.710
They can get into the
epididymis, usually,

01:23:37.710 --> 01:23:41.182
but not into the vas deferens
and so on and so forth.

01:23:41.182 --> 01:23:43.140
So if you've ever wondered
what a vasectomy is,

01:23:43.140 --> 01:23:44.340
that's what a vasectomy is.

01:23:44.340 --> 01:23:48.833
And I mentioned vasectomy
now because it illustrates

01:23:48.833 --> 01:23:51.000
the difference between the
seminal fluid, the semen,

01:23:51.000 --> 01:23:54.240
and the sperm that
the semen contain.

01:23:54.240 --> 01:23:59.010
So 60 days to generate the
sperm, another two weeks

01:23:59.010 --> 01:24:02.160
or so for the sperm to travel
through the various ducts

01:24:02.160 --> 01:24:05.190
to the point where they can
be contained in the ejaculate.

01:24:05.190 --> 01:24:07.950
Let's talk about the
sperm cells themselves.

01:24:07.950 --> 01:24:12.180
The sperm cells, again,
have these 23 pairs

01:24:12.180 --> 01:24:13.890
of single-strand chromosomes.

01:24:13.890 --> 01:24:14.920
They're haploid.

01:24:14.920 --> 01:24:16.830
They have either an X
or a Y sex chromosome

01:24:16.830 --> 01:24:19.110
as the 23rd so-called
sex chromosome.

01:24:19.110 --> 01:24:21.000
And as we all know,
they have a head.

01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:24.190
The head tends to be
oval in most cases.

01:24:24.190 --> 01:24:27.720
The head contains very
important enzymes and proteins

01:24:27.720 --> 01:24:30.990
that are designed to fuse
with the much larger egg

01:24:30.990 --> 01:24:33.570
and to actually take the
membrane of the sperm cell

01:24:33.570 --> 01:24:40.580
and combine to actually mesh
with the egg cell's membrane

01:24:40.580 --> 01:24:44.700
and then deliver the genetic
contents to the egg cell,

01:24:44.700 --> 01:24:46.880
in other words, to
fertilize the egg cell.

01:24:46.880 --> 01:24:50.480
Now, just behind the head is a
region called the mid region.

01:24:50.480 --> 01:24:54.290
That mid region is a
slightly thickened region.

01:24:54.290 --> 01:24:57.080
And here, of course, I'm
talking about healthy sperm cell

01:24:57.080 --> 01:24:57.680
morphology.

01:24:57.680 --> 01:24:59.330
Morphology simply means shape.

01:24:59.330 --> 01:25:02.450
A mid region-- that
mid region has a bunch

01:25:02.450 --> 01:25:04.580
of things related
to cell motility

01:25:04.580 --> 01:25:07.560
and to the forward
progression of the cells.

01:25:07.560 --> 01:25:10.555
First of all, it is chock a
block full of mitochondria.

01:25:10.555 --> 01:25:11.930
In fact, if you
were to look just

01:25:11.930 --> 01:25:14.240
behind the head of the
sperm, what you'd see

01:25:14.240 --> 01:25:18.647
is that it is completely
surrounded by mitochondria.

01:25:18.647 --> 01:25:21.230
There are mitochondria elsewhere
in the cell, but most of them

01:25:21.230 --> 01:25:23.063
are contained in this
mid region compartment

01:25:23.063 --> 01:25:25.970
just behind the
head of the sperm.

01:25:25.970 --> 01:25:30.650
And that thick region is where
the tail movement of the sperm,

01:25:30.650 --> 01:25:37.850
the flagellation back and forth,
is actually generated from.

01:25:37.850 --> 01:25:40.730
Much like if you were to
hold a rope, like a battle

01:25:40.730 --> 01:25:45.020
rope in the gym, and you
were to whip the battle rope,

01:25:45.020 --> 01:25:47.090
the whip at the
one end of the rope

01:25:47.090 --> 01:25:52.160
is what allows for the sort
of-- let's just call it

01:25:52.160 --> 01:25:53.870
what it is-- the
curves in the rope,

01:25:53.870 --> 01:25:55.730
the oscillations, the
rising and falling

01:25:55.730 --> 01:25:57.770
of the rope all the
way out to the end.

01:25:57.770 --> 01:26:02.645
It is the force of the whip
right at that end that with

01:26:02.645 --> 01:26:04.520
the battle rope you're
doing with your hand--

01:26:04.520 --> 01:26:07.460
and with the sperm, that is
occurring just behind the head

01:26:07.460 --> 01:26:08.300
of the sperm--

01:26:08.300 --> 01:26:11.660
that is actually going
to dictate how fast

01:26:11.660 --> 01:26:14.150
and how well that
sperm can swim.

01:26:14.150 --> 01:26:16.700
And indeed, the sperm
has to swim very far.

01:26:16.700 --> 01:26:17.510
How far?

01:26:17.510 --> 01:26:19.340
Well, on a relative scale--

01:26:19.340 --> 01:26:22.820
and again, these are estimations
because they're going to be--

01:26:22.820 --> 01:26:23.750
how should we say?

01:26:23.750 --> 01:26:26.900
There will be differences
in the distance

01:26:26.900 --> 01:26:33.020
from the head of the penis and
where the ejaculation occurs

01:26:33.020 --> 01:26:35.780
to the cervix, depending
on the relative size

01:26:35.780 --> 01:26:38.270
of the vaginal canal
and the penis that

01:26:38.270 --> 01:26:40.220
delivers the ejaculate
to the vaginal canal.

01:26:40.220 --> 01:26:44.570
But once the sperm arrive
at the cervix, which

01:26:44.570 --> 01:26:47.420
is at the back of
the vaginal canal

01:26:47.420 --> 01:26:49.340
just at the opening
to the uterus,

01:26:49.340 --> 01:26:52.940
once the sperm arrive
there, the distance

01:26:52.940 --> 01:26:55.880
from the cervix to
the egg, of course,

01:26:55.880 --> 01:26:58.010
will vary depending
on where that egg is

01:26:58.010 --> 01:27:00.920
in its ovulatory
trajectory, its pathway.

01:27:00.920 --> 01:27:04.430
But it is akin, if
you scale for size,

01:27:04.430 --> 01:27:08.910
to the distance between Los
Angeles and San Francisco,

01:27:08.910 --> 01:27:10.550
which is many, many
hundreds of miles.

01:27:10.550 --> 01:27:12.710
So those sperm have
to swim very far.

01:27:12.710 --> 01:27:16.100
Now, of course, if the sperm are
delivered in the vaginal canal

01:27:16.100 --> 01:27:19.015
somewhat further away, they
will have further to go.

01:27:19.015 --> 01:27:21.140
If they're delivered right
at the cervical opening,

01:27:21.140 --> 01:27:22.820
they will have less far to go.

01:27:22.820 --> 01:27:27.600
The very effective swimming
sperm swim very fast.

01:27:27.600 --> 01:27:29.720
So they are able to
accomplish that distance

01:27:29.720 --> 01:27:30.920
in just a few days.

01:27:30.920 --> 01:27:34.040
And this relates to
a discussion that we

01:27:34.040 --> 01:27:35.840
will get into in
a lot more detail

01:27:35.840 --> 01:27:39.740
later as to how often couples
should have intercourse

01:27:39.740 --> 01:27:41.313
if they're trying to conceive.

01:27:41.313 --> 01:27:43.230
Many people might think,
well, it's every day.

01:27:43.230 --> 01:27:46.280
However, the more frequent
the ejaculation, the lower

01:27:46.280 --> 01:27:49.040
the concentration of
sperm in each ejaculate.

01:27:49.040 --> 01:27:51.110
So this is not a
discussion about how often

01:27:51.110 --> 01:27:53.570
to have intercourse depending
to your preferences,

01:27:53.570 --> 01:27:55.760
for pleasure or bonding
or whatever reason.

01:27:55.760 --> 01:27:58.610
This is a discussion about
how often to have intercourse

01:27:58.610 --> 01:28:02.030
in order to optimize the
probability of fertilization

01:28:02.030 --> 01:28:02.810
of the egg.

01:28:02.810 --> 01:28:05.520
There's some general rules
that, of course, come to mind,

01:28:05.520 --> 01:28:10.350
which is ejaculations close
to ovulation-- both before,

01:28:10.350 --> 01:28:12.830
during, or sometimes after--

01:28:12.830 --> 01:28:15.650
are obviously advantageous.

01:28:15.650 --> 01:28:18.620
But you will also hear
OB/GYNs and urologist

01:28:18.620 --> 01:28:21.290
suggesting intercourse
every other day

01:28:21.290 --> 01:28:24.020
leading up to the
day of ovulation,

01:28:24.020 --> 01:28:26.540
starting about three
to four days out

01:28:26.540 --> 01:28:28.340
from the day of ovulation.

01:28:28.340 --> 01:28:30.170
So we got a little
bit sidetracked,

01:28:30.170 --> 01:28:34.598
albeit I think appropriately so,
in focusing on fertilization.

01:28:34.598 --> 01:28:36.890
But what we were talking
about right up until the point

01:28:36.890 --> 01:28:39.840
of that is the anatomy
of the sperm itself,

01:28:39.840 --> 01:28:41.450
which is the head,
the mid region that

01:28:41.450 --> 01:28:44.280
contains all those
mitochondria, and then the tail.

01:28:44.280 --> 01:28:47.750
Now, what we haven't discussed
is the actual generation

01:28:47.750 --> 01:28:48.540
of the sperm.

01:28:48.540 --> 01:28:51.570
So if you're a male
or if you're a female,

01:28:51.570 --> 01:28:53.570
I think it's really
important to understand

01:28:53.570 --> 01:28:56.810
how spermatogenesis works.

01:28:56.810 --> 01:29:00.050
Spermatogenesis works
in much in the same way

01:29:00.050 --> 01:29:03.578
that the generation and
maturation of eggs work,

01:29:03.578 --> 01:29:05.120
although, as I
mentioned before, it's

01:29:05.120 --> 01:29:08.690
going to occur ongoing
throughout the cycle

01:29:08.690 --> 01:29:11.630
of the male's life
after puberty.

01:29:11.630 --> 01:29:14.270
We already talked about
puberty, and I'll just

01:29:14.270 --> 01:29:16.100
cover this in two
or three sentences

01:29:16.100 --> 01:29:17.480
as it relates to males.

01:29:17.480 --> 01:29:21.350
And it's essentially
the same thing.

01:29:21.350 --> 01:29:24.350
The hypothalamus, up until
the point of puberty,

01:29:24.350 --> 01:29:27.620
is providing suppression
of the release

01:29:27.620 --> 01:29:29.180
of gonadotropin-releasing
hormone.

01:29:29.180 --> 01:29:33.320
Then some biological clock,
which is still not clearly

01:29:33.320 --> 01:29:38.090
understood-- it's probably not
leptin coming from body fat.

01:29:38.090 --> 01:29:40.805
Again, unlike in the female,
it's probably not leptin

01:29:40.805 --> 01:29:41.680
coming from body fat.

01:29:41.680 --> 01:29:44.920
But some other signal
arrives to the hypothalamus,

01:29:44.920 --> 01:29:46.870
removes that
inhibition, and GnRH,

01:29:46.870 --> 01:29:48.850
gonadotropin-releasing
hormone, is now

01:29:48.850 --> 01:29:50.500
released onto the pituitary.

01:29:50.500 --> 01:29:52.870
A bunch of hormones are
deployed from the pituitary

01:29:52.870 --> 01:29:53.660
as a consequence.

01:29:53.660 --> 01:29:56.590
The two most important ones for
the context of this discussion

01:29:56.590 --> 01:30:00.290
are follicle-stimulating
hormone and luteinizing hormone.

01:30:00.290 --> 01:30:02.600
Follicle-stimulating hormone
and luteinizing hormone

01:30:02.600 --> 01:30:05.350
travel to the
testes, and they're

01:30:05.350 --> 01:30:06.770
going to do two main things.

01:30:06.770 --> 01:30:10.090
One, they're going to trigger
the production of testosterone.

01:30:10.090 --> 01:30:12.370
And they're going to
trigger the production

01:30:12.370 --> 01:30:13.780
of the sperm themselves.

01:30:13.780 --> 01:30:15.880
They're going to set in
motion, for essentially

01:30:15.880 --> 01:30:20.470
the rest of the life of the
male, the production of sperm.

01:30:20.470 --> 01:30:22.690
They're going to initiate
the spermatogenesis cycle,

01:30:22.690 --> 01:30:24.232
and that cycle is
going to be ongoing

01:30:24.232 --> 01:30:26.320
at various stages
for different sperm

01:30:26.320 --> 01:30:28.990
for the rest of the man's life.

01:30:28.990 --> 01:30:33.760
This is very different than
the triggering of development

01:30:33.760 --> 01:30:37.600
of oocytes and eggs in females,
where there's an existing

01:30:37.600 --> 01:30:40.345
vault. That vault can be
depleted to the point of zero

01:30:40.345 --> 01:30:41.470
where it can't occur again.

01:30:41.470 --> 01:30:43.870
Men can generate sperm
their entire lifetime.

01:30:43.870 --> 01:30:45.520
Of course, there's
a diminishment

01:30:45.520 --> 01:30:48.880
of sperm production in
very, very late age,

01:30:48.880 --> 01:30:50.260
say, 80s and 90s or 100s.

01:30:50.260 --> 01:30:52.760
But believe it or not, there
are still sperm being produced.

01:30:52.760 --> 01:30:55.030
The quality of those
sperm is another question.

01:30:55.030 --> 01:30:57.160
So everything we're
going to talk about now

01:30:57.160 --> 01:30:59.950
is essentially puberty onward.

01:30:59.950 --> 01:31:02.350
Prior to that,
testicles are present,

01:31:02.350 --> 01:31:04.630
but they're not
generating sperm.

01:31:04.630 --> 01:31:07.360
Ejaculation isn't possible,
or if it is possible,

01:31:07.360 --> 01:31:10.120
it's very unlikely and
unusual, and it's not

01:31:10.120 --> 01:31:12.930
going to contain sperm.

01:31:12.930 --> 01:31:14.730
Everything we're going
to talk about now

01:31:14.730 --> 01:31:20.250
is puberty forward, so puberty
onward to the rest of life.

01:31:20.250 --> 01:31:24.630
And luteinizing hormone
secreted from the pituitary acts

01:31:24.630 --> 01:31:27.930
on the testes and on a
very specific cell type

01:31:27.930 --> 01:31:30.660
in the testes called the Leydig
egg cells, or Leydig cells,

01:31:30.660 --> 01:31:33.000
L-E-Y-D-I-G, the Leydig cells.

01:31:33.000 --> 01:31:37.740
The Leydig cells of the testes
are what produce testosterone.

01:31:37.740 --> 01:31:41.560
Testosterone is going to
have two major effects.

01:31:41.560 --> 01:31:43.290
And here I mean really
major because it

01:31:43.290 --> 01:31:45.630
has many, many hundreds of
effects on different tissues

01:31:45.630 --> 01:31:46.180
of the body.

01:31:46.180 --> 01:31:48.347
In fact, that's the definition
of a hormone, really.

01:31:48.347 --> 01:31:51.090
It's a substance that acts
in an endocrine fashion.

01:31:51.090 --> 01:31:53.460
It can act on the very
tissue that generated it.

01:31:53.460 --> 01:31:55.740
So for instance, testosterone
made by the Leydig cells

01:31:55.740 --> 01:31:57.300
within the testes will
act on the testes,

01:31:57.300 --> 01:31:58.633
as we'll talk about in a moment.

01:31:58.633 --> 01:32:01.000
But it can also act
on other tissues.

01:32:01.000 --> 01:32:02.500
It can act on the
pharynx and larynx

01:32:02.500 --> 01:32:04.500
and deepen the voice, as
it does during puberty.

01:32:04.500 --> 01:32:06.930
It can act on the hair follicles
and generate facial hair.

01:32:06.930 --> 01:32:10.782
It can act on the musculature
and generate protein synthesis

01:32:10.782 --> 01:32:12.240
and development of
muscle, bone, et

01:32:12.240 --> 01:32:13.698
cetera, all the
things we associate

01:32:13.698 --> 01:32:17.410
with puberty and with
testosterone typically.

01:32:17.410 --> 01:32:20.290
Restricting the conversation
to the effects of testosterone

01:32:20.290 --> 01:32:23.200
on the testicle itself
and on spermatogenesis,

01:32:23.200 --> 01:32:25.660
the Leydig cells
make testosterone.

01:32:25.660 --> 01:32:27.945
And keep in mind that
some of that testosterone

01:32:27.945 --> 01:32:29.320
will travel
elsewhere in the body

01:32:29.320 --> 01:32:31.480
and do its thing
for gene expression

01:32:31.480 --> 01:32:34.120
and the more acute effects
of testosterone on the brain

01:32:34.120 --> 01:32:35.680
included.

01:32:35.680 --> 01:32:37.900
But the testosterone
within the testes

01:32:37.900 --> 01:32:40.670
is at extremely
high concentration.

01:32:40.670 --> 01:32:44.830
In fact, the concentration of
intratesticular testosterone

01:32:44.830 --> 01:32:47.970
is at least 100 times higher
than the concentration

01:32:47.970 --> 01:32:49.720
of testosterone anywhere
else in the body,

01:32:49.720 --> 01:32:52.828
even though it's being secreted
into the rest of the body.

01:32:52.828 --> 01:32:54.370
And that's because
there are a number

01:32:54.370 --> 01:32:57.640
of different so-called
binding proteins and enzymes

01:32:57.640 --> 01:33:00.467
that sequester the
testosterone within the testes.

01:33:00.467 --> 01:33:02.300
So the Leydig cells are
making testosterone,

01:33:02.300 --> 01:33:04.840
and a lot of that
testosterone is acting on

01:33:04.840 --> 01:33:06.580
and is restricted to the testes.

01:33:06.580 --> 01:33:11.410
And that turns out to be very
important because testosterone

01:33:11.410 --> 01:33:14.530
within the testes
acts in concert

01:33:14.530 --> 01:33:18.160
with a different biological
program that starts with FSH,

01:33:18.160 --> 01:33:21.370
follicle-stimulating hormone,
that also travels to the testes

01:33:21.370 --> 01:33:25.450
and acts on a very specific
set of cells that are called

01:33:25.450 --> 01:33:27.820
supporting cells or,
more specifically,

01:33:27.820 --> 01:33:29.920
the Sertoli cells.

01:33:29.920 --> 01:33:32.530
The Sertoli cells
are the cells that

01:33:32.530 --> 01:33:36.460
generate something called ABP,
or androgen-binding protein.

01:33:36.460 --> 01:33:39.700
And it is the combination of
testosterone from the Leydig

01:33:39.700 --> 01:33:43.060
cells and ABP from
the Sertoli cells

01:33:43.060 --> 01:33:46.660
that is necessary
for spermatogenesis.

01:33:46.660 --> 01:33:49.240
It's necessary for
those spermatocytes

01:33:49.240 --> 01:33:52.960
to become what will eventually
be healthy, mature sperm that

01:33:52.960 --> 01:33:56.230
have really nice shaped oval
heads, have a mid region,

01:33:56.230 --> 01:33:57.730
chock a block
through mitochondria,

01:33:57.730 --> 01:34:00.340
and can generate a fast
whipping motion of the tail

01:34:00.340 --> 01:34:04.180
to swim from the cervix, or
up the vagina into the cervix,

01:34:04.180 --> 01:34:07.780
and from the cervix to the
egg to fertilize the egg.

01:34:07.780 --> 01:34:10.690
So it's really a basic set
of chemical players that are

01:34:10.690 --> 01:34:13.670
involved here and
so basic, in fact,

01:34:13.670 --> 01:34:16.480
that if you were to disrupt any
one of these chemical players--

01:34:16.480 --> 01:34:19.115
either the luteinizing
hormone, the FSH,

01:34:19.115 --> 01:34:20.740
the testosterone from
the Leydig cells,

01:34:20.740 --> 01:34:23.050
or androgen-binding protein--

01:34:23.050 --> 01:34:27.610
you would observe
pretty marked disruption

01:34:27.610 --> 01:34:31.070
in spermatogenesis or the
elimination of sperm entirely.

01:34:31.070 --> 01:34:33.760
We'll get into a few
deficits in sperm development

01:34:33.760 --> 01:34:36.080
and sperm number and sperm
function a little bit later.

01:34:36.080 --> 01:34:37.780
But just keep in mind--

01:34:37.780 --> 01:34:39.760
or I should say, maybe
sit back and just

01:34:39.760 --> 01:34:42.570
appreciate that the exact
same players generate

01:34:42.570 --> 01:34:45.460
from the hypothalamus,
which causes luteinizing

01:34:45.460 --> 01:34:48.160
hormone and follicle-stimulating
hormone released

01:34:48.160 --> 01:34:51.400
from the pituitary, which
travels to the gonad, which

01:34:51.400 --> 01:34:53.950
in this case is the
testicle, which triggers

01:34:53.950 --> 01:34:55.630
the release of
testosterone from Leydig

01:34:55.630 --> 01:35:00.130
cells, which triggers the
action of the supporting cells,

01:35:00.130 --> 01:35:03.490
the Sertoli cells, which make
androgen-binding protein.

01:35:03.490 --> 01:35:05.230
Testosterone and
androgen-binding protein

01:35:05.230 --> 01:35:08.620
combine and create a
chemical and actually

01:35:08.620 --> 01:35:12.310
a structural milieu in which
those little spermatocytes

01:35:12.310 --> 01:35:14.950
can go from the
walls, from literally

01:35:14.950 --> 01:35:17.530
the walls of the tubes of
the seminiferous tubules,

01:35:17.530 --> 01:35:19.840
can mature into healthy,
well-developed sperm,

01:35:19.840 --> 01:35:23.110
and can hop into those
ducts, those little tubes,

01:35:23.110 --> 01:35:25.900
and then head off to the
epididymis, where they will

01:35:25.900 --> 01:35:29.080
reside-- the epididymis is the
tissue nearby the testicles

01:35:29.080 --> 01:35:31.160
or surrounding one
portion of the testicle--

01:35:31.160 --> 01:35:33.940
and then eventually fuse
with the vas deferens,

01:35:33.940 --> 01:35:36.880
can combine with or be
contained with, rather,

01:35:36.880 --> 01:35:41.410
the seminal fluid, and then can
be ejaculated via the urethra

01:35:41.410 --> 01:35:43.060
into the female,
where then they can

01:35:43.060 --> 01:35:46.840
swim very quickly, effectively
the distance, for them anyway,

01:35:46.840 --> 01:35:48.940
from Los Angeles
to San Francisco,

01:35:48.940 --> 01:35:51.490
over the course of a very
short period of time,

01:35:51.490 --> 01:35:53.710
and fertilize the egg.

01:35:53.710 --> 01:35:56.650
So that's the process of
spermatogenesis, the maturation

01:35:56.650 --> 01:36:00.190
of sperm, which is ongoing
throughout the lifespan

01:36:00.190 --> 01:36:01.660
from puberty onward.

01:36:01.660 --> 01:36:04.540
And in doing so, we talked about
some of the hormonal elements--

01:36:04.540 --> 01:36:07.660
coming from the hypothalamus
and coming from the pituitary,

01:36:07.660 --> 01:36:10.540
and within the testes themselves
the Leydig cells, which

01:36:10.540 --> 01:36:12.320
produce testosterone,
the Sertoli cells,

01:36:12.320 --> 01:36:17.950
which are the support cells that
allow spermatogenesis to occur.

01:36:17.950 --> 01:36:20.320
With that in mind,
next I'd like to think

01:36:20.320 --> 01:36:23.020
about what's actually contained
in the ejaculate in terms

01:36:23.020 --> 01:36:26.163
of numbers of sperm and
what's really being selected

01:36:26.163 --> 01:36:28.330
for in terms of the sperm
that actually successfully

01:36:28.330 --> 01:36:30.880
fertilizes the egg and
what sorts of elements

01:36:30.880 --> 01:36:34.480
come into play in dictating
whether or not fertilization

01:36:34.480 --> 01:36:35.870
will or won't occur.

01:36:35.870 --> 01:36:37.930
And the major themes that
we're going to discuss

01:36:37.930 --> 01:36:41.020
are frequency of
ejaculation, but really

01:36:41.020 --> 01:36:44.590
that's just kind of a proxy
for talking about maximizing

01:36:44.590 --> 01:36:48.940
sperm concentration and quality
of sperm arriving at the egg--

01:36:48.940 --> 01:36:51.280
because, remember, ovulation
and the menstrual cycle

01:36:51.280 --> 01:36:55.580
are really about creating the
opportunity for fertilization.

01:36:55.580 --> 01:36:58.030
And we are also going
to talk about how

01:36:58.030 --> 01:37:01.720
the vaginal duct,
the vagina, and

01:37:01.720 --> 01:37:04.960
the milieu around the cervix
and some other elements

01:37:04.960 --> 01:37:08.410
within the female
herself contribute to

01:37:08.410 --> 01:37:11.518
and support the sperm in
their journey to the egg

01:37:11.518 --> 01:37:13.810
and in the likelihood that
they will fertilize the egg.

01:37:13.810 --> 01:37:17.290
So really what we need to talk
about first is sperm quality.

01:37:17.290 --> 01:37:20.680
And we should also probably
talk about ejaculate quality,

01:37:20.680 --> 01:37:24.820
because, as odd as
that theme might seem,

01:37:24.820 --> 01:37:27.998
really the ejaculate
quality, which

01:37:27.998 --> 01:37:29.540
has a number of
different parameters,

01:37:29.540 --> 01:37:32.620
including the number
of mature sperm

01:37:32.620 --> 01:37:34.780
that are not so mature that
they're swimming slower

01:37:34.780 --> 01:37:36.560
or are dead, but also
quality of sperm.

01:37:36.560 --> 01:37:37.977
They have, for
instance, one tail.

01:37:37.977 --> 01:37:40.300
It's not entirely
uncommon to see sperm

01:37:40.300 --> 01:37:43.060
with two tails because they
just didn't form properly

01:37:43.060 --> 01:37:45.790
or sperm that are
not moving very much.

01:37:45.790 --> 01:37:48.990
In fact, sperm motility is
scored along a scale of 0,

01:37:48.990 --> 01:37:52.990
1, 2, or 3, 3 being the best,
fast forward progressing.

01:37:52.990 --> 01:37:54.940
0 is not moving at all.

01:37:54.940 --> 01:37:57.382
1, they're actually
called twitchers.

01:37:57.382 --> 01:37:59.590
Twitchers are sperm that
sort of just twitch in place

01:37:59.590 --> 01:38:01.990
but don't undergo
forward progression.

01:38:01.990 --> 01:38:06.820
2 is somewhere in between
1 and 3, not surprisingly.

01:38:06.820 --> 01:38:10.825
Different clinics, different
OB/GYNs, different urologists

01:38:10.825 --> 01:38:12.200
will throw out
different numbers.

01:38:12.200 --> 01:38:17.620
But in general, it is hoped
that more than 50% of the sperm

01:38:17.620 --> 01:38:20.470
should be motile in some way
or another, so not scoring a 0,

01:38:20.470 --> 01:38:23.620
but a 1, or 2, or ideally a 3.

01:38:23.620 --> 01:38:25.360
The concentration of sperm--

01:38:25.360 --> 01:38:30.430
of course, if it's higher within
the ejaculate, the total number

01:38:30.430 --> 01:38:33.760
of sperm per milliliter of
ejaculate, if that's higher,

01:38:33.760 --> 01:38:35.290
then there's a
higher probability

01:38:35.290 --> 01:38:38.320
that one of those sperm
will fertilize the egg.

01:38:38.320 --> 01:38:40.000
One thing I didn't
mention before when

01:38:40.000 --> 01:38:42.058
discussing the production
of eggs and ovulation--

01:38:42.058 --> 01:38:43.600
and I probably should
have, so I will

01:38:43.600 --> 01:38:46.480
now-- is that most
often only one

01:38:46.480 --> 01:38:51.060
ovary gives rise to
an ovulating egg.

01:38:51.060 --> 01:38:57.700
It happens, but it's somewhat
rare for two mature eggs, one

01:38:57.700 --> 01:39:00.965
from each ovary, to be deployed
during a single ovulation.

01:39:00.965 --> 01:39:03.590
There's a name for that when it
occurs and both are fertilized.

01:39:03.590 --> 01:39:06.190
It's called fraternal twins.

01:39:06.190 --> 01:39:08.110
If a single egg--

01:39:08.110 --> 01:39:10.240
that, of course, comes
from a single ovary--

01:39:10.240 --> 01:39:14.052
is fertilized and
the egg splits--

01:39:14.052 --> 01:39:16.010
and that's something that
happens further along

01:39:16.010 --> 01:39:19.280
in the process of fertilization
and differentiation

01:39:19.280 --> 01:39:20.070
of the embryo--

01:39:20.070 --> 01:39:23.180
well, then what you get
are identical twins.

01:39:23.180 --> 01:39:26.457
There are other instances that
are quite uncommon in which

01:39:26.457 --> 01:39:28.790
you can get fraternal twins
through other circumstances.

01:39:28.790 --> 01:39:30.457
But in general, that's
the way it works.

01:39:30.457 --> 01:39:32.330
But essentially what
happens is one egg

01:39:32.330 --> 01:39:34.700
from one ovary-- that's
the most common occurrence.

01:39:34.700 --> 01:39:38.810
The sperm, once ejaculated
into the vaginal duct,

01:39:38.810 --> 01:39:42.380
are going to pass
through the cervix

01:39:42.380 --> 01:39:44.570
and then are going to
swim toward the egg.

01:39:44.570 --> 01:39:47.900
The egg could be at
varying locations

01:39:47.900 --> 01:39:50.660
along the female
reproductive axis.

01:39:50.660 --> 01:39:52.880
Now, this is actually
a very important thing

01:39:52.880 --> 01:39:56.645
and actually gets right down
to the safety of both the

01:39:56.645 --> 01:39:58.520
potentially developing
embryo and the mother.

01:39:58.520 --> 01:40:01.190
There is something referred
to as ectopic pregnancy,

01:40:01.190 --> 01:40:04.340
and that's when the
pregnancy actually occurs

01:40:04.340 --> 01:40:05.840
within the Fallopian tubes.

01:40:05.840 --> 01:40:08.360
So the precise location
in which fertilization

01:40:08.360 --> 01:40:11.270
between the sperm and the
egg occurs can vary somewhat.

01:40:11.270 --> 01:40:15.170
But ideally, the fertilized egg
implants into the endometrium

01:40:15.170 --> 01:40:17.330
or the endometrial
lining of the uterus

01:40:17.330 --> 01:40:20.580
and develops there as opposed
to within the Fallopian tubes,

01:40:20.580 --> 01:40:22.280
which is so-called
ectopic pregnancy.

01:40:22.280 --> 01:40:25.940
Now, where the sperm
and the egg meet exactly

01:40:25.940 --> 01:40:27.950
can vary, as I mentioned before.

01:40:27.950 --> 01:40:30.830
But in general, the
faster swimming sperm

01:40:30.830 --> 01:40:34.820
and the more far along the
ovulatory trajectory the egg

01:40:34.820 --> 01:40:38.030
are, the higher the probability
of a successful fertilization

01:40:38.030 --> 01:40:40.610
because of the proximity
to the implantation zone

01:40:40.610 --> 01:40:41.460
of the uterus.

01:40:41.460 --> 01:40:43.820
So basically it's all
a probabilities game.

01:40:43.820 --> 01:40:45.410
It's a probabilities
game related

01:40:45.410 --> 01:40:47.690
to the number of sperm
cells that encounter the egg

01:40:47.690 --> 01:40:50.420
and where the egg is in
terms of its ovulatory cycle

01:40:50.420 --> 01:40:55.280
and also its position where
it is in the ovulatory cycle.

01:40:55.280 --> 01:40:58.010
The sperm parameters--
or I should

01:40:58.010 --> 01:41:01.070
say the semen parameters--
and ejaculate parameters

01:41:01.070 --> 01:41:03.290
that most clinicians
want to see,

01:41:03.290 --> 01:41:05.240
if you were to give
a sperm sample,

01:41:05.240 --> 01:41:11.300
would be somewhere in excess of
15 million sperm per milliliter

01:41:11.300 --> 01:41:12.920
of ejaculate.

01:41:12.920 --> 01:41:15.110
Now, there's a lot of
discussion nowadays.

01:41:15.110 --> 01:41:17.150
It seems to be a very
popular news theme

01:41:17.150 --> 01:41:21.650
to talk about diminishing
sperm counts, the idea that 100

01:41:21.650 --> 01:41:25.250
years ago or maybe even 35 years
ago, the typical male ejaculate

01:41:25.250 --> 01:41:28.010
contained 100 million
sperm per milliliter,

01:41:28.010 --> 01:41:31.040
and nowadays it's down
to 15 to 20 or 50.

01:41:31.040 --> 01:41:34.470
And indeed, sperm counts
do seem to be declining.

01:41:34.470 --> 01:41:36.770
And the exact reasons
for that are not clear.

01:41:36.770 --> 01:41:39.062
I confess I'm a little bit
reluctant to talk about this

01:41:39.062 --> 01:41:42.080
because there have been a lot
of back and forth discussions

01:41:42.080 --> 01:41:44.725
about the safety of EMFs,
of electromagnetic fields,

01:41:44.725 --> 01:41:46.850
and it's not exactly what
we're talking about here.

01:41:46.850 --> 01:41:49.130
But there are some
excellent data

01:41:49.130 --> 01:41:50.720
contained in
meta-analyses and reviews

01:41:50.720 --> 01:41:52.970
that I will provide links
to and that we'll talk about

01:41:52.970 --> 01:41:57.000
in more detail in a
minute that correlate

01:41:57.000 --> 01:41:59.730
the advent of smartphones
and in particular caring

01:41:59.730 --> 01:42:03.300
of smartphones in the pocket
with diminishing sperm counts.

01:42:03.300 --> 01:42:06.000
Although there are certain
to be other factors that

01:42:06.000 --> 01:42:08.490
can explain diminishing
sperm counts as well.

01:42:08.490 --> 01:42:12.510
Dr. Shanna Swan, for instance,
has done beautiful work

01:42:12.510 --> 01:42:16.260
describing how the
phthalates and the BPAs

01:42:16.260 --> 01:42:18.120
and so-called
endocrine disruptors

01:42:18.120 --> 01:42:19.890
might be disrupting
some of the milieu

01:42:19.890 --> 01:42:22.150
of the seminiferous tubules.

01:42:22.150 --> 01:42:24.960
So this would be reductions in
testosterone and/or disruptions

01:42:24.960 --> 01:42:27.120
to the Sertoli cells and
androgen-binding protein

01:42:27.120 --> 01:42:29.820
brought about by endocrine
disruptors such as phthalates

01:42:29.820 --> 01:42:32.690
contained in pesticides and
contained on printed receipts

01:42:32.690 --> 01:42:33.690
and things of that sort.

01:42:33.690 --> 01:42:35.970
There are some data
that that is negatively

01:42:35.970 --> 01:42:38.970
impacting sperm counts.

01:42:38.970 --> 01:42:42.610
How much so is still debatable.

01:42:42.610 --> 01:42:44.770
There are also quite
good data pointing

01:42:44.770 --> 01:42:47.430
to the fact that
both the heat-related

01:42:47.430 --> 01:42:52.500
and the non-heat-related impact
of smartphones and laptops

01:42:52.500 --> 01:42:55.580
contained on the lap are
impacting sperm count

01:42:55.580 --> 01:42:57.202
and in a negative way.

01:42:57.202 --> 01:42:59.160
Again, there's going to
be tremendous variation

01:42:59.160 --> 01:43:00.842
in the concentration
of sperm from one

01:43:00.842 --> 01:43:01.800
individual to the next.

01:43:01.800 --> 01:43:04.740
It will vary according to age
and a number of other factors

01:43:04.740 --> 01:43:07.230
that we'll talk about
a little bit later.

01:43:07.230 --> 01:43:10.260
But in general, if somebody
is wishing to conceive,

01:43:10.260 --> 01:43:13.890
then clinicians like to
see a ejaculate volume

01:43:13.890 --> 01:43:16.720
of more than 2 milliliters.

01:43:16.720 --> 01:43:18.870
So ejaculate volume
can be anywhere

01:43:18.870 --> 01:43:22.570
from 1.5 to 5 milliliters.

01:43:22.570 --> 01:43:24.150
And that will
strongly be determined

01:43:24.150 --> 01:43:27.160
by how frequent
ejaculation is occurring.

01:43:27.160 --> 01:43:29.430
There's a lot that goes
into evaluating the quality

01:43:29.430 --> 01:43:30.780
of ejaculate and sperm.

01:43:30.780 --> 01:43:35.360
But basically these huge
variations that are observed

01:43:35.360 --> 01:43:38.523
of anywhere from 15 million
sperm per milliliter

01:43:38.523 --> 01:43:40.940
or, in some males who are not
producing sperm for whatever

01:43:40.940 --> 01:43:44.420
reason-- we'll talk about
those reasons in a little bit--

01:43:44.420 --> 01:43:47.402
as low as 5 million
sperm per milliliter,

01:43:47.402 --> 01:43:48.860
all the way up to
100 or maybe even

01:43:48.860 --> 01:43:51.200
200 million sperm
per milliliter.

01:43:51.200 --> 01:43:56.060
Huge variation-- the cause
of which is not always clear

01:43:56.060 --> 01:43:58.520
but is certainly
determined in part

01:43:58.520 --> 01:44:00.540
by the frequency of ejaculation.

01:44:00.540 --> 01:44:03.140
So because there are
so many variables

01:44:03.140 --> 01:44:06.380
impacting why one male
versus another male or even

01:44:06.380 --> 01:44:07.790
the same male
across the lifespan

01:44:07.790 --> 01:44:10.730
might have variations in
his concentration of sperm

01:44:10.730 --> 01:44:14.870
within the ejaculate, let's talk
for a second about frequency

01:44:14.870 --> 01:44:17.325
of ejaculation as it relates
to the goal of fertility,

01:44:17.325 --> 01:44:19.700
per se, because that's really
what today's episode is all

01:44:19.700 --> 01:44:20.280
about.

01:44:20.280 --> 01:44:21.800
So what I'd like
to talk about next

01:44:21.800 --> 01:44:24.380
is how people can
increase the probability

01:44:24.380 --> 01:44:26.540
of a successful
fertilization, focusing

01:44:26.540 --> 01:44:29.390
both on the components
from the male side

01:44:29.390 --> 01:44:30.620
and from the female side.

01:44:30.620 --> 01:44:33.470
And I'm mainly going to couch
this discussion in the context

01:44:33.470 --> 01:44:36.800
of the so-called natural
method of sexual intercourse

01:44:36.800 --> 01:44:41.390
and ejaculation in
vivo, within the female.

01:44:41.390 --> 01:44:43.700
But I will also touch
on some parallel themes

01:44:43.700 --> 01:44:45.680
as it relates to
in-vitro fertilization

01:44:45.680 --> 01:44:48.170
and intrauterine insemination.

01:44:48.170 --> 01:44:52.730
So the idea here is that
we want the maximum number

01:44:52.730 --> 01:44:55.670
of high-quality sperm--
that is, rapidly forward,

01:44:55.670 --> 01:44:58.350
motile sperm that are of
the correct morphology--

01:44:58.350 --> 01:44:59.600
that is, shape.

01:44:59.600 --> 01:45:02.270
That's going to require
a lot of mitochondria

01:45:02.270 --> 01:45:04.490
in the mid region,
a well-shaped head--

01:45:04.490 --> 01:45:06.170
so it's going to be
an oval-shaped head.

01:45:06.170 --> 01:45:08.840
The tail is going to be a
single tail, not multiple tails.

01:45:08.840 --> 01:45:11.360
These aren't going to be
the twitcher type of--

01:45:11.360 --> 01:45:14.600
or immotile type of sperm that
are either twitching in place

01:45:14.600 --> 01:45:15.680
or aren't moving forward.

01:45:15.680 --> 01:45:17.690
All of those
components are going

01:45:17.690 --> 01:45:20.480
to be essential for
increasing the probability

01:45:20.480 --> 01:45:21.290
of fertilization.

01:45:21.290 --> 01:45:23.165
But of course, there's
the female side of it,

01:45:23.165 --> 01:45:25.100
too, which is that
ovulation occurs

01:45:25.100 --> 01:45:28.760
on just one day during the
menstrual ovulatory cycle.

01:45:28.760 --> 01:45:31.490
And that egg will be
available for fertilization

01:45:31.490 --> 01:45:33.500
for approximately 24 hours.

01:45:33.500 --> 01:45:35.930
Now, keep in mind that
the sperm can survive

01:45:35.930 --> 01:45:38.810
within the vaginal duct
and within the area

01:45:38.810 --> 01:45:40.760
around the cervix
and within the uterus

01:45:40.760 --> 01:45:44.060
and along the female
reproductive tract for anywhere

01:45:44.060 --> 01:45:46.130
from three to five
or it's even been

01:45:46.130 --> 01:45:47.850
described as up to seven days.

01:45:47.850 --> 01:45:50.420
But generally, it's going to
be about three to five days.

01:45:50.420 --> 01:45:54.200
Now, most women can figure
out the day of their ovulation

01:45:54.200 --> 01:45:57.200
by counting the total number
of days of their typical cycle.

01:45:57.200 --> 01:45:58.700
And this is where
it's really useful

01:45:58.700 --> 01:46:02.330
to have a cycle that's of
more or less regular duration

01:46:02.330 --> 01:46:05.540
or, rather, of more or
less regular length.

01:46:05.540 --> 01:46:08.540
So as we talked about
earlier, if somebody's cycle

01:46:08.540 --> 01:46:12.470
is 21 days or 25 days and it's
21 or 25 days consistently

01:46:12.470 --> 01:46:14.720
or even 30 days
consistently, that's

01:46:14.720 --> 01:46:17.600
going to be a far better
scenario to favor fertilization

01:46:17.600 --> 01:46:20.870
than if it's 20 days
one month and then 21

01:46:20.870 --> 01:46:23.870
days the next month, but then
suddenly 30 days and then

01:46:23.870 --> 01:46:25.010
suddenly 35 days.

01:46:25.010 --> 01:46:28.160
Those varying durations
of the ovulatory cycle

01:46:28.160 --> 01:46:30.470
make it very hard,
obviously, to time

01:46:30.470 --> 01:46:32.760
and understand when
ovulation is going to occur.

01:46:32.760 --> 01:46:36.740
So regular duration
ovulatory cycles

01:46:36.740 --> 01:46:39.770
are the ideal circumstance, and
they're the ideal circumstance,

01:46:39.770 --> 01:46:41.240
because even though
the egg is only

01:46:41.240 --> 01:46:43.032
available for fertilization
for a few days,

01:46:43.032 --> 01:46:46.160
those sperm can survive for
some period of time, which

01:46:46.160 --> 01:46:49.700
leads to the issue of
how often should couples

01:46:49.700 --> 01:46:51.080
be having intercourse.

01:46:51.080 --> 01:46:53.090
And here, I'm
referring specifically

01:46:53.090 --> 01:46:54.530
to intercourse with ejaculation.

01:46:54.530 --> 01:46:56.660
How often should couples
be having intercourse

01:46:56.660 --> 01:47:00.950
around the time of ovulation
if the specific goal is

01:47:00.950 --> 01:47:05.090
successful fertilization of the
egg and the creation of a baby?

01:47:05.090 --> 01:47:08.720
This is leaving aside all
issues, which, of course, are

01:47:08.720 --> 01:47:11.690
interesting issues, related
to how often people are having

01:47:11.690 --> 01:47:13.970
intercourse, whether or
not there's ejaculation

01:47:13.970 --> 01:47:16.670
every time they have intercourse
or not, for sake of pleasure

01:47:16.670 --> 01:47:19.490
or for sake of pair
bonding and pleasure

01:47:19.490 --> 01:47:22.100
or for sake of any number
of other potential goals

01:47:22.100 --> 01:47:22.910
of intercourse.

01:47:22.910 --> 01:47:24.920
Here I'm only referring
to intercourse

01:47:24.920 --> 01:47:29.360
as it relates to the goal
of fertilization of the egg.

01:47:29.360 --> 01:47:35.390
So knowing what we know about
spermatogenesis and the fact

01:47:35.390 --> 01:47:39.050
that ejaculate is going to
contain a certain concentration

01:47:39.050 --> 01:47:42.830
of sperm but that within that
ejaculate some of the sperm

01:47:42.830 --> 01:47:46.630
will be older and less healthy
and some will be optimally

01:47:46.630 --> 01:47:48.380
mature and some might
even be a little bit

01:47:48.380 --> 01:47:50.922
immature-- although there's a
tendency for the immature sperm

01:47:50.922 --> 01:47:55.160
to not have yet exited the
seminiferous tubules, gone

01:47:55.160 --> 01:47:56.870
into the epididymis
and vas deferens.

01:47:56.870 --> 01:47:58.580
But given that the
ejaculate contains

01:47:58.580 --> 01:48:02.270
sperm of varying ages and
therefore varying quality

01:48:02.270 --> 01:48:05.180
and given that with each
successive ejaculation

01:48:05.180 --> 01:48:07.460
in a short period
of time there's

01:48:07.460 --> 01:48:10.430
going to be a decrease in
the concentration of sperm

01:48:10.430 --> 01:48:13.940
per milliliter of
semen, of ejaculate,

01:48:13.940 --> 01:48:16.310
we can make some
good arguments as

01:48:16.310 --> 01:48:19.280
to how often couples
should have intercourse

01:48:19.280 --> 01:48:21.920
with ejaculation around
the time of ovulation

01:48:21.920 --> 01:48:23.300
if the goal is to fertilize.

01:48:23.300 --> 01:48:25.070
If ovulation occurs
on, for instance,

01:48:25.070 --> 01:48:26.690
day 14 of a cycle--
and here we're

01:48:26.690 --> 01:48:28.280
using the kind of
standard average

01:48:28.280 --> 01:48:30.000
of 28 days of the cycle.

01:48:30.000 --> 01:48:32.730
But for some people
with a 30-day cycle,

01:48:32.730 --> 01:48:36.210
it could be day 15, or
with a shorter cycle,

01:48:36.210 --> 01:48:37.920
it could be day
12, for instance.

01:48:37.920 --> 01:48:40.260
But given a 28-day
average cycle,

01:48:40.260 --> 01:48:44.280
let's say ovulation occurs
on day 13 or on day 14.

01:48:44.280 --> 01:48:48.210
And typically, it would occur
on day 14 of a 28-day cycle.

01:48:48.210 --> 01:48:52.350
Well, then, given how long
sperm can survive inside

01:48:52.350 --> 01:48:55.020
of the woman, you might think
that the optimal strategy would

01:48:55.020 --> 01:48:58.920
be to have as much intercourse
with ejaculation in the three

01:48:58.920 --> 01:49:01.890
or four days leading
up to ovulation, hope

01:49:01.890 --> 01:49:04.290
that those sperm have swam
as far as they possibly

01:49:04.290 --> 01:49:06.960
can and will encounter the
egg just as soon as possible

01:49:06.960 --> 01:49:08.370
after it ovulates.

01:49:08.370 --> 01:49:10.320
It turns out that's not
the optimal strategy.

01:49:10.320 --> 01:49:13.830
The optimal strategy is really
to maximize the concentration

01:49:13.830 --> 01:49:16.620
of healthy sperm
within each ejaculate

01:49:16.620 --> 01:49:19.980
and to really center that
around the day of ovulation.

01:49:19.980 --> 01:49:22.560
So what this involves
generally and what

01:49:22.560 --> 01:49:27.060
the typical recommendation is
is to abstain from intercourse

01:49:27.060 --> 01:49:29.700
with ejaculation
about two or three

01:49:29.700 --> 01:49:33.360
days out from ovulation
and then, on the day

01:49:33.360 --> 01:49:37.320
prior to ovulation and
on the day of ovulation,

01:49:37.320 --> 01:49:40.950
to essentially
introduce as much semen

01:49:40.950 --> 01:49:43.230
and ejaculate into the
reproductive pathway

01:49:43.230 --> 01:49:45.970
of the female as possible.

01:49:45.970 --> 01:49:47.730
Now, that's the
general recommendation

01:49:47.730 --> 01:49:50.790
that the OB/GYNs and the
urologists that I spoke to

01:49:50.790 --> 01:49:51.630
gave.

01:49:51.630 --> 01:49:54.120
But you will also hear
a different strategy.

01:49:54.120 --> 01:49:55.440
It's only slightly different.

01:49:55.440 --> 01:49:57.600
But the different
strategy involves

01:49:57.600 --> 01:50:00.857
trying to maximize the
concentration of healthy sperm

01:50:00.857 --> 01:50:02.940
within each ejaculate with
the understanding that,

01:50:02.940 --> 01:50:06.900
with each subsequent ejaculation
over about a 24-hour period,

01:50:06.900 --> 01:50:09.250
that there's going to
be a dramatic reduction

01:50:09.250 --> 01:50:10.500
in the concentration of sperm.

01:50:10.500 --> 01:50:12.630
What that means is that
if a couple, for instance,

01:50:12.630 --> 01:50:15.750
were to have intercourse
with ejaculation many times

01:50:15.750 --> 01:50:17.550
on the day prior
to ovulation, yes,

01:50:17.550 --> 01:50:19.830
that will introduce
a lot of sperm

01:50:19.830 --> 01:50:23.970
into the reproductive pathway
of the female, but what it means

01:50:23.970 --> 01:50:25.860
is that, on the day of
ovulation if they were

01:50:25.860 --> 01:50:29.130
to have intercourse, the
number of high quality sperm

01:50:29.130 --> 01:50:32.730
that will be available to the
egg will be greatly diminished.

01:50:32.730 --> 01:50:35.280
And if none of the sperm
that were introduced

01:50:35.280 --> 01:50:38.400
in the day prior managed
to fertilize that egg,

01:50:38.400 --> 01:50:40.740
well, then essentially
chances are off

01:50:40.740 --> 01:50:43.620
that there will be fertilization
or they're greatly diminished.

01:50:43.620 --> 01:50:47.550
Rather, if they're having
intercourse with ejaculation

01:50:47.550 --> 01:50:50.290
once or twice on the
day prior to ovulation

01:50:50.290 --> 01:50:53.910
and then a maximal number
of times with ejaculation

01:50:53.910 --> 01:50:56.310
on the day of
ovulation, that itself

01:50:56.310 --> 01:50:58.720
can maximize the probability
of fertilization.

01:50:58.720 --> 01:51:00.090
So which strategy is optimal?

01:51:00.090 --> 01:51:01.830
Should couples have
as much intercourse

01:51:01.830 --> 01:51:04.660
with ejaculation on the
day prior to ovulation

01:51:04.660 --> 01:51:06.360
and on the day of ovulation?

01:51:06.360 --> 01:51:10.530
Or should they have intercourse
on the day prior to ovulation

01:51:10.530 --> 01:51:13.860
but not so frequently that it
diminishes the concentration

01:51:13.860 --> 01:51:17.340
of sperm and then
allows for intercourse

01:51:17.340 --> 01:51:20.010
with the maximum
number of ejaculations

01:51:20.010 --> 01:51:21.570
on the day of ovulation?

01:51:21.570 --> 01:51:23.040
You really hear it both ways.

01:51:23.040 --> 01:51:24.720
And what this really
boils down to is,

01:51:24.720 --> 01:51:26.400
frankly, that nobody knows.

01:51:26.400 --> 01:51:28.350
And the reason nobody
knows is that there's

01:51:28.350 --> 01:51:30.180
tremendous variation
among males in terms

01:51:30.180 --> 01:51:33.930
of the absolute concentration
of sperm per milliliter

01:51:33.930 --> 01:51:39.510
of ejaculate and the amount
of sperm per milliliter

01:51:39.510 --> 01:51:41.920
of ejaculate within
a given time frame.

01:51:41.920 --> 01:51:45.840
But what everyone agrees on
is that a period of abstinence

01:51:45.840 --> 01:51:49.860
ranging from 48 to 72 hours
prior to an ejaculation

01:51:49.860 --> 01:51:52.830
increases the concentration
of high-quality sperm

01:51:52.830 --> 01:51:56.460
within that first ejaculation
to occur after the abstinence

01:51:56.460 --> 01:51:57.910
period.

01:51:57.910 --> 01:52:00.852
So again, to reiterate, if one's
goal is to fertilize the egg,

01:52:00.852 --> 01:52:02.310
you want to take
into consideration

01:52:02.310 --> 01:52:05.610
that most often
there is going to be

01:52:05.610 --> 01:52:08.790
a dramatic decline in the
concentration of sperm

01:52:08.790 --> 01:52:12.162
per ejaculate any time those
ejaculations are occurring

01:52:12.162 --> 01:52:13.620
within a short
period of time, say,

01:52:13.620 --> 01:52:16.360
within 12 to 24
hours of one another.

01:52:16.360 --> 01:52:18.390
Now, all of this,
of course, also

01:52:18.390 --> 01:52:21.870
relates to the female
biology and the extent

01:52:21.870 --> 01:52:25.290
to which the woman can
precisely identify the day

01:52:25.290 --> 01:52:26.850
and timing of her ovulation.

01:52:26.850 --> 01:52:30.930
Some women feel as if and
indeed are very accurate

01:52:30.930 --> 01:52:33.540
at estimating their
time of ovulation

01:52:33.540 --> 01:52:36.150
to within a couple of
hours or some women even

01:52:36.150 --> 01:52:39.225
report being able to feel
their actual ovulation,

01:52:39.225 --> 01:52:41.100
whether or not they are
feeling the ovulation

01:52:41.100 --> 01:52:43.947
itself, the deployment of
the egg or not, isn't clear.

01:52:43.947 --> 01:52:45.030
I certainly wouldn't know.

01:52:45.030 --> 01:52:47.782
I've never produced eggs,
nor have I ovulated,

01:52:47.782 --> 01:52:49.740
and I'm certainly not
going to contest the idea

01:52:49.740 --> 01:52:52.405
that women can do that.

01:52:52.405 --> 01:52:54.030
I mean, it makes
sense that some people

01:52:54.030 --> 01:52:57.540
have a very keen
so-called interoceptive

01:52:57.540 --> 01:52:59.700
awareness, an awareness
of the sensory events

01:52:59.700 --> 01:53:01.200
within their body.

01:53:01.200 --> 01:53:03.720
And while, of course,
the ovaries are not

01:53:03.720 --> 01:53:05.430
thought of as an
organ that we want

01:53:05.430 --> 01:53:08.490
to be able to sense what's going
on in there in terms of feel,

01:53:08.490 --> 01:53:10.590
there are sensory
endings within the ovary.

01:53:10.590 --> 01:53:14.497
And so the notion that one
could literally sense changes

01:53:14.497 --> 01:53:16.830
within their ovary, including
the deployment of the egg,

01:53:16.830 --> 01:53:20.640
is not outside the bounds
of reason and, in fact,

01:53:20.640 --> 01:53:21.900
could likely be the case.

01:53:21.900 --> 01:53:25.027
Now, that said, there are
a number of different ways

01:53:25.027 --> 01:53:26.610
that women will track
their ovulation.

01:53:26.610 --> 01:53:28.150
One is the temperature method.

01:53:28.150 --> 01:53:30.660
So they'll actually measure
intravaginal temperature.

01:53:30.660 --> 01:53:32.410
They're looking for
changes in temperature

01:53:32.410 --> 01:53:35.110
that are consistent around
the time of ovulation.

01:53:35.110 --> 01:53:38.020
We're going to have an expert
guest on, an OB/GYN, who

01:53:38.020 --> 01:53:40.927
can tell us a lot more about
the details and nuances

01:53:40.927 --> 01:53:42.010
of the temperature method.

01:53:42.010 --> 01:53:43.880
You'll see a lot of
information about this online,

01:53:43.880 --> 01:53:45.838
but there's a lot of
misunderstanding about it,

01:53:45.838 --> 01:53:46.570
as well.

01:53:46.570 --> 01:53:49.300
Other women will use apps
that take into account

01:53:49.300 --> 01:53:50.890
either the temperature
information

01:53:50.890 --> 01:53:53.565
if they're acquiring
temperature information--

01:53:53.565 --> 01:53:54.940
that'll be entered
into the app--

01:53:54.940 --> 01:53:58.900
as well as marking the
onset of menstruation,

01:53:58.900 --> 01:54:00.370
the onset of
bleeding, therefore,

01:54:00.370 --> 01:54:01.870
the start of the
ovulatory cycle,

01:54:01.870 --> 01:54:03.130
because, of course, as
we mentioned earlier,

01:54:03.130 --> 01:54:04.900
that marks day one
of their cycle.

01:54:04.900 --> 01:54:06.550
And then, again
and again, you can

01:54:06.550 --> 01:54:08.950
see how regularity
of cycle duration

01:54:08.950 --> 01:54:11.680
or relative regularity
of cycle duration

01:54:11.680 --> 01:54:14.080
really favors this whole
process of being able to predict

01:54:14.080 --> 01:54:16.150
when one ovulates.

01:54:16.150 --> 01:54:20.320
And fortunately, if the
goal is fertilization,

01:54:20.320 --> 01:54:24.190
there are some margins for error
that are introduced by the fact

01:54:24.190 --> 01:54:27.430
that the sperm can survive
within the female reproductive

01:54:27.430 --> 01:54:31.300
tract for some period of
days, thereby reducing

01:54:31.300 --> 01:54:35.170
the need for absolute certainty
about the time of ovulation

01:54:35.170 --> 01:54:36.050
and so on.

01:54:36.050 --> 01:54:38.770
In fact, it's pretty well
known that around the time

01:54:38.770 --> 01:54:40.712
of ovulation a couple
of things happen.

01:54:40.712 --> 01:54:42.170
Earlier, we talked
about one thing,

01:54:42.170 --> 01:54:44.920
which is there's an increase in
libido just prior to ovulation.

01:54:44.920 --> 01:54:47.830
This relates to, in
part, an increase

01:54:47.830 --> 01:54:51.250
in some of the androgens,
things like DHEA,

01:54:51.250 --> 01:54:54.730
but also testosterone and
some related androgens

01:54:54.730 --> 01:55:00.940
that can increase libido both
in males and females and changes

01:55:00.940 --> 01:55:04.210
to the reproductive pathway,
the female in particular,

01:55:04.210 --> 01:55:07.480
a change in the pH-- that
is, the relative acidity

01:55:07.480 --> 01:55:12.250
versus basic nature of the
mucosal lining near the cervix

01:55:12.250 --> 01:55:14.740
and also vaginal
secretions, such that,

01:55:14.740 --> 01:55:19.750
around the time of ovulation,
the entire milieu of the vagina

01:55:19.750 --> 01:55:23.320
and the cervix and the locations
in which fertilization can

01:55:23.320 --> 01:55:25.780
occur and certainly in
which the sperm are swimming

01:55:25.780 --> 01:55:27.790
towards the opportunity
for fertilization

01:55:27.790 --> 01:55:31.160
is shifted to support
sperm motility and health.

01:55:31.160 --> 01:55:33.430
In other words, one of the
best environments for sperm

01:55:33.430 --> 01:55:37.510
to survive is going to be within
the female reproductive pathway

01:55:37.510 --> 01:55:38.200
itself.

01:55:38.200 --> 01:55:40.690
And as long as we're talking
about vaginal secretions

01:55:40.690 --> 01:55:43.090
and mucus, it's
important to point out

01:55:43.090 --> 01:55:45.970
that a number of commercially
available lubricants

01:55:45.970 --> 01:55:48.560
can actually be detrimental
for sperm health,

01:55:48.560 --> 01:55:50.908
even if they don't
contain spermicide.

01:55:50.908 --> 01:55:52.450
So this is something
that you'll want

01:55:52.450 --> 01:55:56.890
to discuss with your OB/GYN
or, certainly if you're male,

01:55:56.890 --> 01:55:58.960
you could also discuss
this with your urologist

01:55:58.960 --> 01:56:01.720
and your partner's OB/GYN.

01:56:01.720 --> 01:56:04.150
A lot of the commercially
available lubricants

01:56:04.150 --> 01:56:07.420
contain chemicals that,
while they may favorably

01:56:07.420 --> 01:56:10.240
change the consistency
or the viscosity

01:56:10.240 --> 01:56:13.840
of the vaginal pathway for
purposes of intercourse,

01:56:13.840 --> 01:56:17.830
certainly may not be the most
favorable for maintaining

01:56:17.830 --> 01:56:20.080
the health of the sperm and
the motility of the sperm.

01:56:20.080 --> 01:56:23.620
So again, here we're talking
about intercourse only

01:56:23.620 --> 01:56:26.290
in the context of trying
to maximize fertilization.

01:56:26.290 --> 01:56:28.420
And I should mention
that there are

01:56:28.420 --> 01:56:30.820
certain lubricants that are
more conducive to the sperm

01:56:30.820 --> 01:56:31.540
environment.

01:56:31.540 --> 01:56:33.082
But it's something
that you'll really

01:56:33.082 --> 01:56:34.810
want to talk to
your OB/GYN about

01:56:34.810 --> 01:56:37.540
or at least read up
about if your interest is

01:56:37.540 --> 01:56:40.100
in trying to fertilize
and develop an embryo.

01:56:40.100 --> 01:56:41.800
So we covered the
optimal strategies

01:56:41.800 --> 01:56:44.800
for how often couples
should have intercourse

01:56:44.800 --> 01:56:48.100
with ejaculation around
the time of ovulation

01:56:48.100 --> 01:56:50.410
in order to maximize
the probability

01:56:50.410 --> 01:56:53.440
that successful fertilization
and ultimately pregnancy will

01:56:53.440 --> 01:56:54.460
occur.

01:56:54.460 --> 01:56:56.440
What we haven't
covered yet, however,

01:56:56.440 --> 01:57:01.810
is how long couples should apply
that method over time in order

01:57:01.810 --> 01:57:04.330
to achieve successful
fertilization in pregnancy.

01:57:04.330 --> 01:57:06.070
Now, of course, if
a couple decides

01:57:06.070 --> 01:57:07.630
that they want to
conceive and they

01:57:07.630 --> 01:57:10.930
apply that method or any
other method, for instance,

01:57:10.930 --> 01:57:14.870
and they achieve fertilization
and a successful pregnancy

01:57:14.870 --> 01:57:16.630
the very first
month that they try,

01:57:16.630 --> 01:57:18.520
well, then there's
no other work to do,

01:57:18.520 --> 01:57:20.747
at least until that
child is born and if

01:57:20.747 --> 01:57:23.080
and only if they decide they
want to have more children.

01:57:23.080 --> 01:57:26.740
However, many couples
find that they do not

01:57:26.740 --> 01:57:28.960
conceive in the first
month of trying,

01:57:28.960 --> 01:57:30.970
even when they apply
the optimal methods

01:57:30.970 --> 01:57:34.300
and even if their age and every
other factor related to egg

01:57:34.300 --> 01:57:36.670
quality and sperm
quality is optimized.

01:57:36.670 --> 01:57:38.680
Now, I think it's
the rare instance

01:57:38.680 --> 01:57:41.980
in which egg quality and
sperm quality are optimized.

01:57:41.980 --> 01:57:44.878
In fact, the word "optimal" and
"optimization" and "optimized"

01:57:44.878 --> 01:57:46.420
is a little bit
misleading in general

01:57:46.420 --> 01:57:48.250
because no one really
knows what that is.

01:57:48.250 --> 01:57:49.930
But of course,
there is an ideal.

01:57:49.930 --> 01:57:52.090
There's a perfect
standard to which

01:57:52.090 --> 01:57:53.560
everyone would like to achieve.

01:57:53.560 --> 01:57:56.980
But of course, we all enter the
picture with genetic variables,

01:57:56.980 --> 01:58:00.070
environmental variables,
and so forth, many of which

01:58:00.070 --> 01:58:02.328
we'll talk about because you
can, in fact, adjust them

01:58:02.328 --> 01:58:04.870
in the direction that you would
like to improve sperm and egg

01:58:04.870 --> 01:58:05.680
quality.

01:58:05.680 --> 01:58:09.640
But most people simply
will not succeed

01:58:09.640 --> 01:58:13.480
in achieving a successful
fertilization the first month

01:58:13.480 --> 01:58:14.380
that they try.

01:58:14.380 --> 01:58:16.990
Now, there is a
truth that governs

01:58:16.990 --> 01:58:20.170
how many tries it
ought to take in order

01:58:20.170 --> 01:58:23.110
to achieve successful
fertilization and ultimately

01:58:23.110 --> 01:58:23.740
pregnancy.

01:58:23.740 --> 01:58:25.330
And it's very age dependent.

01:58:25.330 --> 01:58:27.550
And in particular, it's
dependent on the age

01:58:27.550 --> 01:58:30.490
of the mother, because the
age and quality of the egg,

01:58:30.490 --> 01:58:33.990
while it's not the only
factor, is certainly

01:58:33.990 --> 01:58:36.450
one of the most determining
factors in whether or not

01:58:36.450 --> 01:58:38.280
successful fertilization occurs.

01:58:38.280 --> 01:58:40.800
And as women age, the
quality of the eggs

01:58:40.800 --> 01:58:42.900
tends to diminish
over time, largely

01:58:42.900 --> 01:58:44.970
due to changes in the
mitochondrial function

01:58:44.970 --> 01:58:47.520
and the spindle that pulls
the chromosomes apart,

01:58:47.520 --> 01:58:50.260
although there could be other
factors involved as well.

01:58:50.260 --> 01:58:51.880
Now, before continuing
any further,

01:58:51.880 --> 01:58:54.690
I just want to acknowledge that
this whole language around egg

01:58:54.690 --> 01:58:57.600
quality and sperm quality
is not the greatest

01:58:57.600 --> 01:59:00.300
language because it's
entirely subjective.

01:59:00.300 --> 01:59:03.510
And yet the word "quality"
in these instances

01:59:03.510 --> 01:59:06.320
is really there to
explain a broad variety

01:59:06.320 --> 01:59:08.070
of factors that can,
in fact, be measured,

01:59:08.070 --> 01:59:10.650
things like the number of
follicles that are deployed

01:59:10.650 --> 01:59:13.800
each month in a woman's
ovulation or the number

01:59:13.800 --> 01:59:17.040
of motile sperm or the number
of morphologically-- that

01:59:17.040 --> 01:59:19.355
is, correctly shaped sperm
in the male and so forth.

01:59:19.355 --> 01:59:21.480
So when we talk about egg
quality or sperm quality,

01:59:21.480 --> 01:59:25.560
we're really referring to an
amalgam of different features

01:59:25.560 --> 01:59:29.010
related to the different
aspects of ovulation

01:59:29.010 --> 01:59:30.720
leading to successful
fertilization

01:59:30.720 --> 01:59:34.020
or the different aspects of
sperm related to whether or not

01:59:34.020 --> 01:59:36.060
they can arrive and
deliver their DNA contents

01:59:36.060 --> 01:59:36.760
and so forth.

01:59:36.760 --> 01:59:39.270
So I will use the words "egg
quality" and "sperm quality"

01:59:39.270 --> 01:59:41.040
just as general themes
because that's what

01:59:41.040 --> 01:59:42.720
a lot of the clinicians use.

01:59:42.720 --> 01:59:45.180
But I do understand that it's
a little bit of a loaded term

01:59:45.180 --> 01:59:48.090
in both instances, and it
doesn't relate to any one

01:59:48.090 --> 01:59:50.520
specific parameter, per se.

01:59:50.520 --> 01:59:52.770
So getting back to this
issue of how long couples

01:59:52.770 --> 01:59:55.410
should try according to
the age of the female

01:59:55.410 --> 01:59:57.360
and perhaps also
the age of the male.

01:59:57.360 --> 01:59:59.850
Well, most of the data
that have been collected

01:59:59.850 --> 02:00:02.440
relate to the age of the
female, as I mentioned before.

02:00:02.440 --> 02:00:04.655
And what we're
about to discuss is,

02:00:04.655 --> 02:00:06.030
within the scientific
literature,

02:00:06.030 --> 02:00:08.520
described as what's
called fecundability,

02:00:08.520 --> 02:00:12.810
which is the amount of time
over which a given couple needs

02:00:12.810 --> 02:00:14.710
to attempt to
conceive-- of course,

02:00:14.710 --> 02:00:16.830
by having intercourse
with ejaculation--

02:00:16.830 --> 02:00:18.780
around the time of ovulation.

02:00:18.780 --> 02:00:20.280
It assumes that all
the other things

02:00:20.280 --> 02:00:22.350
are being done correctly.

02:00:22.350 --> 02:00:25.650
And what we know is that there's
a strong age-dependent effect

02:00:25.650 --> 02:00:28.860
that largely rests on the
age of the egg-- that is,

02:00:28.860 --> 02:00:29.820
of the female.

02:00:29.820 --> 02:00:34.560
And what we know is that
for females 30 years old

02:00:34.560 --> 02:00:38.565
or younger, if they have
intercourse with ejaculation

02:00:38.565 --> 02:00:40.440
around the time of
ovulation, say, on the day

02:00:40.440 --> 02:00:43.140
before and on the
day of ovulation--

02:00:43.140 --> 02:00:45.720
and there could be other
intercourse with ejaculation

02:00:45.720 --> 02:00:47.730
around that time as well--

02:00:47.730 --> 02:00:51.780
on average, that will result
in a successful fertilization

02:00:51.780 --> 02:00:54.840
in pregnancy about
20% of the time

02:00:54.840 --> 02:00:56.730
on the first month
of attempting,

02:00:56.730 --> 02:00:58.710
the first ovulation cycle.

02:00:58.710 --> 02:01:01.788
Now, if fertilization and
pregnancy occurs, great.

02:01:01.788 --> 02:01:03.330
There'll be at least
a nine-month lag

02:01:03.330 --> 02:01:04.950
until they decide
whether or not they

02:01:04.950 --> 02:01:06.510
want to try and conceive again.

02:01:06.510 --> 02:01:10.350
However, most couples, even
if the woman is 30 years

02:01:10.350 --> 02:01:12.510
old or younger, will
not successfully

02:01:12.510 --> 02:01:15.000
conceive on that first attempt.

02:01:15.000 --> 02:01:17.550
And that's because the
probability is not 100%.

02:01:17.550 --> 02:01:18.420
It's 20%.

02:01:18.420 --> 02:01:20.820
So 80% of the time,
they simply will not

02:01:20.820 --> 02:01:24.810
conceive, which means that
they hopefully will try again

02:01:24.810 --> 02:01:26.020
the very next month.

02:01:26.020 --> 02:01:28.253
And if they successfully
conceive, great.

02:01:28.253 --> 02:01:29.670
And if they don't,
then they ought

02:01:29.670 --> 02:01:32.110
to try again the next month,
the next month, and so forth.

02:01:32.110 --> 02:01:35.520
Now, the typical advice that
an OB/GYN would give you

02:01:35.520 --> 02:01:39.120
is that, for a woman
30 years or younger--

02:01:39.120 --> 02:01:42.810
and leaving aside
the age of the father

02:01:42.810 --> 02:01:46.950
but still assuming that egg
quality and sperm quality

02:01:46.950 --> 02:01:49.680
are sufficiently high to
achieve fertilization--

02:01:49.680 --> 02:01:52.485
that the couple should--

02:01:52.485 --> 02:01:54.360
or if the woman is trying
to have kids alone,

02:01:54.360 --> 02:01:56.820
the woman should
attempt to conceive over

02:01:56.820 --> 02:01:58.590
the period of six months.

02:01:58.590 --> 02:01:59.220
Why?

02:01:59.220 --> 02:02:00.845
Well, if you think
about it, if there's

02:02:00.845 --> 02:02:04.440
a 20% chance in the first month
and it's unsuccessful, well,

02:02:04.440 --> 02:02:07.080
then on the second month,
there'll also be a 20% chance.

02:02:07.080 --> 02:02:09.000
On the third month,
also a 20% chance.

02:02:09.000 --> 02:02:12.000
What I'm describing
here is what obviously

02:02:12.000 --> 02:02:14.430
is independent probabilities.

02:02:14.430 --> 02:02:16.290
That is, if you
were to flip a coin

02:02:16.290 --> 02:02:18.460
and the probability of
getting heads is 50%,

02:02:18.460 --> 02:02:21.480
the probability of getting
tails is 50%, of course.

02:02:21.480 --> 02:02:24.245
You don't expect that the
previous flip had anything

02:02:24.245 --> 02:02:25.620
to do with the
result that you'll

02:02:25.620 --> 02:02:26.670
get on the subsequent flip.

02:02:26.670 --> 02:02:28.420
That's what independent
probabilities are.

02:02:28.420 --> 02:02:31.860
However, when it comes
to fecundability,

02:02:31.860 --> 02:02:33.360
we're really talking
about something

02:02:33.360 --> 02:02:36.120
which is called cumulative
pregnancy rate, which

02:02:36.120 --> 02:02:38.250
is not really independent
probabilities.

02:02:38.250 --> 02:02:39.310
Now, why would that be?

02:02:39.310 --> 02:02:41.310
Why would it be that if
you did not successfully

02:02:41.310 --> 02:02:43.800
conceive in the first
month of trying that,

02:02:43.800 --> 02:02:46.530
by simply trying again and
again and again, the probability

02:02:46.530 --> 02:02:48.130
of conceiving would increase?

02:02:48.130 --> 02:02:50.430
Well, the reason for that
is that this whole business

02:02:50.430 --> 02:02:52.172
of fertilization is
not just about what's

02:02:52.172 --> 02:02:53.130
happening with the egg.

02:02:53.130 --> 02:02:55.200
It's also about what's
happening with the sperm.

02:02:55.200 --> 02:02:57.840
So there are a number of
different events related

02:02:57.840 --> 02:03:00.423
to the biology of the egg and
the biology of the sperm, which

02:03:00.423 --> 02:03:02.340
you are now very familiar
with from everything

02:03:02.340 --> 02:03:03.810
I've talked about up until now.

02:03:03.810 --> 02:03:06.248
And there a bunch
of chance events,

02:03:06.248 --> 02:03:08.040
for instance, that the
sperm won't actually

02:03:08.040 --> 02:03:11.012
arrive at the egg in time
or that the egg won't arrive

02:03:11.012 --> 02:03:12.720
at the sperm in time,
because, of course,

02:03:12.720 --> 02:03:14.720
it's a bidirectional
migration of those two cell

02:03:14.720 --> 02:03:16.740
types, or that, for
whatever reason,

02:03:16.740 --> 02:03:17.935
fertilization won't occur.

02:03:17.935 --> 02:03:19.560
So what we're really
talking about when

02:03:19.560 --> 02:03:22.830
we talk about the cumulative
pregnancy rate over time

02:03:22.830 --> 02:03:25.860
is the fact that there are
multiple probabilities at work.

02:03:25.860 --> 02:03:28.620
And yes, those are somewhat
independent in the sense

02:03:28.620 --> 02:03:31.080
that the biology of the
sperm doesn't really strictly

02:03:31.080 --> 02:03:32.520
depend on the
biology of the egg,

02:03:32.520 --> 02:03:34.410
at least not until they
meet and fertilize.

02:03:34.410 --> 02:03:38.280
But the likelihood
of pregnancy depends

02:03:38.280 --> 02:03:39.940
on those independent
probabilities,

02:03:39.940 --> 02:03:42.635
which makes this a
cumulative pregnancy rate.

02:03:42.635 --> 02:03:44.760
Now, if any of that is
confusing, what it basically

02:03:44.760 --> 02:03:46.710
means is that for
the egg and the sperm

02:03:46.710 --> 02:03:49.140
to meet and to fertilize, a
number of different events

02:03:49.140 --> 02:03:52.015
that carry some intentionality--

02:03:52.015 --> 02:03:53.890
the sperm swims towards
the egg and so forth.

02:03:53.890 --> 02:03:56.820
The egg doesn't have a
personality in there,

02:03:56.820 --> 02:03:57.690
at least not yet.

02:03:57.690 --> 02:04:00.270
But it, quote, unquote,
"wants" to be fertilize.

02:04:00.270 --> 02:04:03.420
It is, in principle,
receptive to fertilization.

02:04:03.420 --> 02:04:05.975
Well, in order for
that to happen,

02:04:05.975 --> 02:04:08.100
there are going to be some
events related to chance

02:04:08.100 --> 02:04:10.188
that could limit the
ability for that to happen,

02:04:10.188 --> 02:04:11.730
and there'll be
other events dictated

02:04:11.730 --> 02:04:13.590
by the biology of those
two cell types that

02:04:13.590 --> 02:04:15.810
are driving that
event to happen,

02:04:15.810 --> 02:04:17.700
that are biasing the
event to, yes, happen.

02:04:17.700 --> 02:04:19.200
And so what we're
talking about when

02:04:19.200 --> 02:04:21.000
we talk about cumulative
pregnancy rate

02:04:21.000 --> 02:04:24.180
is how much of the
biology of the woman

02:04:24.180 --> 02:04:28.030
is skewed towards fertilization
to be likely to occur.

02:04:28.030 --> 02:04:30.870
So to make this very
simple, all we need to know

02:04:30.870 --> 02:04:33.150
is that for women 30
years old or younger,

02:04:33.150 --> 02:04:37.770
because the probability of
getting pregnant on any one

02:04:37.770 --> 02:04:42.210
attempt to conceive
is 20%, well,

02:04:42.210 --> 02:04:44.550
then if that doesn't
occur the first time,

02:04:44.550 --> 02:04:46.920
then she should simply
repeat that at least five

02:04:46.920 --> 02:04:50.580
and probably six times before
deciding to go to an OB/GYN

02:04:50.580 --> 02:04:52.860
and conclude that there's
something going on either

02:04:52.860 --> 02:04:55.290
with the egg or, of course,
it could be with the sperm

02:04:55.290 --> 02:04:56.873
because 20 times 5 is 100.

02:04:56.873 --> 02:04:58.665
So we're talking about
cumulative percent--

02:04:58.665 --> 02:05:01.470
so 20, 40, 60, 80, 100.

02:05:01.470 --> 02:05:03.750
And the six month
there would take you

02:05:03.750 --> 02:05:07.630
to 120%, which is a
different thing altogether.

02:05:07.630 --> 02:05:09.547
But in general,
that's why OB/GYNs

02:05:09.547 --> 02:05:11.130
will tell their
female patients, look,

02:05:11.130 --> 02:05:12.630
if you're setting
out to conceive,

02:05:12.630 --> 02:05:14.560
try for about five
or six months,

02:05:14.560 --> 02:05:17.100
and if you're not successful,
come back and see me.

02:05:17.100 --> 02:05:21.330
Now, for women who
are age 31 to 33,

02:05:21.330 --> 02:05:23.490
the probability of conceiving
in that first month

02:05:23.490 --> 02:05:25.270
drops to about 18%.

02:05:25.270 --> 02:05:27.510
So women in that age
range and their partners

02:05:27.510 --> 02:05:29.790
should certainly try
and conceive naturally

02:05:29.790 --> 02:05:32.490
over a period of six or
seven months in order

02:05:32.490 --> 02:05:34.740
to get to that 100%
cumulative probability.

02:05:34.740 --> 02:05:37.920
And then for women
who are age 34 to 37,

02:05:37.920 --> 02:05:40.500
the probability of conceiving
in that first month

02:05:40.500 --> 02:05:45.238
of trying and certainly every
month thereafter is about 11%.

02:05:45.238 --> 02:05:47.280
So when the age of the
woman starts extending out

02:05:47.280 --> 02:05:50.760
to about 34 or 35 years
old, then the typical advice

02:05:50.760 --> 02:05:54.060
of the OB/GYN is going to be
to attempt to conceive over

02:05:54.060 --> 02:05:56.550
a period of about
nine months to a year

02:05:56.550 --> 02:06:00.750
before deciding to take some
sort of medical intervention.

02:06:00.750 --> 02:06:03.660
And then, of course, as the
age of the woman increases,

02:06:03.660 --> 02:06:06.510
so too does the quality
of the eggs go down.

02:06:06.510 --> 02:06:08.070
Now, that's not true
for every woman.

02:06:08.070 --> 02:06:10.860
There are many women who, in
their late 30s and 40s and even

02:06:10.860 --> 02:06:14.370
early 50s, have successfully
conceived healthy children,

02:06:14.370 --> 02:06:17.250
although the probability of
that-- the likelihood of it

02:06:17.250 --> 02:06:18.730
drops substantially.

02:06:18.730 --> 02:06:21.930
So for instance, for women
who are age 38 to 39,

02:06:21.930 --> 02:06:24.420
the probability of a
successful conception

02:06:24.420 --> 02:06:27.660
by natural conception--
intercourse with ejaculation--

02:06:27.660 --> 02:06:30.060
is going to be about 5%.

02:06:30.060 --> 02:06:32.520
So it's really dropped
to a quarter of what

02:06:32.520 --> 02:06:35.310
it was when that woman was 30.

02:06:35.310 --> 02:06:36.990
Again, these are averages only.

02:06:36.990 --> 02:06:37.870
What does that mean?

02:06:37.870 --> 02:06:41.010
Well, it means that if
you are age 38 or older,

02:06:41.010 --> 02:06:44.670
chances are that you should
probably go to your OB/GYN

02:06:44.670 --> 02:06:46.290
right at the outset
of your desire

02:06:46.290 --> 02:06:49.110
to conceive and ask what you
can do to improve egg quality.

02:06:49.110 --> 02:06:51.680
Otherwise, if you were
to extend the math out,

02:06:51.680 --> 02:06:54.670
we know that if you're age
30 or younger, 20% chance

02:06:54.670 --> 02:06:55.910
in any one given month.

02:06:55.910 --> 02:06:57.970
That means about four
to six months of trying.

02:06:57.970 --> 02:07:02.020
Well, you can simply multiply
that times four or five

02:07:02.020 --> 02:07:04.685
for someone in their
late 30s or early 40s.

02:07:04.685 --> 02:07:06.310
And so what you're
really talking about

02:07:06.310 --> 02:07:07.570
is several years of trying.

02:07:07.570 --> 02:07:09.610
And of course, what's happening
during those several years?

02:07:09.610 --> 02:07:10.990
The woman is getting older.

02:07:10.990 --> 02:07:12.940
And as a consequence,
the quality of the eggs

02:07:12.940 --> 02:07:14.900
is declining even further.

02:07:14.900 --> 02:07:19.450
So if you are 35, 36
years old, it might not

02:07:19.450 --> 02:07:22.030
be entirely unreasonable to
talk to your OB/GYN right

02:07:22.030 --> 02:07:24.132
at the outset of
desiring to conceive,

02:07:24.132 --> 02:07:25.840
but you could also
just take the approach

02:07:25.840 --> 02:07:28.300
of trying to conceive naturally
for about a year or a year

02:07:28.300 --> 02:07:31.330
and a half before deciding
to do that, keeping in mind

02:07:31.330 --> 02:07:33.310
that all the while
you can't stop time.

02:07:33.310 --> 02:07:36.790
So biological time and aging is
going to occur in the backdrop.

02:07:36.790 --> 02:07:40.450
But hopefully this description
of cumulative pregnancy rate

02:07:40.450 --> 02:07:41.200
makes sense.

02:07:41.200 --> 02:07:43.870
Again, the idea is
that while it's true

02:07:43.870 --> 02:07:47.080
that every single month
there's an independent chance

02:07:47.080 --> 02:07:51.370
of the woman getting pregnant
and that chance is dropping

02:07:51.370 --> 02:07:56.080
from abut 20% at age 30 over
time to about, really, 1% to 3%

02:07:56.080 --> 02:07:58.330
for women 40 or
older, there's also

02:07:58.330 --> 02:08:00.730
this notion of cumulative
probability, which

02:08:00.730 --> 02:08:03.130
involves multiple
biological events in both

02:08:03.130 --> 02:08:06.400
the egg and the sperm that have
to converge in time and space

02:08:06.400 --> 02:08:08.920
in order for successful
fertilization to occur.

02:08:08.920 --> 02:08:10.350
As long as we're
on this topic, I

02:08:10.350 --> 02:08:13.600
think it's only fair to address
the issue of miscarriage.

02:08:13.600 --> 02:08:16.360
And miscarriages can arise
from a variety of sources.

02:08:16.360 --> 02:08:18.460
They can arise from
genetic defects.

02:08:18.460 --> 02:08:21.640
They can arise from issues in
the milieu view of the uterus.

02:08:21.640 --> 02:08:24.670
They can arise from issues with
the sperm, for that matter.

02:08:24.670 --> 02:08:27.160
We really don't want to
put all the weight and all

02:08:27.160 --> 02:08:29.360
the responsibility on the egg.

02:08:29.360 --> 02:08:31.330
This is always an
egg/sperm dynamic.

02:08:31.330 --> 02:08:33.190
And when I say
egg/sperm dynamic, now

02:08:33.190 --> 02:08:35.890
hopefully that calls to mind
the huge library of information

02:08:35.890 --> 02:08:37.432
that we've been
covering up until now

02:08:37.432 --> 02:08:39.970
about chromosomal segregation
and the coming together

02:08:39.970 --> 02:08:42.670
of these different cell types
and their genetic information.

02:08:42.670 --> 02:08:45.220
Any number of different
steps within the process

02:08:45.220 --> 02:08:47.320
of fertilization
leading up to pregnancy

02:08:47.320 --> 02:08:49.330
can lead to miscarriage.

02:08:49.330 --> 02:08:52.660
However, the probability
of miscarriage

02:08:52.660 --> 02:08:57.400
greatly increases as a
function of the age of the egg.

02:08:57.400 --> 02:09:00.250
And the basic numbers
on thisare are

02:09:00.250 --> 02:09:05.920
that for women who are 35
years or older, about 25%

02:09:05.920 --> 02:09:09.220
of successful fertilizations
lead to miscarriages.

02:09:09.220 --> 02:09:12.040
Now, when those miscarriages
occur during pregnancy

02:09:12.040 --> 02:09:13.300
can be highly variable.

02:09:13.300 --> 02:09:15.190
Sometimes it's within
the first trimester.

02:09:15.190 --> 02:09:17.360
Sometimes it could be later.

02:09:17.360 --> 02:09:20.320
But the probability
is about 25%.

02:09:20.320 --> 02:09:24.200
That probability increases
greatly over time,

02:09:24.200 --> 02:09:27.220
such that by the time women
are in their early 40s--

02:09:27.220 --> 02:09:28.430
so 40 or older--

02:09:28.430 --> 02:09:30.190
the probability of
miscarriage after

02:09:30.190 --> 02:09:33.520
a successful fertilization
is going to be about 50%.

02:09:33.520 --> 02:09:35.800
And this could be due
to a number of factors,

02:09:35.800 --> 02:09:36.790
as I mentioned before.

02:09:36.790 --> 02:09:39.700
But one common reason
is that there can

02:09:39.700 --> 02:09:41.320
be chromosomal abnormalities.

02:09:41.320 --> 02:09:43.450
And that could be
related typically

02:09:43.450 --> 02:09:46.720
to the segregation
of the egg when

02:09:46.720 --> 02:09:48.220
half of the
chromosomes in that egg

02:09:48.220 --> 02:09:50.620
are removed, taking it
from diploid to haploid.

02:09:50.620 --> 02:09:53.210
If you recall, there's
that little polar body,

02:09:53.210 --> 02:09:56.290
which is the removal of
the chromosomes that's

02:09:56.290 --> 02:09:58.480
ejected from the egg that
will eventually ovulate.

02:09:58.480 --> 02:10:00.460
And sometimes not
all the chromosomes

02:10:00.460 --> 02:10:04.540
that were supposed to be ejected
in that polar body are ejected.

02:10:04.540 --> 02:10:06.790
And as a consequence, there
are multiple chromosomes

02:10:06.790 --> 02:10:09.370
or duplications of chromosomes,
things like trisomies.

02:10:09.370 --> 02:10:11.422
Sometimes too many
chromosomes move away

02:10:11.422 --> 02:10:13.630
and there are actually
removal of entire chromosomes,

02:10:13.630 --> 02:10:16.600
meaning both strands, so that
you have chromosomal deletions.

02:10:16.600 --> 02:10:19.473
And in that case, typically
fertilization won't occur.

02:10:19.473 --> 02:10:21.890
But there are instances in
which fertilization will occur.

02:10:21.890 --> 02:10:23.890
So a woman will get a
positive pregnancy test.

02:10:23.890 --> 02:10:25.390
Her periods will stop.

02:10:25.390 --> 02:10:27.430
And the couple will
think that they're

02:10:27.430 --> 02:10:31.190
advancing along the steps
to a successful pregnancy,

02:10:31.190 --> 02:10:33.670
and then there will be,
sadly, a miscarriage.

02:10:33.670 --> 02:10:35.950
Many, many times
those miscarriages

02:10:35.950 --> 02:10:37.990
are the consequence
of the fact that,

02:10:37.990 --> 02:10:40.930
when there are extra
chromosomes there or there

02:10:40.930 --> 02:10:46.120
are too few chromosomes present,
that embryogenesis can simply

02:10:46.120 --> 02:10:48.430
not progress in a healthy way.

02:10:48.430 --> 02:10:50.620
There are some
instances in which

02:10:50.620 --> 02:10:53.140
all of the chromosomes and all
the chromosomal arrangements

02:10:53.140 --> 02:10:57.080
are perfectly normal and
miscarriages can still occur.

02:10:57.080 --> 02:11:00.100
I'm going to do a future
episode about pregnancy

02:11:00.100 --> 02:11:01.690
and embryonic
development where we

02:11:01.690 --> 02:11:03.140
will get into this more deeply.

02:11:03.140 --> 02:11:06.370
But just understand that the
frequency of miscarriages

02:11:06.370 --> 02:11:10.060
increases dramatically
after about age 34

02:11:10.060 --> 02:11:12.820
and then continues to
increase dramatically,

02:11:12.820 --> 02:11:15.010
extending well
out until the 40s.

02:11:15.010 --> 02:11:16.960
Now, a very important
consideration

02:11:16.960 --> 02:11:18.940
in terms of understanding
and predicting

02:11:18.940 --> 02:11:22.330
fertility and fecundability,
this word that describes

02:11:22.330 --> 02:11:24.850
the probability of getting
pregnant on a given try

02:11:24.850 --> 02:11:29.410
and over time, is
trying to address how,

02:11:29.410 --> 02:11:31.990
quote, unquote,
"fertile" a woman is

02:11:31.990 --> 02:11:36.040
and, importantly, how, quote,
unquote, "fertile" a male is.

02:11:36.040 --> 02:11:38.480
And we'll talk about the
male side in a moment.

02:11:38.480 --> 02:11:42.070
But when trying to address how
fertile a woman is, of course,

02:11:42.070 --> 02:11:45.970
age is going to be one of the
major factors, but just one

02:11:45.970 --> 02:11:46.940
factor.

02:11:46.940 --> 02:11:48.700
We already talked about
how age determines

02:11:48.700 --> 02:11:51.230
the likelihood of a
successful pregnancy

02:11:51.230 --> 02:11:55.330
if the intercourse and
ejaculation is being carried

02:11:55.330 --> 02:11:58.630
out at the correct times
and with viable sperm

02:11:58.630 --> 02:12:00.700
capable of fertilizing eggs.

02:12:00.700 --> 02:12:03.100
And then, of course, there's
the issue of egg quality.

02:12:03.100 --> 02:12:05.380
But in general, most
women would like

02:12:05.380 --> 02:12:10.090
to know how fertile they are
as a function of their age.

02:12:10.090 --> 02:12:13.030
And I actually think this is
one of the most important topics

02:12:13.030 --> 02:12:14.800
in this whole space
around fertility

02:12:14.800 --> 02:12:17.560
that isn't often discussed or
at least isn't often discussed

02:12:17.560 --> 02:12:20.740
until women are in
their late 30s or 40s,

02:12:20.740 --> 02:12:23.012
when oftentimes
they will look back

02:12:23.012 --> 02:12:24.970
and wish that either they
had frozen their eggs

02:12:24.970 --> 02:12:28.600
or they had frozen fertilized
embryos, which is a whole thing

02:12:28.600 --> 02:12:29.223
unto itself.

02:12:29.223 --> 02:12:30.640
And we can talk
about that when we

02:12:30.640 --> 02:12:34.000
have an episode on in-vitro
fertilization in more depth.

02:12:34.000 --> 02:12:37.240
But there is a fairly
straightforward way

02:12:37.240 --> 02:12:39.880
or set of ways that
women can determine

02:12:39.880 --> 02:12:42.670
their basic level of fertility.

02:12:42.670 --> 02:12:44.800
Leaving aside a lot
of the detailed issues

02:12:44.800 --> 02:12:47.560
about the quality of eggs
and so forth, one thing

02:12:47.560 --> 02:12:49.780
that you already learned
is that there's this vault,

02:12:49.780 --> 02:12:52.420
there's this reserve that
we call the ovarian reserve,

02:12:52.420 --> 02:12:55.570
and that each month a
certain number of follicles

02:12:55.570 --> 02:12:59.800
leave that reserve, and
there's the opportunity, based

02:12:59.800 --> 02:13:03.700
on the ovulation of a single
egg, to fertilize that egg

02:13:03.700 --> 02:13:05.290
and for the woman
to get pregnant.

02:13:05.290 --> 02:13:06.910
Now, one thing that
we know for sure

02:13:06.910 --> 02:13:10.450
is that the size of
the population that's

02:13:10.450 --> 02:13:13.330
released from that
vault each month

02:13:13.330 --> 02:13:16.360
has a very strong
positive correlation

02:13:16.360 --> 02:13:19.850
with the size of the
reserve in the vault itself.

02:13:19.850 --> 02:13:22.480
So the way to think
about this, perhaps,

02:13:22.480 --> 02:13:24.580
is that the vault is
like a bank account.

02:13:24.580 --> 02:13:26.900
It has a certain
amount of money--

02:13:26.900 --> 02:13:28.300
in this case, eggs-- in it.

02:13:28.300 --> 02:13:32.050
And you could imagine, if
someone's reasonably logical,

02:13:32.050 --> 02:13:34.420
that if they have more money
in their bank account, then

02:13:34.420 --> 02:13:36.718
they're going to
withdraw a larger amount

02:13:36.718 --> 02:13:39.010
each month than if they have
a small amount each month,

02:13:39.010 --> 02:13:42.370
if the idea is to make
that vault, that bank,

02:13:42.370 --> 02:13:46.870
of eggs available to them over
the longest period of time.

02:13:46.870 --> 02:13:48.860
And indeed, biology
is pretty smart.

02:13:48.860 --> 02:13:53.350
It doesn't deploy or release
half the follicles in one month

02:13:53.350 --> 02:13:55.903
and then just slowly trickle
out the remainder of follicles.

02:13:55.903 --> 02:13:57.070
No, that's not how it works.

02:13:57.070 --> 02:13:59.860
What you find is that, of
course, in younger women--

02:13:59.860 --> 02:14:03.910
so, say, in their late
teens, 20s, and 30s--

02:14:03.910 --> 02:14:05.890
the ovarian reserve
in the vault is

02:14:05.890 --> 02:14:08.560
going to have more eggs
in it, and the number

02:14:08.560 --> 02:14:11.260
of follicles and eggs that
leave that vault each month

02:14:11.260 --> 02:14:12.650
is going to be quite high.

02:14:12.650 --> 02:14:16.210
So one way to evaluate
how, quote, unquote,

02:14:16.210 --> 02:14:17.710
"fertile" you are--

02:14:17.710 --> 02:14:20.890
again, just one way--
is to go to your OB/GYN

02:14:20.890 --> 02:14:23.320
and say that you would like
to know how many follicles

02:14:23.320 --> 02:14:24.507
you have in a given month.

02:14:24.507 --> 02:14:26.590
And of course, they'll
look at them on both sides,

02:14:26.590 --> 02:14:28.030
in both ovaries.

02:14:28.030 --> 02:14:32.950
And for instance, if a woman
has just two or three follicles

02:14:32.950 --> 02:14:36.323
that are out each month, well,
then the assumption-- again,

02:14:36.323 --> 02:14:38.740
it's just an assumption-- but
the assumption that's pretty

02:14:38.740 --> 02:14:41.500
good-- because there is this
positive correlation that

02:14:41.500 --> 02:14:42.400
generally occurs--

02:14:42.400 --> 02:14:44.950
is that that ovarian reserve--

02:14:44.950 --> 02:14:46.810
that the number of
eggs in the vault

02:14:46.810 --> 02:14:49.090
is fairly low
compared to someone

02:14:49.090 --> 02:14:53.200
who, say, has 20 follicles
or 30 follicles each month.

02:14:53.200 --> 02:14:54.490
And that's the typical trend.

02:14:54.490 --> 02:14:55.700
Again, these are averages.

02:14:55.700 --> 02:14:58.330
And it's very important to not
get attached to any one number

02:14:58.330 --> 02:14:58.830
here.

02:14:58.830 --> 02:15:00.170
Again, these are averages.

02:15:00.170 --> 02:15:05.230
So for instance, there are women
who only deploy five follicles

02:15:05.230 --> 02:15:07.810
and eggs each month out
of their ovarian vault

02:15:07.810 --> 02:15:09.800
but who find themselves
to be very fertile.

02:15:09.800 --> 02:15:11.800
And there could be a
number of different factors

02:15:11.800 --> 02:15:12.490
to explain that.

02:15:12.490 --> 02:15:15.130
Other women will
have 20 or 30 eggs

02:15:15.130 --> 02:15:17.710
and follicles that leave that
vault, the ovarian reserve,

02:15:17.710 --> 02:15:18.263
each month.

02:15:18.263 --> 02:15:19.930
And they will have a
harder time getting

02:15:19.930 --> 02:15:21.805
pregnant for any number
of different reasons.

02:15:21.805 --> 02:15:23.980
But in general, the
more eggs and follicles

02:15:23.980 --> 02:15:27.280
that leave the vault each
month, the higher number

02:15:27.280 --> 02:15:29.950
of eggs that are still in
reserve, meaning the greater

02:15:29.950 --> 02:15:32.650
amount of time over which
a given woman could still

02:15:32.650 --> 02:15:35.900
attempt to have
successful fertilizations.

02:15:35.900 --> 02:15:39.138
Now, this small collection
of follicles and eggs

02:15:39.138 --> 02:15:41.180
that are released each
month actually has a name.

02:15:41.180 --> 02:15:42.400
They're called antral follicles.

02:15:42.400 --> 02:15:43.483
These are small follicles.

02:15:43.483 --> 02:15:45.730
They tend to be about 2
to 9 millimeters across.

02:15:45.730 --> 02:15:47.740
The way these are
analyzed or measured

02:15:47.740 --> 02:15:52.030
is woman will go into the OB/GYN
office, and by ultrasound--

02:15:52.030 --> 02:15:53.710
typically there's
some local anesthesia,

02:15:53.710 --> 02:15:55.900
but it's not often a
general anesthesia,

02:15:55.900 --> 02:15:58.990
but by local anesthesia or
sometimes no anesthesia--

02:15:58.990 --> 02:16:02.110
they will essentially count
the number of follicles that

02:16:02.110 --> 02:16:05.050
are present in each side,
on ovary on the left

02:16:05.050 --> 02:16:08.770
and the ovary on the right, and
give a woman some sense of how

02:16:08.770 --> 02:16:09.940
many follicles she has.

02:16:09.940 --> 02:16:12.280
And typically this is done
over a series of months

02:16:12.280 --> 02:16:15.490
to determine how many eggs
are leaving the ovarian

02:16:15.490 --> 02:16:17.890
reserve each month and
therefore how many eggs

02:16:17.890 --> 02:16:21.490
she is likely to still have
in the ovarian reserve.

02:16:21.490 --> 02:16:24.130
now there's a noninvasive
way to do this, as well.

02:16:24.130 --> 02:16:27.370
Although, typically, an OB/GYN
will do both what I just

02:16:27.370 --> 02:16:30.670
described with ultrasound and
measure something called AMH,

02:16:30.670 --> 02:16:34.209
which is anti-Müllerian hormone,
which is a hormone that is

02:16:34.209 --> 02:16:37.120
released by that antral
follicle population,

02:16:37.120 --> 02:16:40.480
the population of follicles
and eggs that leave the ovarian

02:16:40.480 --> 02:16:41.350
reserve each month.

02:16:41.350 --> 02:16:44.500
So one is a blood draw
measure of a hormone, AMH.

02:16:44.500 --> 02:16:46.750
The other is a structural
imaging measure

02:16:46.750 --> 02:16:49.389
of the antral
follicles directly.

02:16:49.389 --> 02:16:53.030
again the typical trend is for
the number of antral follicles

02:16:53.030 --> 02:16:54.600
to decline over time.

02:16:54.600 --> 02:16:56.480
So one might expect,
for instance,

02:16:56.480 --> 02:17:00.290
that a woman in her 20s or
30s might have 20, 30, maybe

02:17:00.290 --> 02:17:02.478
even 40 antral
follicles that are

02:17:02.478 --> 02:17:03.770
exiting the reserve each month.

02:17:03.770 --> 02:17:07.100
And again, that's the
total across both ovaries.

02:17:07.100 --> 02:17:08.520
Again, these are just averages.

02:17:08.520 --> 02:17:09.620
These are going to
be distributions.

02:17:09.620 --> 02:17:10.850
There will be people
with far fewer.

02:17:10.850 --> 02:17:12.308
There will be people
with far more.

02:17:12.308 --> 02:17:18.139
But that over time, regardless
of where a woman starts out,

02:17:18.139 --> 02:17:21.240
from one decade to the
next half decade and decade

02:17:21.240 --> 02:17:24.469
and so on, that the number of
antral follicles will decline

02:17:24.469 --> 02:17:28.770
and the amount of or the levels
of AMH will also decline.

02:17:28.770 --> 02:17:30.629
So what does this all mean?

02:17:30.629 --> 02:17:32.360
What this means
is that if you are

02:17:32.360 --> 02:17:37.730
a woman who is in her 20s or
30s or 40s, whatever your age,

02:17:37.730 --> 02:17:40.290
if you are interested in
conceiving in the future,

02:17:40.290 --> 02:17:44.600
it's very likely a good
idea to go to your OB/GYN

02:17:44.600 --> 02:17:48.860
and get either your AMH levels
measured or your follicle count

02:17:48.860 --> 02:17:52.010
measured and to do that several
times in a given period.

02:17:52.010 --> 02:17:53.510
And I don't mean a
menstrual period.

02:17:53.510 --> 02:17:55.780
I mean given a period of
time across several months

02:17:55.780 --> 02:17:58.280
to determine what is the average
number of follicles, what's

02:17:58.280 --> 02:18:02.240
your average AMH level,
thereby giving you

02:18:02.240 --> 02:18:05.990
some window into how many
eggs you are likely to still

02:18:05.990 --> 02:18:07.370
have in your ovarian reserve.

02:18:07.370 --> 02:18:10.100
I cannot tell you how many women
that I've spoken to and how

02:18:10.100 --> 02:18:10.700
many OB/GYNs--

02:18:10.700 --> 02:18:12.200
more importantly,
because they speak

02:18:12.200 --> 02:18:16.010
to many more women about this
than I ever have or ever will--

02:18:16.010 --> 02:18:18.750
wish that they had
done this earlier.

02:18:18.750 --> 02:18:20.330
They think, oh,
well, I'm in my 20s,

02:18:20.330 --> 02:18:22.038
so I'm likely to have
a ton of follicles,

02:18:22.038 --> 02:18:23.413
or they got pregnant
once before,

02:18:23.413 --> 02:18:25.955
and so they're not so concerned
about the number of follicles

02:18:25.955 --> 02:18:27.020
or their AMH levels.

02:18:27.020 --> 02:18:29.450
But over and over
again, I was told

02:18:29.450 --> 02:18:32.270
in researching for this
episode that the earlier

02:18:32.270 --> 02:18:35.510
and more frequent that women
do this procedure of measuring

02:18:35.510 --> 02:18:38.450
AMH and measuring
their follicle count,

02:18:38.450 --> 02:18:40.730
the higher the probability
that they will eventually

02:18:40.730 --> 02:18:42.830
have a successful
fertilization and pregnancy

02:18:42.830 --> 02:18:44.360
when they seek to do so.

02:18:44.360 --> 02:18:47.780
Now, the mirror image of all
this, of course, is the sperm.

02:18:47.780 --> 02:18:50.299
And there's a kind of
common misconception

02:18:50.299 --> 02:18:53.700
out there that, you know,
the sperm, you only need one.

02:18:53.700 --> 02:18:54.920
And indeed you only need one.

02:18:54.920 --> 02:18:57.410
But actually, you
need many, and it's

02:18:57.410 --> 02:19:01.250
only one that's able to
successfully fertilize the egg.

02:19:01.250 --> 02:19:02.840
So this whole
concept of you only

02:19:02.840 --> 02:19:05.660
need one is both
dismissive of the sperm

02:19:05.660 --> 02:19:07.610
but more importantly
dismissive of the biology

02:19:07.610 --> 02:19:09.860
of the sperm and the egg.

02:19:09.860 --> 02:19:13.653
It only takes one successful
sperm and one successful egg,

02:19:13.653 --> 02:19:15.320
but that's sort of
like telling a woman,

02:19:15.320 --> 02:19:17.299
hey, you only need one egg.

02:19:17.299 --> 02:19:21.260
You need one egg of sufficient
quality in the right time

02:19:21.260 --> 02:19:23.690
and place, and
you need one sperm

02:19:23.690 --> 02:19:26.240
of sufficient quality in
the right time and place

02:19:26.240 --> 02:19:28.580
in order to get successful
fertilization and hopefully

02:19:28.580 --> 02:19:29.930
pregnancy.

02:19:29.930 --> 02:19:34.219
But you need a lot
of sperm in order

02:19:34.219 --> 02:19:38.209
to get a high probability
that that one sperm will

02:19:38.209 --> 02:19:40.379
be able to successfully
fertilize the egg.

02:19:40.379 --> 02:19:43.250
So we have this image of
sperm as these dumb operators

02:19:43.250 --> 02:19:46.603
that just sort of swim
mindlessly towards anything.

02:19:46.603 --> 02:19:49.020
And if they bump into an egg,
then they fertilize the egg.

02:19:49.020 --> 02:19:50.780
And that's really
not the way it works.

02:19:50.780 --> 02:19:52.580
As I talked about
earlier, the sperm--

02:19:52.580 --> 02:19:54.470
with its head, its
mid region, its tail,

02:19:54.470 --> 02:19:57.200
chock a block with mitochondria
in the mid region--

02:19:57.200 --> 02:20:01.190
is really an active motile
cell that indeed will just

02:20:01.190 --> 02:20:04.340
swim forward, if it's a healthy,
forward progressing sperm.

02:20:04.340 --> 02:20:07.190
But many males out
there just simply

02:20:07.190 --> 02:20:10.040
do not have any knowledge
of how many quality

02:20:10.040 --> 02:20:11.630
sperm that they happen to have.

02:20:11.630 --> 02:20:13.490
Now, given the fact
that sperm analysis

02:20:13.490 --> 02:20:17.270
is relatively inexpensive and
also the fact that freezing

02:20:17.270 --> 02:20:19.600
sperm is relatively
inexpensive, I

02:20:19.600 --> 02:20:22.430
think it stands to reason that
most men should at least get

02:20:22.430 --> 02:20:25.747
some window into the number
and quality of their sperm.

02:20:25.747 --> 02:20:27.830
Now, it's a fair assumption
to say that if someone

02:20:27.830 --> 02:20:31.670
is in their late teens
or early 20s or 30s

02:20:31.670 --> 02:20:33.620
that they probably have
high-quality sperm.

02:20:33.620 --> 02:20:36.440
But again, as with the
egg and the importance

02:20:36.440 --> 02:20:39.800
of measuring AMH and
follicle count across time,

02:20:39.800 --> 02:20:42.205
men should really evaluate
the quality and number

02:20:42.205 --> 02:20:42.830
of their sperm.

02:20:42.830 --> 02:20:44.247
And we talked a
little bit earlier

02:20:44.247 --> 02:20:47.840
about some of the parameters
that urologists and OB/GYNs

02:20:47.840 --> 02:20:50.840
like to see when
evaluating sperm.

02:20:50.840 --> 02:20:53.960
There's a minimum number
or concentration of sperm

02:20:53.960 --> 02:20:56.330
that they'd like to see if
a couple is going to use

02:20:56.330 --> 02:20:58.070
IVF, in-vitro fertilization.

02:20:58.070 --> 02:21:00.500
And typically that's going
to be about 15 to 20 million

02:21:00.500 --> 02:21:03.680
per mil of sperm or semen.

02:21:03.680 --> 02:21:06.860
And typically they want to
see somewhere between 2 and 5

02:21:06.860 --> 02:21:09.860
milliliters of semen,
overall, in a given

02:21:09.860 --> 02:21:14.120
ejaculate after a 72 to 48 hour
abstinence period, because,

02:21:14.120 --> 02:21:15.920
of course, the
more ejaculations,

02:21:15.920 --> 02:21:19.520
the smaller the volume
of the ejaculate

02:21:19.520 --> 02:21:21.090
in a short period of time.

02:21:21.090 --> 02:21:24.080
But after 48 to 72
hours, you more or less

02:21:24.080 --> 02:21:26.300
maximize the volume
of ejaculate.

02:21:26.300 --> 02:21:29.270
And then, of course, they
want to see 50% but typically

02:21:29.270 --> 02:21:32.730
60% or more of motile
sperm in order to get IVF,

02:21:32.730 --> 02:21:33.790
but more is better.

02:21:33.790 --> 02:21:35.540
And of course, there
is an enormous range,

02:21:35.540 --> 02:21:36.457
as I mentioned before.

02:21:36.457 --> 02:21:41.150
Some males will have anywhere
from 10 to 20 million sperm

02:21:41.150 --> 02:21:44.480
per milliliter of
ejaculate, and some men

02:21:44.480 --> 02:21:47.495
will have 100 to 200 million.

02:21:47.495 --> 02:21:49.370
But just because they
have 100 to 200 million

02:21:49.370 --> 02:21:51.832
doesn't mean that all of those
sperm are of high quality

02:21:51.832 --> 02:21:52.790
and can fertilize eggs.

02:21:52.790 --> 02:21:55.700
Sometimes more than
half will be twitchers,

02:21:55.700 --> 02:21:57.810
and some will be immotile,
and so on and so forth.

02:21:57.810 --> 02:21:59.883
So it's very
straightforward what

02:21:59.883 --> 02:22:01.550
I believe most people
should do and what

02:22:01.550 --> 02:22:05.030
the urologists I spoke to
in advance of this episode

02:22:05.030 --> 02:22:07.820
said to do, which is to
simply do a sperm analysis.

02:22:07.820 --> 02:22:11.090
Refrain from ejaculation
for 48 to 72 hours.

02:22:11.090 --> 02:22:12.890
Give a sperm sample.

02:22:12.890 --> 02:22:14.630
Have that sperm sample analyzed.

02:22:14.630 --> 02:22:19.040
The cost of the sperm analysis
is not typically that much.

02:22:19.040 --> 02:22:22.640
And considering that conception
and healthy conception

02:22:22.640 --> 02:22:24.800
and fertilization is
an expensive process

02:22:24.800 --> 02:22:27.500
if you have to go the
in-vitro fertilization route,

02:22:27.500 --> 02:22:30.080
it stands to reason that the
cost is pretty well justified.

02:22:30.080 --> 02:22:32.660
You also have the option
to freeze sperm over time.

02:22:32.660 --> 02:22:35.330
There is evidence that
the age of the father

02:22:35.330 --> 02:22:37.550
and therefore the
age of the sperm

02:22:37.550 --> 02:22:39.230
can dictate whether
or not there's

02:22:39.230 --> 02:22:42.800
a higher incidence of
problematic pregnancy

02:22:42.800 --> 02:22:45.380
or developmental outcomes,
including autism.

02:22:45.380 --> 02:22:46.708
That is true.

02:22:46.708 --> 02:22:48.500
You've probably heard
that if the father is

02:22:48.500 --> 02:22:51.530
40 years or older, the
incidence of autism

02:22:51.530 --> 02:22:52.850
is increased significantly.

02:22:52.850 --> 02:22:53.690
That is true.

02:22:53.690 --> 02:22:58.880
Although the overall probability
of having an autistic offspring

02:22:58.880 --> 02:23:01.760
if somebody-- if the father,
that is-- is 40 years or older

02:23:01.760 --> 02:23:04.880
is still quite a bit lower
than you would imagine.

02:23:04.880 --> 02:23:08.490
It's not as if the probability
suddenly skyrockets.

02:23:08.490 --> 02:23:10.400
So we'll have an
episode on autism

02:23:10.400 --> 02:23:13.850
and genetic and
non-genetic influences

02:23:13.850 --> 02:23:16.910
on autism and other aspects
of the autism spectrum.

02:23:16.910 --> 02:23:19.700
But the point is this.

02:23:19.700 --> 02:23:22.040
I believe and the
urologists I spoke

02:23:22.040 --> 02:23:24.800
to who are interested in
fertility and male health

02:23:24.800 --> 02:23:26.930
and sexual health
suggest that men

02:23:26.930 --> 02:23:31.010
get their sperm analyzed
at least once every five

02:23:31.010 --> 02:23:33.350
years and certainly,
if they're going

02:23:33.350 --> 02:23:36.050
to want to conceive children
in the distant future,

02:23:36.050 --> 02:23:38.690
that they consider freezing
their sperm because that, too,

02:23:38.690 --> 02:23:41.850
is fairly nominal cost in order
to freeze sperm at a younger

02:23:41.850 --> 02:23:42.350
age.

02:23:42.350 --> 02:23:44.540
And of course, if you
can freeze and use sperm

02:23:44.540 --> 02:23:47.220
from the time in which you
were younger, why wouldn't you,

02:23:47.220 --> 02:23:47.720
right?

02:23:47.720 --> 02:23:50.360
I mean, you can still opt
to go for natural pregnancy

02:23:50.360 --> 02:23:51.890
later if that's
what you want to do.

02:23:51.890 --> 02:23:55.310
But having that in reserve
is generally a good idea.

02:23:55.310 --> 02:23:58.010
And I discussed some of the
parameters that are looked for.

02:23:58.010 --> 02:24:00.710
And perhaps most
importantly, there

02:24:00.710 --> 02:24:03.470
is the possibility of an
underlying issue whereby,

02:24:03.470 --> 02:24:09.020
for instance, there is very
little sperm in an ejaculate.

02:24:09.020 --> 02:24:11.780
As I mentioned earlier, the
seminal fluid in the ejaculate

02:24:11.780 --> 02:24:14.540
could have zero sperm in it,
but the volume of ejaculate

02:24:14.540 --> 02:24:16.080
could appear completely normal.

02:24:16.080 --> 02:24:19.400
So just because your ejaculate
volume is normal to you

02:24:19.400 --> 02:24:22.772
or is in that range
of 2 to 5 milliliters,

02:24:22.772 --> 02:24:24.230
well, then that
doesn't necessarily

02:24:24.230 --> 02:24:25.688
mean that there
are any sperm there

02:24:25.688 --> 02:24:30.080
or that there are very few sperm
there and the few sperm that

02:24:30.080 --> 02:24:33.120
are there or the many sperm that
there are functionally motile.

02:24:33.120 --> 02:24:34.250
So get this analyzed.

02:24:34.250 --> 02:24:35.257
It's really worth doing.

02:24:35.257 --> 02:24:37.590
And again, it's not something
you have to do every year.

02:24:37.590 --> 02:24:40.370
It's something that you want to
do probably every five years,

02:24:40.370 --> 02:24:41.480
at least until the
point where you've

02:24:41.480 --> 02:24:43.813
conceived as many children
as you ever want to conceive.

02:24:43.813 --> 02:24:46.370
So the basic takeaway here
is that, if you're a woman,

02:24:46.370 --> 02:24:49.940
to get your egg count--
your antral follicle count,

02:24:49.940 --> 02:24:50.780
that is--

02:24:50.780 --> 02:24:54.950
and therefore your reserve
of eggs, indirectly measured,

02:24:54.950 --> 02:24:57.590
and of course also get
your AMH levels measured,

02:24:57.590 --> 02:24:59.720
and if you're a male to
have a sperm analysis

02:24:59.720 --> 02:25:01.100
and to do that relatively early.

02:25:01.100 --> 02:25:02.600
In fact, another
incentive for doing

02:25:02.600 --> 02:25:04.267
that early is that
you have a comparison

02:25:04.267 --> 02:25:06.780
point so that, for instance,
if you are in your early 20s

02:25:06.780 --> 02:25:08.780
and you're not thinking
about having kids at all

02:25:08.780 --> 02:25:10.370
or you're thinking that
you might someday have kids

02:25:10.370 --> 02:25:13.280
but it's a really someday,
someday, far off in the future,

02:25:13.280 --> 02:25:16.280
well, it's wonderful to have
a reference point from which

02:25:16.280 --> 02:25:19.460
to compare your biology
in your early 20s

02:25:19.460 --> 02:25:22.490
to your biology in your
mid or late 30s or 40s when

02:25:22.490 --> 02:25:25.340
you might happen to be
interested in conceiving.

02:25:25.340 --> 02:25:28.550
And if that doesn't
provide incentive enough,

02:25:28.550 --> 02:25:30.950
I should mention-- and this
is important to point out

02:25:30.950 --> 02:25:34.100
and that I think both
males and females are not

02:25:34.100 --> 02:25:38.030
aware of-- is that one in
five couples that have issues

02:25:38.030 --> 02:25:41.150
with fertility,
the issue ends up

02:25:41.150 --> 02:25:44.720
falling on the biology that
is the quality of the sperm

02:25:44.720 --> 02:25:46.830
or a lack of number of sperm.

02:25:46.830 --> 02:25:49.550
So I think there's a
misconception that when

02:25:49.550 --> 02:25:52.740
fertility is an issue it's
always an issue with the eggs

02:25:52.740 --> 02:25:56.507
and this age-dependent decline
in the egg quality-- again,

02:25:56.507 --> 02:25:59.090
it's the best language we have
available to us at the moment--

02:25:59.090 --> 02:26:02.630
this age-dependent decline in
egg quality is often to blame,

02:26:02.630 --> 02:26:03.560
but not always.

02:26:03.560 --> 02:26:06.147
One in five couples that
have challenges conceiving it

02:26:06.147 --> 02:26:08.480
turns out that it's going to
be an issue with the sperm.

02:26:08.480 --> 02:26:09.920
And of course, there are a
number of different sperm

02:26:09.920 --> 02:26:12.860
analyses that, should all
the other parameters of sperm

02:26:12.860 --> 02:26:14.870
appear normal,
now, for instance,

02:26:14.870 --> 02:26:17.472
you can get a DNA
fragmentation analysis.

02:26:17.472 --> 02:26:19.430
You can see whether or
not the DNA of the sperm

02:26:19.430 --> 02:26:20.990
are somehow disrupted.

02:26:20.990 --> 02:26:24.530
Urologists these days are
excellent at figuring out,

02:26:24.530 --> 02:26:27.230
for instance, if a male
has lots and lots of sperm,

02:26:27.230 --> 02:26:30.200
everything looks great, but the
shape of the head of the sperm

02:26:30.200 --> 02:26:32.240
isn't quite right-- if
it's not oval enough

02:26:32.240 --> 02:26:35.690
and it's too rounded, that could
be a genetic defect under which

02:26:35.690 --> 02:26:41.150
conditions there is zero
probability of the male ever

02:26:41.150 --> 02:26:44.780
naturally conceiving, regardless
of who the female partner is.

02:26:44.780 --> 02:26:47.120
Believe it or not, males
can have a ton of sperm,

02:26:47.120 --> 02:26:49.400
but if they carry a
certain genetic defect,

02:26:49.400 --> 02:26:52.940
those sperm will be incapable
of depositing those 23

02:26:52.940 --> 02:26:55.080
chromosomes into the egg.

02:26:55.080 --> 02:26:58.400
However, there are ways
in which that sperm can

02:26:58.400 --> 02:27:01.160
be coaxed or forced
to fertilize the egg

02:27:01.160 --> 02:27:03.710
and deposit its genetic contents
by in-vitro fertilization

02:27:03.710 --> 02:27:05.370
and then implantation
into the female.

02:27:05.370 --> 02:27:08.540
So again, lots of
reasons to have a egg

02:27:08.540 --> 02:27:10.850
reserve analysis by
ultrasound and AMH

02:27:10.850 --> 02:27:13.460
for females and lots
of reasons for males

02:27:13.460 --> 02:27:14.870
to have a sperm analysis.

02:27:14.870 --> 02:27:17.090
And of course, typically
with a sperm analysis

02:27:17.090 --> 02:27:22.720
and a ovarian reserve analysis
will be a hormone analysis.

02:27:22.720 --> 02:27:26.530
And I'm a very strong believer
in people getting an insight--

02:27:26.530 --> 02:27:27.400
that is, a window--

02:27:27.400 --> 02:27:30.250
into their hormonal
composition, not just

02:27:30.250 --> 02:27:32.980
when they encounter
problems but starting

02:27:32.980 --> 02:27:35.590
at a pretty early age, even if
it's only done once every five

02:27:35.590 --> 02:27:38.770
years or so, having a
reference point to your 20s

02:27:38.770 --> 02:27:41.650
and to your 30s and mid-30s for
when you felt a certain way.

02:27:41.650 --> 02:27:44.200
Maybe, as in the case
for many people I know,

02:27:44.200 --> 02:27:45.880
they actually feel
better in their 40s

02:27:45.880 --> 02:27:47.170
than they did in their
20s because they're

02:27:47.170 --> 02:27:48.760
doing a lot of things
to support their health.

02:27:48.760 --> 02:27:49.760
That is possible.

02:27:49.760 --> 02:27:51.760
But in many cases,
people start feeling

02:27:51.760 --> 02:27:55.103
not as well or their fertility
seems to be dropping off

02:27:55.103 --> 02:27:57.520
or any number of different
parameters that we've discussed

02:27:57.520 --> 02:28:00.100
today were related to
vitality and longevity seem

02:28:00.100 --> 02:28:01.960
to be dropping off
over time, and they

02:28:01.960 --> 02:28:04.745
want to get a insight into
what could be the issue.

02:28:04.745 --> 02:28:06.370
And hormones are
sometimes, not always,

02:28:06.370 --> 02:28:09.200
but sometimes involved in
those underlying issues.

02:28:09.200 --> 02:28:13.210
And there is nothing as valuable
as having a reference point

02:28:13.210 --> 02:28:15.490
from a time in which
things were going well

02:28:15.490 --> 02:28:18.850
to evaluate the, for
instance, levels of hormones,

02:28:18.850 --> 02:28:21.920
not just testosterone but
also estrogen and progesterone

02:28:21.920 --> 02:28:22.850
and so forth.

02:28:22.850 --> 02:28:24.550
So you need a comparison
point in order

02:28:24.550 --> 02:28:26.570
to determine what really
needs to be changed.

02:28:26.570 --> 02:28:30.058
So all of this is a strong
push for people to use

02:28:30.058 --> 02:28:32.350
your insurance, if you're
able to put it on insurance--

02:28:32.350 --> 02:28:34.390
oftentimes people are--

02:28:34.390 --> 02:28:38.920
and if not, to try and find a
reasonable or reasonably priced

02:28:38.920 --> 02:28:42.340
way to do a sperm
and egg analysis

02:28:42.340 --> 02:28:45.380
and to ideally do a
hormone analysis as well.

02:28:45.380 --> 02:28:47.860
It's really going to set you
up for the maximum probability

02:28:47.860 --> 02:28:49.985
of being able to conceive
children when you want to

02:28:49.985 --> 02:28:52.960
and also to avoid a bunch of
other health-related issues

02:28:52.960 --> 02:28:56.350
that involve hormones
and reproductive health

02:28:56.350 --> 02:28:59.290
and, in general, to support
your mental health and physical

02:28:59.290 --> 02:28:59.805
health.

02:28:59.805 --> 02:29:01.930
So I've been talking about
a bunch of things to do.

02:29:01.930 --> 02:29:05.470
There are a couple of things to
be mindful of to actively avoid

02:29:05.470 --> 02:29:08.410
if your goal is to be
and remain fertile.

02:29:08.410 --> 02:29:10.300
And that's regardless
of whether or not

02:29:10.300 --> 02:29:13.240
you want to conceive children
in the future or not.

02:29:13.240 --> 02:29:15.040
Now, in the context
of this discussion,

02:29:15.040 --> 02:29:16.750
the same things that
we've heard to be

02:29:16.750 --> 02:29:18.430
true for other
aspects of our health

02:29:18.430 --> 02:29:20.060
turn out to also be true.

02:29:20.060 --> 02:29:22.660
So let's just start
with the basics.

02:29:22.660 --> 02:29:26.430
Everybody should be getting
approximately six to eight

02:29:26.430 --> 02:29:27.640
hours of sleep every night.

02:29:27.640 --> 02:29:29.110
That should be quality sleep.

02:29:29.110 --> 02:29:31.977
Optimizing your sleep is
fundamental to balancing

02:29:31.977 --> 02:29:32.560
your hormones.

02:29:32.560 --> 02:29:34.060
Now, balancing your
hormones is kind

02:29:34.060 --> 02:29:36.520
of a catch phrase for all
things related to proper hormone

02:29:36.520 --> 02:29:38.050
regulation.

02:29:38.050 --> 02:29:40.190
Sleep is the fundamental
layer of mental health,

02:29:40.190 --> 02:29:42.610
physical health, and
performance of all kinds

02:29:42.610 --> 02:29:44.680
and, believe it
or not, fertility.

02:29:44.680 --> 02:29:47.350
When people are not
sleeping well or enough,

02:29:47.350 --> 02:29:49.510
stress hormones, in
particular cortisol,

02:29:49.510 --> 02:29:51.670
shift to peaking
later in the day,

02:29:51.670 --> 02:29:54.130
and those elevated cortisol
levels later in the day

02:29:54.130 --> 02:29:56.410
cause a bunch of
different problems

02:29:56.410 --> 02:29:59.110
in both males and females,
many of which impact fertility.

02:29:59.110 --> 02:30:03.080
So controlling cortisol starts
with controlling your sleep.

02:30:03.080 --> 02:30:06.890
It also impacts testosterone
and estrogen levels.

02:30:06.890 --> 02:30:09.400
So of course, the proper ratios
of testosterone and estrogen

02:30:09.400 --> 02:30:11.300
will vary from males to females.

02:30:11.300 --> 02:30:13.480
But in order to get
those right or as right

02:30:13.480 --> 02:30:15.473
as they can be without
other interventions,

02:30:15.473 --> 02:30:17.890
you want to make sure you're
getting enough quality sleep.

02:30:17.890 --> 02:30:18.610
How much sleep?

02:30:18.610 --> 02:30:21.580
Most people need about six to
eight hours of sleep per night.

02:30:21.580 --> 02:30:23.277
Waking up once,
maybe twice per night

02:30:23.277 --> 02:30:25.360
in the middle of the night
and going back to sleep

02:30:25.360 --> 02:30:28.150
is not such a big deal, but six
to eight hours of solid sleep

02:30:28.150 --> 02:30:28.788
would be ideal.

02:30:28.788 --> 02:30:30.580
Some people need a
little bit less in order

02:30:30.580 --> 02:30:32.152
to function-- five hours.

02:30:32.152 --> 02:30:33.610
Some people need
a little bit more.

02:30:33.610 --> 02:30:36.125
Developing teenagers and babies
and kids need a lot more.

02:30:36.125 --> 02:30:38.000
People who are sick or
recovering from injury

02:30:38.000 --> 02:30:38.740
need a lot more.

02:30:38.740 --> 02:30:40.990
We've done multiple
episodes on sleep.

02:30:40.990 --> 02:30:43.090
We have a toolkit for
sleep available free

02:30:43.090 --> 02:30:44.378
at hubermanlab.com.

02:30:44.378 --> 02:30:44.920
You go there.

02:30:44.920 --> 02:30:46.780
You don't even have to
sign up for the newsletter,

02:30:46.780 --> 02:30:47.988
although you can if you want.

02:30:47.988 --> 02:30:50.230
Just go to a Toolkit for
Sleep under the menu,

02:30:50.230 --> 02:30:52.000
and you'll be able
to download that,

02:30:52.000 --> 02:30:53.210
or you can even just
view it on the screen

02:30:53.210 --> 02:30:54.100
if you don't want
to download it.

02:30:54.100 --> 02:30:54.975
It has lots of tools.

02:30:54.975 --> 02:30:58.030
We've done an episode
called "Perfect Your Sleep"

02:30:58.030 --> 02:31:00.067
that has a lot of tools.

02:31:00.067 --> 02:31:01.400
They're all timestamped for you.

02:31:01.400 --> 02:31:03.520
We've done a "Master Your
Sleep" episode, so lots of tools

02:31:03.520 --> 02:31:04.520
to get your sleep right.

02:31:04.520 --> 02:31:06.370
Get your sleep right
if you are wishing

02:31:06.370 --> 02:31:09.820
to conceive and/or to
simply have healthy biology,

02:31:09.820 --> 02:31:11.100
to be fertile, or otherwise.

02:31:11.100 --> 02:31:12.100
That's just fundamental.

02:31:12.100 --> 02:31:15.490
Now, there are other
things to not do.

02:31:15.490 --> 02:31:18.063
And those, again, fall into the
somewhat obvious categories,

02:31:18.063 --> 02:31:19.480
but I think a lot
of people aren't

02:31:19.480 --> 02:31:24.130
aware of just how striking an
effect these certain behaviors

02:31:24.130 --> 02:31:26.920
that you want to avoid can have
in diminishing your fertility

02:31:26.920 --> 02:31:28.157
for both males and females.

02:31:28.157 --> 02:31:29.240
So let's talk about those.

02:31:29.240 --> 02:31:30.640
The first one is smoking.

02:31:30.640 --> 02:31:32.140
And when we talk
about smoking here,

02:31:32.140 --> 02:31:34.660
we're talking about
smoking nicotine

02:31:34.660 --> 02:31:36.730
and we're talking
about smoking cannabis.

02:31:36.730 --> 02:31:38.380
And indeed, there
are strong data--

02:31:38.380 --> 02:31:39.970
and I will put a
reference to one

02:31:39.970 --> 02:31:42.250
of the better larger
analyses of these data.

02:31:42.250 --> 02:31:44.380
There are strong data
showing that cannabis

02:31:44.380 --> 02:31:45.920
reduces fertility.

02:31:45.920 --> 02:31:48.490
Now, I can already hear
the screams from the back,

02:31:48.490 --> 02:31:52.300
although they're probably
fairly drawled out screams,

02:31:52.300 --> 02:31:54.950
from the back of people
saying they smoke cannabis

02:31:54.950 --> 02:31:56.920
and they had no
trouble conceiving.

02:31:56.920 --> 02:31:58.420
Certainly, there
will be exceptions.

02:31:58.420 --> 02:32:00.340
But whether or not
you're male or female,

02:32:00.340 --> 02:32:02.530
smoking cannabis is a
bad idea if you want

02:32:02.530 --> 02:32:03.850
to conceive a healthy child.

02:32:03.850 --> 02:32:07.630
Can you still conceive a healthy
child while smoking cannabis?

02:32:07.630 --> 02:32:09.340
Probably certain people can.

02:32:09.340 --> 02:32:12.850
Many people will greatly
decrease the probability

02:32:12.850 --> 02:32:16.400
of a healthy fertilization and
pregnancy by smoking cannabis.

02:32:16.400 --> 02:32:18.870
There are excellent
data to support that.

02:32:18.870 --> 02:32:22.110
As well, nicotine,
both smoked or vaped,

02:32:22.110 --> 02:32:27.150
is going to disrupt the
process of fertilization

02:32:27.150 --> 02:32:29.830
and can disrupt
pregnancy dramatically.

02:32:29.830 --> 02:32:31.075
So just avoid it altogether.

02:32:31.075 --> 02:32:31.950
How does this happen?

02:32:31.950 --> 02:32:34.325
Well, it turns out that smoking
increases what are called

02:32:34.325 --> 02:32:35.740
reactive oxygen species.

02:32:35.740 --> 02:32:38.088
This greatly
disrupts the quality

02:32:38.088 --> 02:32:40.380
of the egg at the level of
the spindle and mitochondria

02:32:40.380 --> 02:32:41.820
and a number of other features.

02:32:41.820 --> 02:32:45.450
And in the sperm, turns out
that smoking doesn't necessarily

02:32:45.450 --> 02:32:47.340
disrupt the sperm
directly, although it

02:32:47.340 --> 02:32:50.070
can cause DNA
fragmentation, which

02:32:50.070 --> 02:32:51.900
can cause all sorts
of abnormalities,

02:32:51.900 --> 02:32:54.360
can prevent fertilization,
can lead to birth defects

02:32:54.360 --> 02:32:55.150
in the offspring.

02:32:55.150 --> 02:32:57.720
But more importantly,
it increases

02:32:57.720 --> 02:33:00.450
what are called reactive oxygen
species in the seminal fluid,

02:33:00.450 --> 02:33:02.200
in the semen that
contain the sperm,

02:33:02.200 --> 02:33:04.980
this very, under
normal circumstances,

02:33:04.980 --> 02:33:07.140
under healthy
circumstances, beautifully

02:33:07.140 --> 02:33:10.200
orchestrated chemistry of
fluid that allows the sperm

02:33:10.200 --> 02:33:13.650
to thrive in their
trajectory and attempt

02:33:13.650 --> 02:33:16.300
to fertilize the egg and
lead to a healthy pregnancy.

02:33:16.300 --> 02:33:19.740
So if you are a smoker
and you want to conceive,

02:33:19.740 --> 02:33:21.870
the best advice I can give
you is to quit smoking.

02:33:21.870 --> 02:33:23.740
And yes, that includes
cannabis as well.

02:33:23.740 --> 02:33:25.830
Now, I am not somebody
who believes that cannabis

02:33:25.830 --> 02:33:27.220
across the board is not useful.

02:33:27.220 --> 02:33:29.470
There are medical applications
and other applications.

02:33:29.470 --> 02:33:32.160
I talk about that in an
episode all about cannabis

02:33:32.160 --> 02:33:33.300
for health and disease.

02:33:33.300 --> 02:33:34.800
And notice, health
was in there too.

02:33:34.800 --> 02:33:37.770
So you cannabis smokers,
don't come after me with--

02:33:37.770 --> 02:33:40.050
I guess, whatever it
is-- with bongs and pipes

02:33:40.050 --> 02:33:42.150
or whatever it is that
you want-- or with vapes.

02:33:42.150 --> 02:33:44.730
The point is that,
while it can be

02:33:44.730 --> 02:33:46.380
beneficial for
certain populations,

02:33:46.380 --> 02:33:48.490
it's certainly bad for others.

02:33:48.490 --> 02:33:50.550
And if you're
trying to conceive,

02:33:50.550 --> 02:33:53.880
it is bad for fertility and
for a healthy pregnancy.

02:33:53.880 --> 02:33:57.810
Now, that's smoking--
and vaping, by the way.

02:33:57.810 --> 02:33:59.400
Vaping is included there.

02:33:59.400 --> 02:34:03.420
Now, the next category of
don'ts relates to alcohol.

02:34:03.420 --> 02:34:05.820
Now, everyone has heard that
drinking during pregnancy

02:34:05.820 --> 02:34:07.050
is a bad idea.

02:34:07.050 --> 02:34:08.490
You may have heard
and some people

02:34:08.490 --> 02:34:10.350
have talked about
the fact that there

02:34:10.350 --> 02:34:13.470
are cultures in
which they allow,

02:34:13.470 --> 02:34:16.230
if you will, or
even condone, sadly,

02:34:16.230 --> 02:34:18.180
one or two drinks
while pregnant,

02:34:18.180 --> 02:34:20.790
provided it's just champagne
or something of that sort.

02:34:20.790 --> 02:34:22.450
That is a terrible idea.

02:34:22.450 --> 02:34:24.520
I did an episode
all about alcohol,

02:34:24.520 --> 02:34:26.730
both its potential
health effects,

02:34:26.730 --> 02:34:28.500
of which there turned
out to be zero.

02:34:28.500 --> 02:34:30.540
And yes, that includes red wine.

02:34:30.540 --> 02:34:32.462
It is far better to
not drink at all.

02:34:32.462 --> 02:34:34.170
And if you're going
to drink, the limit--

02:34:34.170 --> 02:34:35.520
if you're a healthy
adult who's not

02:34:35.520 --> 02:34:36.895
trying to conceive,
not pregnant,

02:34:36.895 --> 02:34:38.760
and you don't have
issues with alcoholism--

02:34:38.760 --> 02:34:42.040
is probably two
drinks per week total.

02:34:42.040 --> 02:34:44.160
That's right, two
drinks per week total.

02:34:44.160 --> 02:34:45.840
And that's the level
that you really

02:34:45.840 --> 02:34:47.760
should consider if you're a
drinker if you're somebody

02:34:47.760 --> 02:34:48.900
who's trying to conceive.

02:34:48.900 --> 02:34:51.265
However, for a woman
who becomes pregnant,

02:34:51.265 --> 02:34:53.640
the total number of drinks
that you should allow yourself

02:34:53.640 --> 02:34:57.750
per week while pregnant and
breastfeeding is indeed zero.

02:34:57.750 --> 02:35:00.870
There is absolutely no evidence
that one can, quote, unquote,

02:35:00.870 --> 02:35:03.150
"get away" with drinking
during pregnancy.

02:35:03.150 --> 02:35:04.860
And people say, well, I had
a perfectly healthy child.

02:35:04.860 --> 02:35:07.360
But, of course, you don't know
what the health of that child

02:35:07.360 --> 02:35:09.480
would have been had
you not drank at all.

02:35:09.480 --> 02:35:11.970
Now, I'm not here with any
generally strong stance

02:35:11.970 --> 02:35:12.780
against alcohol.

02:35:12.780 --> 02:35:16.680
I myself am somebody who
has a drink every once

02:35:16.680 --> 02:35:18.730
in a while, although I
don't consider myself

02:35:18.730 --> 02:35:21.600
somebody who has a strong
proclivity for alcohol.

02:35:21.600 --> 02:35:23.850
And of course, at
this moment, I'm

02:35:23.850 --> 02:35:27.010
not trying to conceive children
and I'm certainly not pregnant.

02:35:27.010 --> 02:35:28.770
So that's safe for me.

02:35:28.770 --> 02:35:31.690
But frankly, I haven't had
a drink in a very long time.

02:35:31.690 --> 02:35:32.950
And so I don't miss it.

02:35:32.950 --> 02:35:33.540
And that's me.

02:35:33.540 --> 02:35:36.840
But I do realize that a lot
of people enjoy alcohol,

02:35:36.840 --> 02:35:38.430
and so it's that
two drinks per week

02:35:38.430 --> 02:35:40.860
limit that really
sets the upper limit

02:35:40.860 --> 02:35:43.260
and threshold beyond which
you start running into issues

02:35:43.260 --> 02:35:45.120
with cellular mutation.

02:35:45.120 --> 02:35:49.380
You start running into issues
of oxidative stress, greatly

02:35:49.380 --> 02:35:51.900
increase cancer risk, in
particular breast cancer risk.

02:35:51.900 --> 02:35:54.960
All of that's covered in the
alcohol episode that we did.

02:35:54.960 --> 02:35:56.550
You can find it
at hubermanlab.com

02:35:56.550 --> 02:35:59.320
and timestamped if you want
to navigate to specific topics

02:35:59.320 --> 02:36:01.560
and so forth, find out all
about the data supporting

02:36:01.560 --> 02:36:04.120
the statements that I'm
making, so on and so forth.

02:36:04.120 --> 02:36:06.960
Now, if you're somebody who's
seeking to conceive or you fall

02:36:06.960 --> 02:36:09.450
into this category that some
couples describe themselves

02:36:09.450 --> 02:36:11.863
as we're not trying but
we're not not trying--

02:36:11.863 --> 02:36:13.530
meaning they're not
using birth control,

02:36:13.530 --> 02:36:16.830
they're kind of letting
chance run its course--

02:36:16.830 --> 02:36:18.600
well, then you
should definitely be

02:36:18.600 --> 02:36:21.090
aware of the data
showing that even just

02:36:21.090 --> 02:36:25.090
one bout, one bout of
so-called binge drinking,

02:36:25.090 --> 02:36:29.430
which is five to six drinks
in a given night or half day,

02:36:29.430 --> 02:36:32.970
in a 12-hour period-- one
bout of five to six drinks,

02:36:32.970 --> 02:36:35.250
if you're a woman
or you're a man,

02:36:35.250 --> 02:36:40.410
greatly increases both the
likelihood of mutations

02:36:40.410 --> 02:36:43.870
in the embryo that would
result from a fertilization

02:36:43.870 --> 02:36:45.870
and at the same time, for
reasons that should be

02:36:45.870 --> 02:36:48.328
obvious to you based on all
the biology we've talked about,

02:36:48.328 --> 02:36:51.070
a greatly reduced
probability of fertilization.

02:36:51.070 --> 02:36:52.830
Now, that absolutely
does not mean

02:36:52.830 --> 02:36:55.380
that you should use the
ingestion of five or six drinks

02:36:55.380 --> 02:36:57.480
as a method of birth control.

02:36:57.480 --> 02:36:58.920
That is not what
I'm saying here.

02:36:58.920 --> 02:37:02.550
What I'm saying is that, if
you go out on a given night

02:37:02.550 --> 02:37:04.770
and you have five or six
drinks and you happen

02:37:04.770 --> 02:37:06.390
to become pregnant,
the probability

02:37:06.390 --> 02:37:10.140
that that pregnancy will
be disrupted in some way

02:37:10.140 --> 02:37:11.640
is greatly increased.

02:37:11.640 --> 02:37:15.070
What the exact consequences
are, no one can tell you.

02:37:15.070 --> 02:37:19.360
But also, if you're somebody
who is interested in conceiving

02:37:19.360 --> 02:37:21.340
a child, well,
then you absolutely

02:37:21.340 --> 02:37:25.875
should abstain from ingesting
drinks more than one or two

02:37:25.875 --> 02:37:28.000
during the time in which
you're trying to conceive,

02:37:28.000 --> 02:37:29.650
and ideally it would be zero.

02:37:29.650 --> 02:37:32.110
And you certainly would
want to avoid drinking

02:37:32.110 --> 02:37:33.460
multiple drinks per night.

02:37:33.460 --> 02:37:36.970
And so this idea of going out
and having three or four drinks

02:37:36.970 --> 02:37:38.830
or four or five
drinks in a given

02:37:38.830 --> 02:37:41.020
night at a time in
which you're also

02:37:41.020 --> 02:37:44.740
trying to conceive children,
the biology tells us,

02:37:44.740 --> 02:37:47.650
the epidemiology tells us that
this is just a terrible idea.

02:37:47.650 --> 02:37:50.260
It's going to reduce the
likelihood of fertility

02:37:50.260 --> 02:37:51.680
and successful pregnancy.

02:37:51.680 --> 02:37:53.720
And if there is a
successful pregnancy,

02:37:53.720 --> 02:37:56.380
the word "success" needs
to be in quotes, right?

02:37:56.380 --> 02:37:58.450
I mean, I think every parent--

02:37:58.450 --> 02:38:00.700
every species, for
that matter-- wants

02:38:00.700 --> 02:38:04.520
to increase the probability
of having healthy offspring.

02:38:04.520 --> 02:38:08.650
And so, to my mind anyway and to
the OB/GYNs and the urologists

02:38:08.650 --> 02:38:10.900
that are focused on
fertility that I spoke to,

02:38:10.900 --> 02:38:13.480
everyone will say,
try as hard as you

02:38:13.480 --> 02:38:16.535
can to avoid these so-called
binge drinking episodes.

02:38:16.535 --> 02:38:18.160
And again, these
episodes are one night

02:38:18.160 --> 02:38:19.690
of consuming five to six drinks.

02:38:19.690 --> 02:38:22.030
Now, another important thing
to remember in this context

02:38:22.030 --> 02:38:25.990
is that the negative effects
of consuming five or six drinks

02:38:25.990 --> 02:38:29.860
in a given night extend
over many weeks following

02:38:29.860 --> 02:38:31.750
the ingestion of that alcohol.

02:38:31.750 --> 02:38:34.150
If you're a male,
what that means

02:38:34.150 --> 02:38:37.840
is that's going to impact
the quality of your sperm

02:38:37.840 --> 02:38:39.550
and greatly decrease
the likelihood

02:38:39.550 --> 02:38:44.650
of successful fertilization
and/or healthy pregnancy

02:38:44.650 --> 02:38:48.460
over the period of that entire
spermatogenesis window, which

02:38:48.460 --> 02:38:52.492
is, as we talked about before,
60 to 90 days, 60 to generate

02:38:52.492 --> 02:38:54.700
the sperm and then some
additional time for the sperm

02:38:54.700 --> 02:38:58.110
to be transported to the point
where they could be ejaculated.

02:38:58.110 --> 02:39:00.610
If you're a woman and you have
five or six drinks on a given

02:39:00.610 --> 02:39:04.180
night, well, then you are going
to disrupt the quality not

02:39:04.180 --> 02:39:06.850
of just the egg that
eventually ovulates

02:39:06.850 --> 02:39:09.340
but indeed the entire
pool of follicles that

02:39:09.340 --> 02:39:11.380
leaves the ovarian
vault in reserve

02:39:11.380 --> 02:39:13.850
and from which the one
egg will be selected.

02:39:13.850 --> 02:39:18.550
In other words, you are reducing
the quality of all of the eggs

02:39:18.550 --> 02:39:20.260
that you happen to
deploy that month.

02:39:20.260 --> 02:39:22.928
Now, some of you who were really
following the biology earlier

02:39:22.928 --> 02:39:24.970
might say, well, what if
I have those five or six

02:39:24.970 --> 02:39:28.150
drinks during the time in which
I'm menstruating, just in which

02:39:28.150 --> 02:39:29.770
there's bleeding present?

02:39:29.770 --> 02:39:32.510
And therefore, I
haven't yet ovulated.

02:39:32.510 --> 02:39:33.010
Ah!

02:39:33.010 --> 02:39:35.560
But if you remember the
biology we talked about earlier

02:39:35.560 --> 02:39:39.290
specifically, there is a
subset of follicles and eggs

02:39:39.290 --> 02:39:44.650
that leave that ovarian reserve
quite a bit before that one egg

02:39:44.650 --> 02:39:46.200
is selected for and ovulates.

02:39:46.200 --> 02:39:48.700
And of course, there are all
the different hormonal cascades

02:39:48.700 --> 02:39:50.860
and the general milieu
of the ovary which

02:39:50.860 --> 02:39:52.493
are important and
are being regulated

02:39:52.493 --> 02:39:53.410
by different hormones.

02:39:53.410 --> 02:39:55.960
And yes, indeed, the
regulation of those hormones

02:39:55.960 --> 02:39:58.435
is strongly impacted by
alcohol through a number

02:39:58.435 --> 02:40:00.310
of different pathways,
through the regulation

02:40:00.310 --> 02:40:02.893
of the neurotransmitter
GABA up in the brain--

02:40:02.893 --> 02:40:04.810
it's actually a lot of
GABA and GABA receptors

02:40:04.810 --> 02:40:06.790
in the hypothalamus, the
very region from which

02:40:06.790 --> 02:40:09.550
gonadotropin-releasing hormone,
our old friend from a couple

02:40:09.550 --> 02:40:12.070
hours ago in this
discussion, going

02:40:12.070 --> 02:40:14.080
to disrupt GnRH secretion.

02:40:14.080 --> 02:40:17.140
You can disrupt pituitary
function with alcohol.

02:40:17.140 --> 02:40:18.910
Again and again,
what we're seeing

02:40:18.910 --> 02:40:22.750
is that consuming more than
one or two drinks per week

02:40:22.750 --> 02:40:25.960
of alcohol is really detrimental
to the entire process

02:40:25.960 --> 02:40:29.440
of fertility and the entire
process of healthy pregnancy.

02:40:29.440 --> 02:40:32.170
And that's true from both
the male side and the sperm,

02:40:32.170 --> 02:40:34.630
and it's true from the
female side and the egg.

02:40:34.630 --> 02:40:36.580
So my simple advice
on this is if you

02:40:36.580 --> 02:40:40.960
are wishing to have a healthy
fertilization and pregnancy,

02:40:40.960 --> 02:40:43.340
the best thing to do would
be avoid alcohol altogether

02:40:43.340 --> 02:40:45.298
and, if you are going to
drink, to really limit

02:40:45.298 --> 02:40:48.640
that drinking to one or two
drinks per week maximum.

02:40:48.640 --> 02:40:49.900
So those are the major don'ts.

02:40:49.900 --> 02:40:51.670
Really avoid excessive stress.

02:40:51.670 --> 02:40:53.290
And I should mention,
excessive stress

02:40:53.290 --> 02:40:55.630
is not just best avoided by
getting enough quality sleep

02:40:55.630 --> 02:40:56.000
at night.

02:40:56.000 --> 02:40:57.490
Although that is
the primary way.

02:40:57.490 --> 02:40:58.900
There are other ways
to avoid stress.

02:40:58.900 --> 02:41:00.483
We've done entire
episodes about this,

02:41:00.483 --> 02:41:02.560
and we have a toolkit
related to reducing stress

02:41:02.560 --> 02:41:04.210
with very simple,
zero-cost tools.

02:41:04.210 --> 02:41:06.310
Again, you can find all
that at hubermanlab.com.

02:41:06.310 --> 02:41:07.685
And I should
mention, if you want

02:41:07.685 --> 02:41:10.090
to find any episode
or topic or timestamp,

02:41:10.090 --> 02:41:13.900
that website is keyword
search available.

02:41:13.900 --> 02:41:15.730
So you can just go
to hubermanlab.com,

02:41:15.730 --> 02:41:18.040
put into the search
function "stress tools,"

02:41:18.040 --> 02:41:19.900
and a bunch of different
links will pop up

02:41:19.900 --> 02:41:23.075
related to those topics,
likewise with sleep, likewise

02:41:23.075 --> 02:41:24.700
with any number of
different topics you

02:41:24.700 --> 02:41:25.700
might be interested in.

02:41:25.700 --> 02:41:29.050
So get enough quality sleep
and thereby reduce stress

02:41:29.050 --> 02:41:31.720
and also directly buffer
stress with real-time tools

02:41:31.720 --> 02:41:34.810
to buffer stress that I've
talked about in the episodes

02:41:34.810 --> 02:41:35.770
that you can access.

02:41:35.770 --> 02:41:39.280
And there are ways to greatly
reduce your overall level

02:41:39.280 --> 02:41:41.590
of stress, to limit
any cortisol that's

02:41:41.590 --> 02:41:44.212
released to early in the day,
which is when you want cortisol

02:41:44.212 --> 02:41:45.920
released, and not have
it late in the day

02:41:45.920 --> 02:41:47.030
and so on and so forth.

02:41:47.030 --> 02:41:48.160
So reduce your stress.

02:41:48.160 --> 02:41:53.070
And as I just told
you, by all means,

02:41:53.070 --> 02:41:55.400
do not drink more than
two drinks per week.

02:41:55.400 --> 02:41:56.810
And zero is better than two.

02:41:56.810 --> 02:41:58.460
If anyone tells you,
oh, well, there's

02:41:58.460 --> 02:42:01.940
all this resveratrol in red
wine, and that's good for us,

02:42:01.940 --> 02:42:03.500
the data simply
tell us there's not

02:42:03.500 --> 02:42:05.393
enough resveratrol in
red wine to really have

02:42:05.393 --> 02:42:06.560
any positive health benefit.

02:42:06.560 --> 02:42:08.780
The data around
resveratrol and health

02:42:08.780 --> 02:42:11.330
benefits itself is
under question nowadays.

02:42:11.330 --> 02:42:14.180
Zero alcohol is better
than any alcohol.

02:42:14.180 --> 02:42:15.800
Two drinks per
week is the limit.

02:42:15.800 --> 02:42:21.830
Also, limit or eliminate or
avoid nicotine and ideally

02:42:21.830 --> 02:42:24.710
cannabis, smoking and vaping,
at the time in which you

02:42:24.710 --> 02:42:26.480
are trying to get pregnant.

02:42:26.480 --> 02:42:28.070
And certainly, if
you are pregnant,

02:42:28.070 --> 02:42:30.800
avoid all of the things, as
best you can, that I just

02:42:30.800 --> 02:42:32.250
described a moment ago.

02:42:32.250 --> 02:42:34.542
Now, there are a couple of
other don'ts that are really

02:42:34.542 --> 02:42:35.190
important.

02:42:35.190 --> 02:42:37.790
One of the most important
don'ts relates to STIs,

02:42:37.790 --> 02:42:39.770
or sexually-transmitted
infections.

02:42:39.770 --> 02:42:42.570
Everyone who is sexually
active should get an STI check.

02:42:42.570 --> 02:42:44.660
In fact, if you go
to a fertility clinic

02:42:44.660 --> 02:42:47.120
or you go for sperm analysis
or you go for egg analysis,

02:42:47.120 --> 02:42:50.000
almost always they
will do an STI check,

02:42:50.000 --> 02:42:52.400
even if you happen to be in
a monogamous relationship,

02:42:52.400 --> 02:42:54.233
even if you happen to
be not sexually active

02:42:54.233 --> 02:42:55.650
and you're somebody
who is seeking

02:42:55.650 --> 02:42:58.010
to use IVF with a sperm donor
or something of that sort.

02:42:58.010 --> 02:42:59.253
Why would they do that?

02:42:59.253 --> 02:43:00.920
Why is there so much
concern about that?

02:43:00.920 --> 02:43:03.260
Is it about avoiding
giving birth

02:43:03.260 --> 02:43:08.383
to a child that has something
like a herpes infection or HIV?

02:43:08.383 --> 02:43:09.800
Well, certainly
that's one reason,

02:43:09.800 --> 02:43:11.450
but that's a down-the-line
reason, because

02:43:11.450 --> 02:43:13.658
at the time when someone
goes into the clinic for one

02:43:13.658 --> 02:43:16.910
of these sperm or egg analyses,
that's well in advance

02:43:16.910 --> 02:43:18.170
of any pregnancy, right?

02:43:18.170 --> 02:43:20.900
The reason is there
are a number of STIs--

02:43:20.900 --> 02:43:24.350
in particular chlamydia-- for
which it greatly increases

02:43:24.350 --> 02:43:25.790
the probability of miscarriage.

02:43:25.790 --> 02:43:30.390
So chlamydia is one of those
very insidious and cryptic STIs

02:43:30.390 --> 02:43:32.390
because a lot of people,
both males and females,

02:43:32.390 --> 02:43:34.490
don't even realize that
they have chlamydia,

02:43:34.490 --> 02:43:36.932
and then they can
carry chlamydia

02:43:36.932 --> 02:43:38.390
at the time in
which they conceive,

02:43:38.390 --> 02:43:40.265
and then that can lead
to ectopic pregnancies

02:43:40.265 --> 02:43:41.480
and/or miscarriages.

02:43:41.480 --> 02:43:43.940
So by all means,
get an STI check

02:43:43.940 --> 02:43:46.520
if you are somebody who's
seeking to conceive children

02:43:46.520 --> 02:43:49.430
or evaluating your
fertility generally.

02:43:49.430 --> 02:43:51.980
Chlamydia can also have damaging
effects on the epididymis

02:43:51.980 --> 02:43:55.040
and on the various other aspects
of male reproductive health.

02:43:55.040 --> 02:43:56.540
In the future, we
will do an episode

02:43:56.540 --> 02:43:57.700
all about sexual health.

02:43:57.700 --> 02:43:58.950
This is not the time for that.

02:43:58.950 --> 02:44:00.920
But get an STI
check if your goal

02:44:00.920 --> 02:44:02.660
is to conceive a healthy child.

02:44:02.660 --> 02:44:05.210
Now, the other thing that can
have a very negative impact

02:44:05.210 --> 02:44:10.220
on fertility and healthy
pregnancy is a viral infection.

02:44:10.220 --> 02:44:13.353
For instance, if a male has
had a severe viral illness--

02:44:13.353 --> 02:44:15.770
and this could be any number
of different viral illnesses,

02:44:15.770 --> 02:44:18.110
from flu to cold or any
number of different viruses.

02:44:18.110 --> 02:44:20.660
Pick your favorite virus--

02:44:20.660 --> 02:44:23.330
in the previous 70
to 90 days, that

02:44:23.330 --> 02:44:27.990
can greatly diminish the
number and/or quality of sperm.

02:44:27.990 --> 02:44:29.115
So that's really important.

02:44:29.115 --> 02:44:31.698
This is also important if you're
going to go in and do a sperm

02:44:31.698 --> 02:44:33.440
analysis and you had
a viral infection

02:44:33.440 --> 02:44:35.385
in the previous 70 to 90 days.

02:44:35.385 --> 02:44:37.010
Well, then you need
to be aware of that

02:44:37.010 --> 02:44:39.680
because it could greatly impact
the parameters of that sperm

02:44:39.680 --> 02:44:40.370
analysis.

02:44:40.370 --> 02:44:42.980
Likewise, for women, if you've
had a serious viral infection

02:44:42.980 --> 02:44:44.870
in the previous 30 days,
does that mean you should not

02:44:44.870 --> 02:44:45.578
try and conceive?

02:44:45.578 --> 02:44:49.280
Not necessarily, but you should
talk to your OB/GYN about that.

02:44:49.280 --> 02:44:52.550
There are data showing
that viral infection--

02:44:52.550 --> 02:44:55.340
in particular of influenza--
in the mother in the first

02:44:55.340 --> 02:44:59.480
trimester of pregnancy has some
correlation-- it's not 100%--

02:44:59.480 --> 02:45:02.540
but some correlation with
negative mental health outcomes

02:45:02.540 --> 02:45:04.975
of the offspring sometime
later, including schizophrenia.

02:45:04.975 --> 02:45:06.350
This is some of
the work that was

02:45:06.350 --> 02:45:09.140
done at Caltech a
number of years ago

02:45:09.140 --> 02:45:11.150
and other laboratories, as well.

02:45:11.150 --> 02:45:13.790
Those data are still
being built up over time.

02:45:13.790 --> 02:45:15.440
Again, it's not one-for-one.

02:45:15.440 --> 02:45:16.680
It's not causal.

02:45:16.680 --> 02:45:19.715
So if you did get an influenza
or a cold or other kind

02:45:19.715 --> 02:45:21.590
of viral infection during
the first trimester

02:45:21.590 --> 02:45:24.500
or any trimester of pregnancy,
I don't want to cause alarm,

02:45:24.500 --> 02:45:26.960
but you should talk to
your OB/GYN about this.

02:45:26.960 --> 02:45:29.450
The goal, of course, is to
avoid viral illness at any time

02:45:29.450 --> 02:45:32.660
when you're trying to conceive
or have a healthy pregnancy.

02:45:32.660 --> 02:45:34.760
But of course, sometimes
people will get ill,

02:45:34.760 --> 02:45:38.078
and the children can turn out
to be perfectly normal and fine.

02:45:38.078 --> 02:45:39.870
But it is something
that you want to avoid.

02:45:39.870 --> 02:45:42.290
And it will impact
your egg analysis,

02:45:42.290 --> 02:45:44.385
and it will impact
sperm analysis.

02:45:44.385 --> 02:45:46.010
And one thing I found
really surprising

02:45:46.010 --> 02:45:51.350
in researching this episode
was that 1 in 25 men

02:45:51.350 --> 02:45:55.680
carry a copy of a mutation
for cystic fibrosis.

02:45:55.680 --> 02:45:58.370
Now, some of you are probably
familiar with cystic fibrosis

02:45:58.370 --> 02:46:00.952
as a condition that
can cause issues

02:46:00.952 --> 02:46:02.660
with the lungs, the
accumulation of fluid

02:46:02.660 --> 02:46:04.610
in the lungs or other tissues.

02:46:04.610 --> 02:46:07.070
Cystic fibrosis,
in order to express

02:46:07.070 --> 02:46:09.110
that way of accumulation
of fluid in the lungs,

02:46:09.110 --> 02:46:10.670
you really need two copies.

02:46:10.670 --> 02:46:13.880
You need two mutant copies
or you need two copies

02:46:13.880 --> 02:46:16.520
of the cystic fibrosis gene.

02:46:16.520 --> 02:46:19.280
1 in 25 men will
carry just one copy

02:46:19.280 --> 02:46:22.820
and therefore will not have any
symptoms of cystic fibrosis.

02:46:22.820 --> 02:46:27.080
But those 1 in 25
men will have defects

02:46:27.080 --> 02:46:30.620
in the architecture of
the vas deferens, the duct

02:46:30.620 --> 02:46:32.600
through which the
ejaculate needs

02:46:32.600 --> 02:46:36.500
to pass in order to
eventually be ejaculated out

02:46:36.500 --> 02:46:37.530
of the urethra.

02:46:37.530 --> 02:46:40.220
And so what that means
is that these men can

02:46:40.220 --> 02:46:42.260
have what appears to
be normal semen volume

02:46:42.260 --> 02:46:45.620
but that they won't have
normal numbers of sperm.

02:46:45.620 --> 02:46:48.553
And that's not because of a
deficit in making the sperm.

02:46:48.553 --> 02:46:49.970
The testes can
function just fine.

02:46:49.970 --> 02:46:52.370
The brain and the
pituitary are communicating

02:46:52.370 --> 02:46:53.640
with the testes just fine.

02:46:53.640 --> 02:46:55.280
But that literally
the passageway

02:46:55.280 --> 02:46:57.800
by which those sperm arrive
within the seminal fluid

02:46:57.800 --> 02:47:00.260
and are eventually
ejaculated is disrupted

02:47:00.260 --> 02:47:01.700
by the cystic fibrosis gene.

02:47:01.700 --> 02:47:05.030
Luckily, if somebody has just
one copy of the cystic fibrosis

02:47:05.030 --> 02:47:08.000
gene and they're male
and this is the issue,

02:47:08.000 --> 02:47:13.550
the vas deferens either can be
repaired by a urologist who's

02:47:13.550 --> 02:47:15.770
expert in the surgical
repair of vas deferens

02:47:15.770 --> 02:47:18.908
or sperm can be extracted from
the testicle directly, which

02:47:18.908 --> 02:47:20.450
might sound like a
painful procedure,

02:47:20.450 --> 02:47:22.640
but I believe
nowadays, in talking

02:47:22.640 --> 02:47:24.500
with various experts
on this, it turns out

02:47:24.500 --> 02:47:26.930
that it can be done with
a minimum of discomfort.

02:47:26.930 --> 02:47:29.240
And certainly, if the goal
is to have a healthy child,

02:47:29.240 --> 02:47:30.440
you're going to
need those sperm,

02:47:30.440 --> 02:47:32.815
so you're going to want to
get them one way or the other,

02:47:32.815 --> 02:47:34.048
regardless of the discomfort.

02:47:34.048 --> 02:47:35.840
Now, before getting
into some of the things

02:47:35.840 --> 02:47:37.550
that you can do in
the positive sense

02:47:37.550 --> 02:47:39.093
to increase your
fertility, we do

02:47:39.093 --> 02:47:40.760
need to touch on just
a few other things

02:47:40.760 --> 02:47:43.040
that you want to avoid
in order to avoid

02:47:43.040 --> 02:47:44.540
diminishing your fertility.

02:47:44.540 --> 02:47:46.040
And this mainly
relates to males,

02:47:46.040 --> 02:47:48.625
but it will also be
relevant to females.

02:47:48.625 --> 02:47:50.750
And of course, when I say
also relevant to females,

02:47:50.750 --> 02:47:53.840
I'm referring to the fact that,
if it's a woman and a man who

02:47:53.840 --> 02:47:56.585
are trying to conceive,
then she, of course,

02:47:56.585 --> 02:47:59.210
is going to be interested in her
egg quality but also the sperm

02:47:59.210 --> 02:47:59.780
quality.

02:47:59.780 --> 02:48:01.197
And of course,
there are women who

02:48:01.197 --> 02:48:04.790
are conceiving by way of sperm
donor, through IVF or IUI

02:48:04.790 --> 02:48:05.570
or otherwise.

02:48:05.570 --> 02:48:10.760
But in any case, the need
to understand and maximize

02:48:10.760 --> 02:48:13.440
the quality of both the egg
and the sperm is paramount.

02:48:13.440 --> 02:48:16.580
So in order for men to maximize
the quality of their sperm,

02:48:16.580 --> 02:48:18.500
as I mentioned
earlier, does not seem

02:48:18.500 --> 02:48:20.810
to be a big difference
whether or not they use boxers

02:48:20.810 --> 02:48:23.150
or briefs or whether or not
they, quote, unquote, "go

02:48:23.150 --> 02:48:27.090
commando," they don't wear any
boxers or briefs of any kind.

02:48:27.090 --> 02:48:30.620
However, it is important to
keep the testicles cool enough.

02:48:30.620 --> 02:48:32.420
They need to be about
2 degrees cooler

02:48:32.420 --> 02:48:33.930
than the rest of the body.

02:48:33.930 --> 02:48:36.360
And there are a number of
different ways to do that.

02:48:36.360 --> 02:48:38.695
As I mentioned before,
avoid going in hot tubs

02:48:38.695 --> 02:48:40.070
during the period
in which you're

02:48:40.070 --> 02:48:42.650
trying to conceive children.

02:48:42.650 --> 02:48:44.413
You should also
avoid going in saunas

02:48:44.413 --> 02:48:45.830
during the period
in which you are

02:48:45.830 --> 02:48:46.997
trying to conceive children.

02:48:46.997 --> 02:48:49.670
And if you do go in the sauna,
you can bring an ice pack there

02:48:49.670 --> 02:48:51.890
and you can put it
on the testicles

02:48:51.890 --> 02:48:55.100
in order to offset
the heat of the sauna

02:48:55.100 --> 02:48:58.608
and keep the testicles
cool while in the sauna.

02:48:58.608 --> 02:49:00.650
The other thing that you'll
definitely want to do

02:49:00.650 --> 02:49:03.620
is avoid putting a laptop
or any other hot device

02:49:03.620 --> 02:49:04.910
directly onto your lap.

02:49:04.910 --> 02:49:08.362
There are a number
of different devices

02:49:08.362 --> 02:49:09.570
that you can put on your lap.

02:49:09.570 --> 02:49:11.130
You could put books
or a box or there

02:49:11.130 --> 02:49:13.230
are these devices that
are designed to dispel

02:49:13.230 --> 02:49:14.480
the heat from the laptop.

02:49:14.480 --> 02:49:16.230
I would say, if you're
trying to conceive,

02:49:16.230 --> 02:49:17.933
just keep the laptop
off of your lap.

02:49:17.933 --> 02:49:20.100
Just put it on a table or
standing desk or whatever.

02:49:20.100 --> 02:49:22.200
Just keep it off of your lap.

02:49:22.200 --> 02:49:24.300
Also, there are some
really interesting data

02:49:24.300 --> 02:49:27.288
showing that the amount of
time that men spend sitting,

02:49:27.288 --> 02:49:28.830
regardless of whether
or not they sit

02:49:28.830 --> 02:49:33.030
with their ankle on their
opposite knee or with knees

02:49:33.030 --> 02:49:37.410
spread, the classic man spread
stance, or any other kind

02:49:37.410 --> 02:49:39.810
of seated stance is
going to increase

02:49:39.810 --> 02:49:42.815
the temperature of the
scrotum for reasons that

02:49:42.815 --> 02:49:44.190
are somewhat
obvious if you think

02:49:44.190 --> 02:49:45.520
about the architecture
of all this.

02:49:45.520 --> 02:49:47.250
I think both men and women, if
you put enough thought to it,

02:49:47.250 --> 02:49:49.458
you go, oh yeah, that would
increase the temperature.

02:49:49.458 --> 02:49:53.190
Obviously avoid seat heaters
in cars or otherwise.

02:49:53.190 --> 02:49:57.300
But reducing the total amount
of time that you spend seated

02:49:57.300 --> 02:50:00.300
is really important if you
want to keep the temperature

02:50:00.300 --> 02:50:03.330
milieu of the scrotum
optimal for sperm quality

02:50:03.330 --> 02:50:04.297
and fertilization.

02:50:04.297 --> 02:50:05.880
And as I mentioned
earlier, it's going

02:50:05.880 --> 02:50:08.610
to be important to make
sure that your legs are not

02:50:08.610 --> 02:50:11.730
really big to the point
where they are creating

02:50:11.730 --> 02:50:15.360
a hotter than is healthy
environment for the scrotum

02:50:15.360 --> 02:50:16.080
and testicles.

02:50:16.080 --> 02:50:19.530
So a hotter than normal
environment for the testicles

02:50:19.530 --> 02:50:21.960
can be caused by legs
that are very large,

02:50:21.960 --> 02:50:25.710
upper thighs that are very
large due to obesity or due

02:50:25.710 --> 02:50:27.840
to those upper thighs
being too muscular.

02:50:27.840 --> 02:50:29.370
So by all means,
don't skip leg day.

02:50:29.370 --> 02:50:30.780
But be aware that if
you're somebody who's

02:50:30.780 --> 02:50:32.572
trying to conceive,
you want to do whatever

02:50:32.572 --> 02:50:36.060
you can to reduce the
temperature of the scrotum

02:50:36.060 --> 02:50:40.090
or at least not let it
get too hot for too long.

02:50:40.090 --> 02:50:43.297
So I can think of
all sorts of reasons

02:50:43.297 --> 02:50:44.880
now that men are
going to come up with

02:50:44.880 --> 02:50:47.970
to do the man spread
stance of their knees

02:50:47.970 --> 02:50:50.460
really far apart, even further
if they have large legs.

02:50:50.460 --> 02:50:52.110
That's not a discussion
we want to have here,

02:50:52.110 --> 02:50:53.940
and that's not really what
today's discussion is about.

02:50:53.940 --> 02:50:56.107
Really the principle is
what's most important, which

02:50:56.107 --> 02:50:57.990
is to keep the
temperature of the scrotum

02:50:57.990 --> 02:51:01.330
and testicles lower than
the rest of your body.

02:51:01.330 --> 02:51:04.380
There's a direct blood flow from
the body to the testicle that

02:51:04.380 --> 02:51:05.280
provides blood flow.

02:51:05.280 --> 02:51:09.780
It's designed in a way
that that blood pathway

02:51:09.780 --> 02:51:12.420
should be outside the
body and as far away

02:51:12.420 --> 02:51:14.310
from the body as
possible in order

02:51:14.310 --> 02:51:16.200
to get the temperature
milieu of the scrotum

02:51:16.200 --> 02:51:18.930
and testicle correct for
healthy sperm quality.

02:51:18.930 --> 02:51:21.417
Now, a topic that is sure
to be a bit controversial--

02:51:21.417 --> 02:51:23.250
but it really shouldn't
be because the data,

02:51:23.250 --> 02:51:25.800
at least to me, are very clear--

02:51:25.800 --> 02:51:29.910
is this issue of phone
use and sperm quality.

02:51:29.910 --> 02:51:34.170
Now, this can open up a
whole array of issues related

02:51:34.170 --> 02:51:36.210
to things like EMFs,
and you've got people

02:51:36.210 --> 02:51:40.140
out there who have ideas about
5G and all of this stuff.

02:51:40.140 --> 02:51:42.060
That is not what this
discussion is about.

02:51:42.060 --> 02:51:45.150
The discussion I'm about to have
with you relates to the fact

02:51:45.150 --> 02:51:49.320
that the electromagnetic fields
and the heat-related effects

02:51:49.320 --> 02:51:53.250
of smartphones can indeed
have a detrimental effect

02:51:53.250 --> 02:51:56.730
on sperm quality and, yes,
indeed, on testosterone levels

02:51:56.730 --> 02:51:57.540
as well.

02:51:57.540 --> 02:51:59.090
I'm going to refer
you to a paper.

02:51:59.090 --> 02:52:00.840
We will link it in the
show note captions.

02:52:00.840 --> 02:52:03.450
The title of this paper is
"Effects of Mobile Phone

02:52:03.450 --> 02:52:04.950
Usage on Sperm Quality.

02:52:04.950 --> 02:52:07.710
No time-dependent
relationship on usage.

02:52:07.710 --> 02:52:10.240
A systematic review and
updated meta-analysis."

02:52:10.240 --> 02:52:13.200
This is the paper
that came out in 2021

02:52:13.200 --> 02:52:16.020
and talks about the fact
that phones emit a radio

02:52:16.020 --> 02:52:18.180
frequency electromagnetic
waves, which

02:52:18.180 --> 02:52:22.500
are called RF, radio frequency,
EMWs, electromagnetic waves,

02:52:22.500 --> 02:52:26.850
at a low level between 80
and 2,200 megahertz that

02:52:26.850 --> 02:52:29.310
can be absorbed by the
human body-- we know this.

02:52:29.310 --> 02:52:31.980
This is not controversial-- and
have potential adverse effects

02:52:31.980 --> 02:52:33.270
on brain, heart,
endocrine system,

02:52:33.270 --> 02:52:34.353
and reproductive function.

02:52:34.353 --> 02:52:36.120
That has been established.

02:52:36.120 --> 02:52:39.120
Keep in mind, there is
basically no controversy

02:52:39.120 --> 02:52:41.550
that radio frequency
waves and EMFs

02:52:41.550 --> 02:52:43.810
can have a negative impact
on biological tissues.

02:52:43.810 --> 02:52:47.910
The question is, how intense
are those radiofrequency waves

02:52:47.910 --> 02:52:51.225
and EMFs, and how
detrimental are those

02:52:51.225 --> 02:52:53.220
on those biological tissues?

02:52:53.220 --> 02:52:54.730
It's a matter of degrees.

02:52:54.730 --> 02:52:56.550
But there is very
little controversy as to

02:52:56.550 --> 02:52:58.925
whether or not they have an
effect on biological tissues.

02:52:58.925 --> 02:53:01.290
And I'm aware of absolutely
zero data showing

02:53:01.290 --> 02:53:03.780
that they can have a positive
effect on biological tissues.

02:53:03.780 --> 02:53:06.510
Since what we're mainly talking
about now are smartphones,

02:53:06.510 --> 02:53:08.910
we want to separate out the
heat effects of smartphones

02:53:08.910 --> 02:53:10.740
from the EMFs
related to the fact

02:53:10.740 --> 02:53:13.230
that they are Wi-Fi
smartphones or they're

02:53:13.230 --> 02:53:16.740
using cellular
towers and Wi-Fi, one

02:53:16.740 --> 02:53:18.310
or the other or a combination.

02:53:18.310 --> 02:53:20.190
So there are a number of
different things in the phone

02:53:20.190 --> 02:53:21.210
that could be detrimental.

02:53:21.210 --> 02:53:22.140
We need to separate those out.

02:53:22.140 --> 02:53:22.740
Why?

02:53:22.740 --> 02:53:24.330
Well, because you
might have heard

02:53:24.330 --> 02:53:25.955
that carrying your
phone in your pocket

02:53:25.955 --> 02:53:28.590
can reduce your testosterone
levels and sperm count.

02:53:28.590 --> 02:53:30.960
And guess what, that is true.

02:53:30.960 --> 02:53:33.240
The data contained
within this meta-analyses

02:53:33.240 --> 02:53:35.670
and other meta-analyses
clearly point out

02:53:35.670 --> 02:53:39.420
that it can reduce sperm count
and maybe testosterone levels

02:53:39.420 --> 02:53:42.330
significantly, but certainly
sperm count and motility

02:53:42.330 --> 02:53:43.110
significantly.

02:53:43.110 --> 02:53:44.850
It reduces sperm quality.

02:53:44.850 --> 02:53:48.970
So should you avoid putting your
phone in your pocket, certainly

02:53:48.970 --> 02:53:49.720
your front pocket?

02:53:49.720 --> 02:53:52.020
I would suggest yes,
if you are somebody

02:53:52.020 --> 02:53:53.820
who is seeking to conceive.

02:53:53.820 --> 02:53:56.237
I'm not somebody who is going
to stop using my smartphone.

02:53:56.237 --> 02:53:58.778
I don't expect anyone's going
to stop using their smartphone.

02:53:58.778 --> 02:54:01.410
The question is, should you
carry it in your front pocket

02:54:01.410 --> 02:54:02.490
if you're a male?

02:54:02.490 --> 02:54:04.590
I think, to be on the
safe side, the answer

02:54:04.590 --> 02:54:07.010
is probably avoid doing
that too much of the time.

02:54:07.010 --> 02:54:08.810
Ideally, don't do it at all.

02:54:08.810 --> 02:54:12.980
Then people will say, well,
what if I turn off the Wi-Fi

02:54:12.980 --> 02:54:15.500
or I turn off the
cellular access?

02:54:15.500 --> 02:54:17.070
Then is it still a problem?

02:54:17.070 --> 02:54:19.910
Well, it's a problem due to
the heat-related effects.

02:54:19.910 --> 02:54:21.770
And then people say,
well, I don't actually

02:54:21.770 --> 02:54:22.895
feel the heat of the phone.

02:54:22.895 --> 02:54:24.050
It doesn't get that warm.

02:54:24.050 --> 02:54:28.700
But the temperature effects
of the phone, it turns out,

02:54:28.700 --> 02:54:31.490
are enough, even under
conditions in which people

02:54:31.490 --> 02:54:34.400
don't report it to be
uncomfortably warm, that it can

02:54:34.400 --> 02:54:36.483
change the temperature
milieu of the testicle

02:54:36.483 --> 02:54:38.150
in ways that can
diminish sperm quality.

02:54:38.150 --> 02:54:40.820
How much and how that
relates to fertility

02:54:40.820 --> 02:54:43.490
and healthy pregnancy,
not clear, but since we're

02:54:43.490 --> 02:54:45.590
talking about things
to avoid, if your goal

02:54:45.590 --> 02:54:49.145
is to have a healthy
fertilization and pregnancy,

02:54:49.145 --> 02:54:51.020
well, then, by all means,
just don't carry it

02:54:51.020 --> 02:54:51.830
in your front pocket.

02:54:51.830 --> 02:54:53.270
Then people say, well,
what about back pocket

02:54:53.270 --> 02:54:54.320
or what about backpack?

02:54:54.320 --> 02:54:57.170
Look, it's very
clear that avoiding

02:54:57.170 --> 02:55:00.380
being too close to the phone is
probably better for your sperm

02:55:00.380 --> 02:55:04.190
quality than putting the phone
very close to your testicles

02:55:04.190 --> 02:55:05.930
or anywhere else on your body.

02:55:05.930 --> 02:55:08.240
But it's also the reality
that most people are going

02:55:08.240 --> 02:55:10.280
to carry a phone nowadays.

02:55:10.280 --> 02:55:11.340
It's just the reality.

02:55:11.340 --> 02:55:14.840
I think the current estimates--
and it's discussed in this

02:55:14.840 --> 02:55:19.040
paper-- that 90% of the human
population has a smartphone--

02:55:19.040 --> 02:55:22.430
90%, which is incredible-- the
adult population, of course.

02:55:22.430 --> 02:55:24.180
Although a lot of kids
have them, as well.

02:55:24.180 --> 02:55:26.780
So this paper goes on to detail
a number of different studies

02:55:26.780 --> 02:55:27.890
and outcomes from studies.

02:55:27.890 --> 02:55:30.307
But basically what they find--
and here I'm paraphrasing--

02:55:30.307 --> 02:55:33.855
is that the data indicate
that sperm quality declines

02:55:33.855 --> 02:55:35.480
when people start
using a mobile phone.

02:55:35.480 --> 02:55:37.250
So from the point they
start using a mobile phone,

02:55:37.250 --> 02:55:39.450
regardless of the usage
time-- this is important.

02:55:39.450 --> 02:55:42.200
It used to be thought that it
was four hours a day or more

02:55:42.200 --> 02:55:45.630
of holding your phone or having
that phone close to your body

02:55:45.630 --> 02:55:47.130
was going to diminish
sperm quality.

02:55:47.130 --> 02:55:49.010
It turns out that it's
not related to usage time.

02:55:49.010 --> 02:55:50.480
That's even the
title of the paper.

02:55:50.480 --> 02:55:51.897
It's just the fact
that people are

02:55:51.897 --> 02:55:55.700
using mobile phones is reducing
sperm count and quality.

02:55:55.700 --> 02:55:56.660
That's the reality.

02:55:56.660 --> 02:55:59.918
Is it entirely responsible for
all the reductions in sperm

02:55:59.918 --> 02:56:01.460
quality and maybe
even the reductions

02:56:01.460 --> 02:56:03.752
in testosterone levels that
we're observing from decade

02:56:03.752 --> 02:56:05.390
to decade going forward?

02:56:05.390 --> 02:56:06.680
I doubt that's the case.

02:56:06.680 --> 02:56:09.140
Is it likely to be one
of the major players?

02:56:09.140 --> 02:56:13.100
I've got my bet on the fact
that it is based on the data

02:56:13.100 --> 02:56:13.970
that I've observed.

02:56:13.970 --> 02:56:15.830
And so if any of you
would like to peruse

02:56:15.830 --> 02:56:18.020
the data in this meta-analysis,
they're quite good.

02:56:18.020 --> 02:56:22.340
This study looked at 18 studies
that include 4,280 samples.

02:56:22.340 --> 02:56:24.620
They were able to
separate out the radio

02:56:24.620 --> 02:56:26.390
frequency versus
the heat effects,

02:56:26.390 --> 02:56:30.680
and they were able to eliminate
this time of usage variable,

02:56:30.680 --> 02:56:32.630
that previously we thought
if you were exposed

02:56:32.630 --> 02:56:35.163
to a lot of cell
phone contact, then

02:56:35.163 --> 02:56:37.580
it was far worse than if you
were exposed to a little bit.

02:56:37.580 --> 02:56:39.230
Turns out, if you're
exposed to any at all,

02:56:39.230 --> 02:56:40.770
you're going to
diminish sperm quality.

02:56:40.770 --> 02:56:41.510
What does that mean?

02:56:41.510 --> 02:56:42.710
Does that mean
that no matter what

02:56:42.710 --> 02:56:44.793
you do, if you own a
smartphone, that you're going

02:56:44.793 --> 02:56:46.010
to diminish sperm quality?

02:56:46.010 --> 02:56:49.430
I think the short answer is yes,
but that you can mitigate it.

02:56:49.430 --> 02:56:50.480
What might you do?

02:56:50.480 --> 02:56:52.898
Well, keeping your phone away
from your groin or as far

02:56:52.898 --> 02:56:54.440
from your groin as
possible if you're

02:56:54.440 --> 02:56:56.690
a male who's wishing to
conceive and maybe even a male

02:56:56.690 --> 02:56:59.990
who's wishing to maximize his
testosterone levels because it

02:56:59.990 --> 02:57:02.390
does appear that radiofrequency
waves and the heat

02:57:02.390 --> 02:57:03.200
from the phone--

02:57:03.200 --> 02:57:06.110
so both of those factors,
independently and together,

02:57:06.110 --> 02:57:06.800
of course--

02:57:06.800 --> 02:57:08.990
can disrupt the Leydig
cells of the testes

02:57:08.990 --> 02:57:10.580
and the production
of testosterone,

02:57:10.580 --> 02:57:12.890
and intratesticular
testosterone is

02:57:12.890 --> 02:57:14.420
important for sperm production.

02:57:14.420 --> 02:57:17.360
The exact biological variables
leading to all of these changes

02:57:17.360 --> 02:57:18.780
isn't exactly clear.

02:57:18.780 --> 02:57:20.360
But if you're like
me, you say, OK,

02:57:20.360 --> 02:57:23.720
probably not a problem for most
males to carry their phone.

02:57:23.720 --> 02:57:26.660
But probably best to not
carry it in the front pocket.

02:57:26.660 --> 02:57:29.010
Maybe even avoid carrying it
in the back pocket as well.

02:57:29.010 --> 02:57:30.885
Again, in the future,
we will have an episode

02:57:30.885 --> 02:57:31.850
all about Bluetooth.

02:57:31.850 --> 02:57:34.760
We'll talk about
various aspects of EMFs.

02:57:34.760 --> 02:57:37.010
It's a super
interesting data set.

02:57:37.010 --> 02:57:40.160
And it's a data set for which
there's a ton of controversy.

02:57:40.160 --> 02:57:41.995
It's really
interesting, however,

02:57:41.995 --> 02:57:44.120
and there are more and more
quality data coming out

02:57:44.120 --> 02:57:44.713
all the time.

02:57:44.713 --> 02:57:46.130
And I think, going
forward, we are

02:57:46.130 --> 02:57:48.547
going to see that, indeed,
there are some negative effects

02:57:48.547 --> 02:57:51.350
of smartphones related to
both the radio frequency

02:57:51.350 --> 02:57:55.670
transmission and the fact
that they generate heat.

02:57:55.670 --> 02:57:58.770
And in general, heat is not
good for biological tissues.

02:57:58.770 --> 02:58:00.710
So any discussion
about heat and sperm

02:58:00.710 --> 02:58:03.680
and how heat is
detrimental to sperm

02:58:03.680 --> 02:58:05.540
has to raise this
issue of whether or not

02:58:05.540 --> 02:58:07.400
cold is good for the testicle.

02:58:07.400 --> 02:58:09.830
OK, well, now there's
a lot of data starting

02:58:09.830 --> 02:58:12.410
to come out about
the positive effects,

02:58:12.410 --> 02:58:16.790
the positive biological effects,
of deliberate cold exposure

02:58:16.790 --> 02:58:19.790
on different aspects
of brain biology,

02:58:19.790 --> 02:58:22.070
such as the release of
dopamine and norepinephrine,

02:58:22.070 --> 02:58:25.400
and on the biology of the
body, to some extent metabolism

02:58:25.400 --> 02:58:27.950
but more so the impact on
brown fat stores, which

02:58:27.950 --> 02:58:30.560
are good for us, so-called
brown fat thermogenesis.

02:58:30.560 --> 02:58:33.300
There's a lot related to
deliberate cold exposure,

02:58:33.300 --> 02:58:36.050
and we've done entire episodes
on deliberate cold exposure.

02:58:36.050 --> 02:58:37.910
Again, you can find
that at hubermanlab.com.

02:58:37.910 --> 02:58:39.950
We did a guest
episode with an expert

02:58:39.950 --> 02:58:42.518
on the use of cold for
health and performance

02:58:42.518 --> 02:58:44.810
with my colleague Craig Heller
from Stanford Department

02:58:44.810 --> 02:58:45.380
of Biology.

02:58:45.380 --> 02:58:49.640
We also have a toolkit on how to
apply deliberate, cold exposure

02:58:49.640 --> 02:58:52.310
for health for both
females and for males--

02:58:52.310 --> 02:58:54.690
for sports performance,
cognitive performance, mood,

02:58:54.690 --> 02:58:55.430
sleep, et cetera.

02:58:55.430 --> 02:58:57.472
You can find all that,
again, at hubermanlab.com.

02:58:57.472 --> 02:58:59.055
Totally zero cost.

02:58:59.055 --> 02:59:01.430
Just go into the menu, go to
newsletter, and scroll down,

02:59:01.430 --> 02:59:04.070
and you'll find those.

02:59:04.070 --> 02:59:06.290
When thinking about
sperm quality,

02:59:06.290 --> 02:59:08.860
we want remember that
excessive heat is bad.

02:59:08.860 --> 02:59:11.770
Now, does that mean that
deliberate cold is good?

02:59:11.770 --> 02:59:15.760
Well, it turns out that one
of the major causes of lowered

02:59:15.760 --> 02:59:20.320
sperm count and overall
reduced sperm quality that's

02:59:20.320 --> 02:59:22.870
quite common is the presence
of what's called a varicocele.

02:59:22.870 --> 02:59:26.800
A varicocele is kind of like
varicose veins of the veins

02:59:26.800 --> 02:59:28.600
that innervate the testicle.

02:59:28.600 --> 02:59:31.780
And what it
essentially does is it

02:59:31.780 --> 02:59:36.190
means that blood will pool
in the testicular region.

02:59:36.190 --> 02:59:38.560
It can't circulate back to
the body quickly enough.

02:59:38.560 --> 02:59:40.750
And therefore, the temperature
of that environment increases.

02:59:40.750 --> 02:59:42.583
There are some other
things that varicoceles

02:59:42.583 --> 02:59:44.710
do which can be obstructive
at the physical level.

02:59:44.710 --> 02:59:46.690
So they're not just
temperature related.

02:59:46.690 --> 02:59:50.470
It's pretty clear that using
deliberate cold exposure

02:59:50.470 --> 02:59:53.110
can be healthy for the
sperm because of the ways

02:59:53.110 --> 02:59:58.120
not that cold directly supports
testosterone or sperm quality

02:59:58.120 --> 03:00:01.120
but rather because
cold reduces heat.

03:00:01.120 --> 03:00:05.505
So you will find
available online--

03:00:05.505 --> 03:00:06.880
I think they're
actually called--

03:00:06.880 --> 03:00:08.260
forgive me, but that's
what they're called.

03:00:08.260 --> 03:00:09.843
I didn't name them--
called snowballs.

03:00:09.843 --> 03:00:14.530
These are-- they're sort of
like gel pack cold briefs

03:00:14.530 --> 03:00:17.380
that you can buy and men will
wear for some period of time.

03:00:17.380 --> 03:00:18.880
I don't think you
wear them all day.

03:00:18.880 --> 03:00:20.860
You wear them for
some period of time.

03:00:20.860 --> 03:00:24.040
A lot of people are now using
cold showers and ice baths

03:00:24.040 --> 03:00:26.380
and circulating cold baths
or going into a cold ocean

03:00:26.380 --> 03:00:28.482
or lake for any number
of different reasons

03:00:28.482 --> 03:00:29.440
I talked about earlier.

03:00:29.440 --> 03:00:32.320
I, myself, start every
day with either a one

03:00:32.320 --> 03:00:33.980
to three-minute
cold shower or a one

03:00:33.980 --> 03:00:36.520
to three-minute
immersion up to my neck

03:00:36.520 --> 03:00:40.840
in a cold bath, cold
water, circulating water,

03:00:40.840 --> 03:00:41.743
or a cold shower.

03:00:41.743 --> 03:00:43.660
I do that mainly for the
psychological effects

03:00:43.660 --> 03:00:45.400
related to the long
lasting increases

03:00:45.400 --> 03:00:46.935
in dopamine and epinephrine.

03:00:46.935 --> 03:00:48.310
But there are
other data starting

03:00:48.310 --> 03:00:51.370
to come out showing that
that sort of approach

03:00:51.370 --> 03:00:54.340
or similar approaches can
increase testosterone levels

03:00:54.340 --> 03:00:55.990
and maybe even sperm
counts, can reduce

03:00:55.990 --> 03:00:58.540
cortisol late in the evening if
the cold exposure is done early

03:00:58.540 --> 03:00:59.832
in the day, so on and so forth.

03:00:59.832 --> 03:01:02.170
So a lot of interesting data
coming out in really good

03:01:02.170 --> 03:01:06.783
journals that are peer-reviewed
and so on-- in humans,

03:01:06.783 --> 03:01:08.950
I should mention, those
studies are done in humans--

03:01:08.950 --> 03:01:10.990
to support the use of
deliberate cold exposure.

03:01:10.990 --> 03:01:13.407
But again, if you're going to
use deliberate cold exposure

03:01:13.407 --> 03:01:15.310
to improve sperm
quality, can it work?

03:01:15.310 --> 03:01:17.800
Yes, indeed, it can
work, either indirectly

03:01:17.800 --> 03:01:19.750
by increasing
testosterone or directly

03:01:19.750 --> 03:01:21.130
by improving sperm quality.

03:01:21.130 --> 03:01:23.830
But both of those effects
are likely to be indirect

03:01:23.830 --> 03:01:26.740
by virtue of reducing the
temperature of the testicle

03:01:26.740 --> 03:01:30.490
overall, not because there's
any sort of magic effect of cold

03:01:30.490 --> 03:01:31.420
on the testicle.

03:01:31.420 --> 03:01:33.253
Now, I have to imagine
that a number of you,

03:01:33.253 --> 03:01:35.410
in particular the females
listening to this,

03:01:35.410 --> 03:01:38.318
are going to say, is
deliberate cold exposure--

03:01:38.318 --> 03:01:40.360
and for that matter, is
deliberate heat exposure,

03:01:40.360 --> 03:01:43.630
like sauna or hot tub--
good or bad for the ovary,

03:01:43.630 --> 03:01:45.040
for eggs, and for fertility?

03:01:45.040 --> 03:01:49.300
Now, there are fewer data
to look to, unfortunately.

03:01:49.300 --> 03:01:52.450
But what we do know is that
deliberate cold exposure

03:01:52.450 --> 03:01:54.260
done in the way that
I just described-- one

03:01:54.260 --> 03:01:56.438
to three minutes a day,
ideally early in the day,

03:01:56.438 --> 03:01:58.480
through cold shower or
immersion up to the neck--

03:01:58.480 --> 03:01:59.772
doesn't have to be an ice bath.

03:01:59.772 --> 03:02:02.140
It could be cold
circulating water or even

03:02:02.140 --> 03:02:03.580
non-circulating cold water.

03:02:03.580 --> 03:02:05.140
And people will
say, well, how cold?

03:02:05.140 --> 03:02:06.640
I should have
mentioned that before.

03:02:06.640 --> 03:02:08.150
How cold?

03:02:08.150 --> 03:02:10.567
There is no way I can
tell you exactly how

03:02:10.567 --> 03:02:12.650
cold the water should be,
because for some people,

03:02:12.650 --> 03:02:14.998
60 degrees Fahrenheit
will be exceedingly cold.

03:02:14.998 --> 03:02:17.540
For other people, 40 degrees is
going to be more appropriate.

03:02:17.540 --> 03:02:18.800
How cold should you make it?

03:02:18.800 --> 03:02:21.810
If you're going to embrace
these practices, you want--

03:02:21.810 --> 03:02:23.810
according to the literature,
what you want to do

03:02:23.810 --> 03:02:26.030
is make it
uncomfortably cold such

03:02:26.030 --> 03:02:28.280
that you really want
to get out, but safe.

03:02:28.280 --> 03:02:31.190
You don't want to go into
30-degree water immediately.

03:02:31.190 --> 03:02:33.690
You can actually have a heart
attack and die if you do that.

03:02:33.690 --> 03:02:36.860
So you want to progress
gradually into the cold.

03:02:36.860 --> 03:02:39.020
So you don't want to shock
your system too much.

03:02:39.020 --> 03:02:41.840
Although it is the adrenaline
evoked by that [GASPS],,

03:02:41.840 --> 03:02:44.060
that quickening or
shortening or elimination

03:02:44.060 --> 03:02:45.727
of the breath for a
short period of time

03:02:45.727 --> 03:02:47.900
when you get into
uncomfortably cold water that

03:02:47.900 --> 03:02:50.570
correlates with or is
actually the reflection of--

03:02:50.570 --> 03:02:52.970
would be more accurate to
say-- the release of adrenaline

03:02:52.970 --> 03:02:54.830
and then dopamine
and so forth, which

03:02:54.830 --> 03:02:56.640
has been very well documented.

03:02:56.640 --> 03:03:00.270
So uncomfortably cold,
but safe to stay in.

03:03:00.270 --> 03:03:03.980
And I cannot tell you an exact
number that is uncomfortably

03:03:03.980 --> 03:03:05.100
cold but safe for you.

03:03:05.100 --> 03:03:06.410
It's going to differ
person by person.

03:03:06.410 --> 03:03:07.310
You want to figure that out.

03:03:07.310 --> 03:03:09.727
Just like I can't tell you how
much weight that you should

03:03:09.727 --> 03:03:12.175
squat in order to achieve
some effective resistance

03:03:12.175 --> 03:03:13.550
training for the
legs, it's going

03:03:13.550 --> 03:03:16.010
to differ depending
on your strength

03:03:16.010 --> 03:03:17.730
and your prior
experience and so forth.

03:03:17.730 --> 03:03:18.530
So ease into it.

03:03:18.530 --> 03:03:19.220
Be safe.

03:03:19.220 --> 03:03:21.380
But it does appear
that both for men,

03:03:21.380 --> 03:03:25.700
for reasons I talked about a
few minutes ago, and for women

03:03:25.700 --> 03:03:28.940
that deliberate, cold
exposure can be beneficial

03:03:28.940 --> 03:03:31.610
for fertility and for
hormone production,

03:03:31.610 --> 03:03:35.145
but in particular for females
in terms of regulating cortisol

03:03:35.145 --> 03:03:36.270
and for hormone production.

03:03:36.270 --> 03:03:38.300
Now, you might say, OK,
getting into cold is stressful.

03:03:38.300 --> 03:03:40.070
How can that be helpful
for regulating stress?

03:03:40.070 --> 03:03:42.028
Well, it turns out, when
you get into the cold,

03:03:42.028 --> 03:03:43.460
you get a big
surge in adrenaline

03:03:43.460 --> 03:03:45.440
and then dopamine, which
is very long lasting,

03:03:45.440 --> 03:03:47.700
provided that's done in
the early part of the day.

03:03:47.700 --> 03:03:50.090
So I would say, not
too close to sleep.

03:03:50.090 --> 03:03:53.300
Then what you do is you restrict
your maximum cortisol release

03:03:53.300 --> 03:03:57.320
to a period earlier in
the day that buffers--

03:03:57.320 --> 03:03:59.150
reduces, that is--
the likelihood

03:03:59.150 --> 03:04:01.907
that you would have excessive
amounts of cortisol later

03:04:01.907 --> 03:04:03.740
in the day, which not
only can disrupt sleep

03:04:03.740 --> 03:04:07.430
but is correlated with a number
of other hormonal effects that

03:04:07.430 --> 03:04:08.960
are not good for
us and therefore

03:04:08.960 --> 03:04:10.100
not good for fertility.

03:04:10.100 --> 03:04:11.990
So here what I'm
describing are positive

03:04:11.990 --> 03:04:16.490
yet indirect effects of
a cold on hormone levels

03:04:16.490 --> 03:04:19.080
both in males and in females.

03:04:19.080 --> 03:04:21.680
So for men, we talked about
increased testosterone,

03:04:21.680 --> 03:04:23.750
improved sperm quality
that was indirect.

03:04:23.750 --> 03:04:26.120
You're reducing the
temperature of the testicle.

03:04:26.120 --> 03:04:28.262
But it's not that cold
itself is positively

03:04:28.262 --> 03:04:29.220
impacting those things.

03:04:29.220 --> 03:04:29.690
Does that make sense?

03:04:29.690 --> 03:04:30.480
Heat is bad.

03:04:30.480 --> 03:04:32.330
Therefore, reducing
temperature is good.

03:04:32.330 --> 03:04:35.390
Likewise, with females,
deliberate cold exposure

03:04:35.390 --> 03:04:38.150
can be good for the
overall fertility process,

03:04:38.150 --> 03:04:41.240
not because cold is good
for the ovary or being

03:04:41.240 --> 03:04:44.820
cold is good for the ovary
or for luteinizing hormone

03:04:44.820 --> 03:04:46.790
or for follicle-stimulating
hormone or anything

03:04:46.790 --> 03:04:51.020
else like that, but rather that
using deliberate cold exposure

03:04:51.020 --> 03:04:53.360
as a way to restrict
stress in a deliberate

03:04:53.360 --> 03:04:56.330
way to a particular
time of day increases

03:04:56.330 --> 03:04:59.427
the release of cortisol,
then, and indirectly reduces

03:04:59.427 --> 03:05:01.010
the amount of cortisol
that's released

03:05:01.010 --> 03:05:04.050
at other times along
the 24-hour cycle.

03:05:04.050 --> 03:05:06.360
So these are positive
yet indirect effects.

03:05:06.360 --> 03:05:09.710
So if you're a woman who really
is interested in exploring

03:05:09.710 --> 03:05:12.500
deliberate cold exposure or
who enjoys it or is already

03:05:12.500 --> 03:05:15.110
doing it and you're
wishing to conceive, great.

03:05:15.110 --> 03:05:15.825
Explore it.

03:05:15.825 --> 03:05:17.450
Do it safely, of
course, but explore it

03:05:17.450 --> 03:05:18.360
and continue to do it.

03:05:18.360 --> 03:05:20.330
However, if you're somebody
who just hates the cold

03:05:20.330 --> 03:05:21.650
and doesn't want to
go anywhere near it,

03:05:21.650 --> 03:05:23.600
there's no reason to think
that you absolutely need it,

03:05:23.600 --> 03:05:25.970
provided that your stress,
your sleep, and other factors

03:05:25.970 --> 03:05:27.578
are all being
carried out properly.

03:05:27.578 --> 03:05:29.120
The next things that
we'll talk about

03:05:29.120 --> 03:05:30.980
in terms of positive
things or things

03:05:30.980 --> 03:05:33.410
that we can do in order
to maximize fertility

03:05:33.410 --> 03:05:35.390
for both females and
males are the things

03:05:35.390 --> 03:05:37.910
that you also generally
hear about elsewhere.

03:05:37.910 --> 03:05:41.090
Right along with sleep and
avoiding alcohol and avoiding

03:05:41.090 --> 03:05:44.060
nicotine and avoiding cannabis,
avoiding excessive heat

03:05:44.060 --> 03:05:46.880
for the testicle,
avoiding excessive stress,

03:05:46.880 --> 03:05:51.650
is that you want to try
to get enough exercise.

03:05:51.650 --> 03:05:54.570
Why would exercise have
anything to do with any of this?

03:05:54.570 --> 03:05:57.530
Well, exercise-- and that
is both a combination

03:05:57.530 --> 03:05:59.900
of resistance training and
cardiovascular exercise--

03:05:59.900 --> 03:06:02.390
is going to improve the
health of the mitochondria--

03:06:02.390 --> 03:06:04.352
in particular,
cardiovascular exercise.

03:06:04.352 --> 03:06:06.560
And I realize that for you
fitness experts out there,

03:06:06.560 --> 03:06:09.185
any time someone says "cardio,"
people kind of roll their eyes,

03:06:09.185 --> 03:06:10.250
like, what is that?

03:06:10.250 --> 03:06:11.600
There's endurance training.

03:06:11.600 --> 03:06:12.710
There's interval training.

03:06:12.710 --> 03:06:13.730
There's HIIT training.

03:06:13.730 --> 03:06:14.467
There's sprints.

03:06:14.467 --> 03:06:16.050
There's all sorts
of different things.

03:06:16.050 --> 03:06:16.790
Some of those overlap.

03:06:16.790 --> 03:06:18.020
Some of them are separate.

03:06:18.020 --> 03:06:19.250
Indeed, that's the case.

03:06:19.250 --> 03:06:22.280
But we can use a general
rule of thumb here, which

03:06:22.280 --> 03:06:25.220
is that, for most people,
getting anywhere from 30

03:06:25.220 --> 03:06:29.240
and ideally 45 to 60
minutes of exercise per day

03:06:29.240 --> 03:06:31.490
for six days per week,
maybe even seven--

03:06:31.490 --> 03:06:33.560
but most people like to
take a day off or need

03:06:33.560 --> 03:06:35.180
to take a complete
day off each week--

03:06:35.180 --> 03:06:36.860
six to seven days
per week is going

03:06:36.860 --> 03:06:39.342
to be good for mitochondrial
health and function.

03:06:39.342 --> 03:06:41.300
It's also going to impact
all the other things,

03:06:41.300 --> 03:06:43.550
like quality sleep,
mood, reducing stress,

03:06:43.550 --> 03:06:44.670
and so on and so forth.

03:06:44.670 --> 03:06:48.650
So exercise we can handle pretty
quickly by just saying everyone

03:06:48.650 --> 03:06:49.820
should be doing it.

03:06:49.820 --> 03:06:52.920
Now, when people are pregnant,
they might have to, of course,

03:06:52.920 --> 03:06:55.148
change the amount of exercise
or the type of exercise

03:06:55.148 --> 03:06:55.940
that they're doing.

03:06:55.940 --> 03:06:57.398
There are varying
opinions on that,

03:06:57.398 --> 03:07:00.350
but certainly the type of
exercise and the amount

03:07:00.350 --> 03:07:01.860
can vary when
people are pregnant.

03:07:01.860 --> 03:07:03.497
But if you're
seeking to conceive,

03:07:03.497 --> 03:07:05.330
getting enough exercise
is good because it's

03:07:05.330 --> 03:07:06.413
good for the mitochondria.

03:07:06.413 --> 03:07:10.340
The mitochondria are present in
that mid region of the sperm.

03:07:10.340 --> 03:07:14.480
And mitochondria are critical
for chromosomal segregation

03:07:14.480 --> 03:07:16.700
and the spindle
and other aspects

03:07:16.700 --> 03:07:18.890
of the formation of a
healthy egg, ovulation,

03:07:18.890 --> 03:07:20.228
and fertilization in the female.

03:07:20.228 --> 03:07:21.770
One thing that I
know a lot of people

03:07:21.770 --> 03:07:24.770
are interested in nowadays is
so-called intermittent fasting

03:07:24.770 --> 03:07:26.300
or time-restricted feeding.

03:07:26.300 --> 03:07:28.877
I mean, let's be fair, everybody
is restricting their feeding

03:07:28.877 --> 03:07:30.710
time because hopefully
everybody is sleeping

03:07:30.710 --> 03:07:32.510
at some point in
the 24-hour cycle,

03:07:32.510 --> 03:07:35.330
and nobody is eating
while they are sleeping.

03:07:35.330 --> 03:07:37.970
That said, many
people are employing

03:07:37.970 --> 03:07:40.562
a so-called eight-hour feeding
window or a 10-hour feeding

03:07:40.562 --> 03:07:42.020
window or a 12-hour
feeding window.

03:07:42.020 --> 03:07:45.005
And indeed, there are some data
to support the idea that that

03:07:45.005 --> 03:07:48.080
can be a good thing for a number
of different biological and

03:07:48.080 --> 03:07:48.900
health parameters.

03:07:48.900 --> 03:07:51.832
However, there are
also a lot of data,

03:07:51.832 --> 03:07:53.540
especially recently,
pointing to the fact

03:07:53.540 --> 03:07:55.970
that your overall
number of calories

03:07:55.970 --> 03:07:57.740
and the quality of
your food sources

03:07:57.740 --> 03:07:59.930
is going to be the most
important variable.

03:07:59.930 --> 03:08:02.690
And some people simply find
that time-restricted feeding--

03:08:02.690 --> 03:08:05.150
intermittent fasting,
as it's also called--

03:08:05.150 --> 03:08:07.070
is just a convenient
way to ensure

03:08:07.070 --> 03:08:09.230
that your total
intake of calories

03:08:09.230 --> 03:08:11.270
is not excessive
for what you need.

03:08:11.270 --> 03:08:14.210
Now, with all that
said, there is evidence

03:08:14.210 --> 03:08:15.703
that I've covered
in a solo episode

03:08:15.703 --> 03:08:17.120
and will soon have
an expert guest

03:08:17.120 --> 03:08:21.320
on showing that time-restricted
feeding can have

03:08:21.320 --> 03:08:25.040
certain positive outcomes
for various aspects of organ,

03:08:25.040 --> 03:08:27.230
cellular, and tissue health.

03:08:27.230 --> 03:08:29.030
This is somewhat
controversial, but there

03:08:29.030 --> 03:08:31.580
is growing evidence that,
by restricting your feeding

03:08:31.580 --> 03:08:34.550
window to, say, 8 hours
or 10 hours or 12 hours,

03:08:34.550 --> 03:08:37.100
that it is better than if
you were to eat over a longer

03:08:37.100 --> 03:08:39.560
period of each 24-hour cycle.

03:08:39.560 --> 03:08:41.625
But again, the data
are still incoming.

03:08:41.625 --> 03:08:44.000
The reason we want to talk
about time-restricted feeding,

03:08:44.000 --> 03:08:46.070
intermittent fasting
is that a lot of people

03:08:46.070 --> 03:08:48.290
do use it because
they find it easier

03:08:48.290 --> 03:08:51.470
to not eat at certain periods
of their 24-hour cycle

03:08:51.470 --> 03:08:52.790
than to restrict calories.

03:08:52.790 --> 03:08:56.132
But again, keep in mind, you
have to restrict calories

03:08:56.132 --> 03:08:57.590
if your goal is to
maintain or lose

03:08:57.590 --> 03:08:59.870
weight, a discussion
that we've covered

03:08:59.870 --> 03:09:01.790
in that episode on
intermittent fasting

03:09:01.790 --> 03:09:03.920
and in the episode
with Dr. Layne Norton

03:09:03.920 --> 03:09:08.160
and that we will cover in
other episodes in the future.

03:09:08.160 --> 03:09:10.790
So refer to those episodes
at hubermanlab.com

03:09:10.790 --> 03:09:13.310
if you would like to learn more
about intermittent fasting,

03:09:13.310 --> 03:09:14.060
per se.

03:09:14.060 --> 03:09:16.700
For sake of this conversation,
a number of people

03:09:16.700 --> 03:09:19.610
are probably asking, if
I restrict my feeding

03:09:19.610 --> 03:09:22.983
to a certain window each
24 hours because that's

03:09:22.983 --> 03:09:24.650
what's convenient or
because I'm excited

03:09:24.650 --> 03:09:26.180
about the potential
positive effects

03:09:26.180 --> 03:09:29.030
of intermittent
fasting, is that going

03:09:29.030 --> 03:09:33.500
to disrupt the likelihood
of fertility and thereby

03:09:33.500 --> 03:09:34.670
a healthy pregnancy?

03:09:34.670 --> 03:09:37.730
And the short answer to
that is, if you are a female

03:09:37.730 --> 03:09:39.950
and you are having regular
menstrual cycles that

03:09:39.950 --> 03:09:42.450
is a fairly
consistent duration--

03:09:42.450 --> 03:09:44.240
so maybe it's 21
days, maybe it's

03:09:44.240 --> 03:09:45.830
35, or anywhere in
between, but it's

03:09:45.830 --> 03:09:47.488
fairly consistent
from month to month--

03:09:47.488 --> 03:09:49.280
and you are following
intermittent fasting,

03:09:49.280 --> 03:09:51.140
time-restricted
feeding, well, then

03:09:51.140 --> 03:09:53.480
chances are pretty
good that it's not

03:09:53.480 --> 03:09:57.910
disrupting your fertility and
likelihood of fertilization

03:09:57.910 --> 03:09:58.910
and a healthy pregnancy.

03:09:58.910 --> 03:10:01.940
Of course, during pregnancy,
you need to talk to your doctor

03:10:01.940 --> 03:10:03.980
and make sure that you're
eating in a way that's

03:10:03.980 --> 03:10:06.410
supportive both of you and
of the developing fetus.

03:10:06.410 --> 03:10:07.860
That's extremely important.

03:10:07.860 --> 03:10:10.850
I am not aware of
data exploring,

03:10:10.850 --> 03:10:13.100
in a regimented way,
time-restricted feeding

03:10:13.100 --> 03:10:14.340
during pregnancy.

03:10:14.340 --> 03:10:16.520
So please, please, please,
if you're pregnant,

03:10:16.520 --> 03:10:18.380
do not jump on a
time-restricted feeding,

03:10:18.380 --> 03:10:19.880
so-called intermittent
fasting diet.

03:10:19.880 --> 03:10:22.070
Talk to your OB/GYN.

03:10:22.070 --> 03:10:23.720
Talk to your doctor.

03:10:23.720 --> 03:10:25.790
Talk to multiple
doctors, for that matter,

03:10:25.790 --> 03:10:28.010
before doing anything like
that, because, of course,

03:10:28.010 --> 03:10:30.410
you're now eating for two, or
if you have twins in there,

03:10:30.410 --> 03:10:32.150
you're eating for three.

03:10:32.150 --> 03:10:33.080
Very important.

03:10:33.080 --> 03:10:34.580
If, however, you're
not yet pregnant

03:10:34.580 --> 03:10:39.020
and you want to be fertile, get
pregnant, or simply maintain

03:10:39.020 --> 03:10:42.770
a fertile potential
and biology and you're

03:10:42.770 --> 03:10:44.780
following intermittent
fasting, it's

03:10:44.780 --> 03:10:47.748
going to be the regularity of
those periods and regularity

03:10:47.748 --> 03:10:49.790
of cycle length that will
tell you whether or not

03:10:49.790 --> 03:10:51.350
that's a good idea or not.

03:10:51.350 --> 03:10:54.680
Keeping in mind, of course,
that if your total number

03:10:54.680 --> 03:10:57.800
of calories is too low,
your periods will cease.

03:10:57.800 --> 03:10:59.670
That's a well-known effect.

03:10:59.670 --> 03:11:02.780
But of course, stress
can also induce

03:11:02.780 --> 03:11:05.420
cessation of menstruation.

03:11:05.420 --> 03:11:07.760
And there are other factors
that can induce cessation

03:11:07.760 --> 03:11:09.150
of menstruation as well.

03:11:09.150 --> 03:11:12.417
Some of them start with changes
in the brain, literally,

03:11:12.417 --> 03:11:13.250
in the hypothalamus.

03:11:13.250 --> 03:11:14.930
Some occur in the pituitary.

03:11:14.930 --> 03:11:17.390
Many lifestyle
factors can do that.

03:11:17.390 --> 03:11:19.190
But most typically,
it's going to be

03:11:19.190 --> 03:11:21.710
excessive caloric
restriction or it's

03:11:21.710 --> 03:11:24.320
going to be a caloric
deficit brought on

03:11:24.320 --> 03:11:26.520
by excess physical activity.

03:11:26.520 --> 03:11:28.280
So even if someone's
eating a lot,

03:11:28.280 --> 03:11:32.060
if they're not eating enough to
offset their physical activity

03:11:32.060 --> 03:11:34.220
or they're not eating
enough of, in particular,

03:11:34.220 --> 03:11:37.490
fats, the essential
fatty acids and protein,

03:11:37.490 --> 03:11:40.240
but also carbohydrates, well,
then menstruation can cease.

03:11:40.240 --> 03:11:41.990
And of course, if
menstruation is ceasing,

03:11:41.990 --> 03:11:44.150
chances are, almost
with certainty,

03:11:44.150 --> 03:11:46.320
that you're not getting
regular ovulations.

03:11:46.320 --> 03:11:48.243
Now, in terms of males
and whether or not

03:11:48.243 --> 03:11:49.910
intermittent fasting
is going to disrupt

03:11:49.910 --> 03:11:53.660
spermatogenesis and
testosterone production,

03:11:53.660 --> 03:11:56.490
there's essentially no
data we can look to.

03:11:56.490 --> 03:11:58.100
But we can look to
the general logic

03:11:58.100 --> 03:12:02.420
around the relationship
between body fat, testosterone,

03:12:02.420 --> 03:12:03.530
and spermatogenesis.

03:12:03.530 --> 03:12:05.210
And this was something
that was covered

03:12:05.210 --> 03:12:08.950
in a discussion I had on
optimization of hormone

03:12:08.950 --> 03:12:11.350
health for males that I
had with Dr. Kyle Gillette,

03:12:11.350 --> 03:12:13.720
who's a medical doctor
and obesity specialist.

03:12:13.720 --> 03:12:16.030
Again, you find that
episode at hubermanlab.com

03:12:16.030 --> 03:12:19.000
if you want to learn all about
hormone optimization in males.

03:12:19.000 --> 03:12:21.620
And essentially, the
story is as follows.

03:12:21.620 --> 03:12:24.770
If a male is
excessively overweight,

03:12:24.770 --> 03:12:27.370
he's carrying too much body
fat in particular, not too

03:12:27.370 --> 03:12:27.912
much muscle--

03:12:27.912 --> 03:12:29.328
although that can
be an issue too,

03:12:29.328 --> 03:12:31.450
but too much body fat
is typically the issue--

03:12:31.450 --> 03:12:35.530
so more than, say,
20% body fat--

03:12:35.530 --> 03:12:38.020
well, then losing
body fat is going

03:12:38.020 --> 03:12:41.290
to be the primary goal for
maximizing testosterone, sperm

03:12:41.290 --> 03:12:43.690
health, and spermatogenesis.

03:12:43.690 --> 03:12:47.920
If, however, a male is already
lean, well, then actually

03:12:47.920 --> 03:12:51.190
increasing calories will
increase testosterone.

03:12:51.190 --> 03:12:53.587
So it's a bit of a
complicated story,

03:12:53.587 --> 03:12:56.170
although not so complicated that
none of us can understand it.

03:12:56.170 --> 03:12:58.030
Basically, if you're
overweight, you

03:12:58.030 --> 03:13:00.940
should focus on losing weight in
order to maximize sperm quality

03:13:00.940 --> 03:13:01.510
and health.

03:13:01.510 --> 03:13:05.080
If you are very lean, well,
then restricting your calories

03:13:05.080 --> 03:13:07.960
to the point where you are
starting to lose weight

03:13:07.960 --> 03:13:10.660
or you're dropping
even more body fat

03:13:10.660 --> 03:13:13.750
is unlikely to increase
your testosterone further.

03:13:13.750 --> 03:13:15.370
It doesn't necessarily
mean it's bad

03:13:15.370 --> 03:13:17.590
or that you shouldn't
try and go, for instance,

03:13:17.590 --> 03:13:19.025
from 15% to 10% body fat.

03:13:19.025 --> 03:13:20.650
I'm not saying that
that's bad and that

03:13:20.650 --> 03:13:22.000
will reduce your testosterone.

03:13:22.000 --> 03:13:23.380
But in general,
if you're already

03:13:23.380 --> 03:13:26.408
very lean-- so 10%
body fat, 5% body

03:13:26.408 --> 03:13:28.450
fat-- and you start
restricting calories further,

03:13:28.450 --> 03:13:30.710
your testosterone
levels will drop.

03:13:30.710 --> 03:13:32.760
So in the context of
intermittent fasting,

03:13:32.760 --> 03:13:34.510
it's really not an
issue of whether or not

03:13:34.510 --> 03:13:36.640
your feeding window is
8 hours or 12 hours.

03:13:36.640 --> 03:13:38.223
It's really an issue
of whether or not

03:13:38.223 --> 03:13:40.900
you're getting enough calories
to offset the physical demands

03:13:40.900 --> 03:13:43.030
and activities of your
life, whether or not

03:13:43.030 --> 03:13:45.280
you're on a maintenance diet
to maintain your weight.

03:13:45.280 --> 03:13:47.230
And of course, you have to
put all that in the context of

03:13:47.230 --> 03:13:49.540
whether or not you're overweight
or lean to begin with.

03:13:49.540 --> 03:13:51.250
The simple thing to
take away from this

03:13:51.250 --> 03:13:53.140
is, if you're a
male who's using--

03:13:53.140 --> 03:13:55.120
because you like it--
intermittent fasting,

03:13:55.120 --> 03:13:56.560
so-called
time-restricted feeding,

03:13:56.560 --> 03:13:59.523
and you're following an
eight hour or maybe even

03:13:59.523 --> 03:14:00.940
a one meal per day
type approach--

03:14:00.940 --> 03:14:02.110
although I don't
really recommend

03:14:02.110 --> 03:14:04.610
that for a number of reasons
we could talk about separately.

03:14:04.610 --> 03:14:07.960
If you're eating over the course
of 8 or 10 or 12 hours per day

03:14:07.960 --> 03:14:10.900
because that's what works
for you and you are ingesting

03:14:10.900 --> 03:14:13.420
enough calories to maintain
your weight if you're already

03:14:13.420 --> 03:14:18.510
lean or you are
ingesting fewer calories

03:14:18.510 --> 03:14:21.010
than you are burning in order
to lose weight because you are

03:14:21.010 --> 03:14:24.295
already overweight and
you want to lose body fat,

03:14:24.295 --> 03:14:26.170
you're probably optimizing
for all the things

03:14:26.170 --> 03:14:28.930
that you need to do in order
to improve sperm quality

03:14:28.930 --> 03:14:30.310
and testosterone levels.

03:14:30.310 --> 03:14:32.020
Now, also in that
episode that I did

03:14:32.020 --> 03:14:35.080
with Dr. Kyle Gillette on
optimizing hormones for males,

03:14:35.080 --> 03:14:37.420
we talked about testosterone
replacement therapy.

03:14:37.420 --> 03:14:40.190
It's not a topic I want to get
into in any detail right now.

03:14:40.190 --> 03:14:41.740
But I will say this.

03:14:41.740 --> 03:14:44.380
Remember earlier when we were
talking about spermatogenesis

03:14:44.380 --> 03:14:46.870
and the fact that in order
for sperm to be generated

03:14:46.870 --> 03:14:50.830
consistently every month
ongoing from the time of puberty

03:14:50.830 --> 03:14:54.040
until essentially the
time that a man dies,

03:14:54.040 --> 03:14:55.250
you need two things.

03:14:55.250 --> 03:14:57.640
You need testosterone
production from the Leydig cells

03:14:57.640 --> 03:15:01.420
of the testes, and you
need spermatogenesis

03:15:01.420 --> 03:15:04.540
to be supported by that
androgen-binding protein

03:15:04.540 --> 03:15:07.420
coming from the support
cells, from the Sertoli cells.

03:15:07.420 --> 03:15:08.800
So you need
testosterone, and you

03:15:08.800 --> 03:15:11.380
need androgen-binding protein,
and you need the Leydig cells

03:15:11.380 --> 03:15:13.270
and the Sertoli cells active.

03:15:13.270 --> 03:15:16.390
When men take exogenous,
meaning from outside the body,

03:15:16.390 --> 03:15:19.510
testosterone, either by cream or
by patch or by pellets or more

03:15:19.510 --> 03:15:22.030
typically by injection--
the most typical TRT

03:15:22.030 --> 03:15:24.190
approach nowadays is
testosterone cypionate, which

03:15:24.190 --> 03:15:28.000
is biologically identical
to the kind of testosterone

03:15:28.000 --> 03:15:28.690
you would make.

03:15:28.690 --> 03:15:31.120
Well, because of negative
feedback loops, which you also

03:15:31.120 --> 03:15:33.820
learned about
earlier, the testicles

03:15:33.820 --> 03:15:37.690
themselves shut down their
own testosterone production.

03:15:37.690 --> 03:15:38.440
Why would that be?

03:15:38.440 --> 03:15:41.140
OK, so you're taking
testosterone in by syringe

03:15:41.140 --> 03:15:43.880
or by patch or any other method.

03:15:43.880 --> 03:15:46.180
So the circulating testosterone
and the amount that

03:15:46.180 --> 03:15:49.690
arrives at the testicle
is going to be hopefully

03:15:49.690 --> 03:15:51.760
clinically appropriate,
not super physiological,

03:15:51.760 --> 03:15:54.010
but it'll be somewhere in
the healthy reference range,

03:15:54.010 --> 03:15:55.203
maybe a little bit higher.

03:15:55.203 --> 03:15:57.370
Nowadays, some people are
going a little bit higher.

03:15:57.370 --> 03:15:59.230
So we're not talking about
full blown, quote, unquote,

03:15:59.230 --> 03:16:01.280
"anabolic steroid
use," keeping in mind,

03:16:01.280 --> 03:16:02.947
of course, that
estrogen is a steroid.

03:16:02.947 --> 03:16:04.030
Testosterone is a steroid.

03:16:04.030 --> 03:16:04.960
But when we think
about steroids,

03:16:04.960 --> 03:16:06.793
we mean like
performance-enhancing drugs, so

03:16:06.793 --> 03:16:08.650
super physiological doses.

03:16:08.650 --> 03:16:10.750
We're talking about
within physiological

03:16:10.750 --> 03:16:12.620
or near physiological ranges.

03:16:12.620 --> 03:16:14.380
So if someone's taking
their testosterone

03:16:14.380 --> 03:16:18.130
in from an outside,
exogenous, source,

03:16:18.130 --> 03:16:19.870
the levels of
circulating testosterone

03:16:19.870 --> 03:16:22.150
will be sufficiently
high that the pituitary

03:16:22.150 --> 03:16:26.320
will register that and will
stop making luteinizing hormone

03:16:26.320 --> 03:16:28.480
and generally
follicle-stimulating hormone,

03:16:28.480 --> 03:16:29.080
as well.

03:16:29.080 --> 03:16:31.720
And as a consequence,
spermatogenesis

03:16:31.720 --> 03:16:34.480
is vastly reduced or eliminated.

03:16:34.480 --> 03:16:38.320
In other words, for men
who are on TRT or who

03:16:38.320 --> 03:16:41.950
are taking testosterone
from an external source,

03:16:41.950 --> 03:16:43.900
the number of sperm that
they're going to make

03:16:43.900 --> 03:16:45.530
is going to be
dramatically reduced.

03:16:45.530 --> 03:16:47.572
There are things that they
can do to offset that,

03:16:47.572 --> 03:16:50.500
like taking hCG, human chorionic
gonadotropin, which is just

03:16:50.500 --> 03:16:52.180
kind of a mimic for
luteinizing hormone

03:16:52.180 --> 03:16:56.230
to stimulate the testes to
continue to make testosterone.

03:16:56.230 --> 03:16:58.450
And some men will also--

03:16:58.450 --> 03:17:02.800
or instead-- take FSH to
stimulate the Sertoli cells

03:17:02.800 --> 03:17:06.730
to support spermatogenesis--
excuse me--

03:17:06.730 --> 03:17:08.330
or both or some combination.

03:17:08.330 --> 03:17:10.090
Some people take
clomiphene, Clomid.

03:17:10.090 --> 03:17:11.673
There are any number
of different ways

03:17:11.673 --> 03:17:15.580
to bypass or offset the
sperm-reducing effects

03:17:15.580 --> 03:17:17.600
of taking exogenous
testosterone.

03:17:17.600 --> 03:17:19.330
This is a conversation
that was covered

03:17:19.330 --> 03:17:21.910
in a fair amount of detail in
that episode with Dr. Gillette.

03:17:21.910 --> 03:17:25.630
But just keep in mind that if
you are taking testosterone

03:17:25.630 --> 03:17:29.568
from an exogenous source, your
sperm counts will dramatically

03:17:29.568 --> 03:17:31.610
be reduced, unless you do
something to offset it.

03:17:31.610 --> 03:17:33.137
So if you are
wishing to conceive,

03:17:33.137 --> 03:17:34.720
you need to think
about whether or not

03:17:34.720 --> 03:17:37.180
you're going to offset the
testosterone replacement

03:17:37.180 --> 03:17:40.610
therapy or whether or not you're
going to come off it entirely.

03:17:40.610 --> 03:17:43.000
So you'll need to talk to
a urologist endocrinologist

03:17:43.000 --> 03:17:44.650
about that.

03:17:44.650 --> 03:17:47.080
And again, a number of these
different themes and ways

03:17:47.080 --> 03:17:48.820
to go about tapering
off TRT were

03:17:48.820 --> 03:17:51.040
covered in that episode
with Dr. Kyle Gillette.

03:17:51.040 --> 03:17:53.380
So if you're on TRT or
you're considering taking it

03:17:53.380 --> 03:17:55.088
and you're interested
in having children,

03:17:55.088 --> 03:17:56.875
not just now but at
any point, you really

03:17:56.875 --> 03:17:58.750
want to take these things
into consideration.

03:17:58.750 --> 03:18:01.630
Now, I do want to point out
that, for the number of you

03:18:01.630 --> 03:18:04.390
out there who are taking
supplements, some of which

03:18:04.390 --> 03:18:05.860
we've talked about
on this podcast

03:18:05.860 --> 03:18:08.270
and I've talked about in other
podcasts, such as tongkat ali--

03:18:08.270 --> 03:18:10.353
it turns out that there
are a lot of men and women

03:18:10.353 --> 03:18:13.240
taking tongkat ali to reduce
sex hormone binding globulin

03:18:13.240 --> 03:18:16.000
levels, to increase testosterone
and estrogen, in some cases,

03:18:16.000 --> 03:18:18.190
libido and so forth.

03:18:18.190 --> 03:18:20.980
Those approaches, meaning
supplement-based approaches,

03:18:20.980 --> 03:18:25.540
to increase testosterone
or free testosterone

03:18:25.540 --> 03:18:28.360
or some related
hormones, are not

03:18:28.360 --> 03:18:31.000
going to shut down your
own endogenous testosterone

03:18:31.000 --> 03:18:33.940
production and reduce the
number of sperm that you make

03:18:33.940 --> 03:18:36.835
or, at least as far as we
know, disrupt ovulation

03:18:36.835 --> 03:18:38.710
in any kind of way,
provided that the dosages

03:18:38.710 --> 03:18:39.760
are within normal ranges.

03:18:39.760 --> 03:18:42.970
Again, supplementation
to support your hormones

03:18:42.970 --> 03:18:47.470
should not disrupt
ovulation or spermatogenesis

03:18:47.470 --> 03:18:48.760
or testosterone production.

03:18:48.760 --> 03:18:49.760
Quite the opposite.

03:18:49.760 --> 03:18:50.740
It should enhance it.

03:18:50.740 --> 03:18:52.930
What I just described
around TRT as taking

03:18:52.930 --> 03:18:55.390
exogenous testosterone,
that itself

03:18:55.390 --> 03:18:57.070
is an entirely different beast.

03:18:57.070 --> 03:18:58.840
Now, with all of
that said, there

03:18:58.840 --> 03:19:02.080
are some supplements
out there that

03:19:02.080 --> 03:19:05.500
include testosterone
as a ingredient that's

03:19:05.500 --> 03:19:09.308
been snuck in to various
formulas that include

03:19:09.308 --> 03:19:10.600
blends and things of that sort.

03:19:10.600 --> 03:19:11.808
You want to be aware of that.

03:19:11.808 --> 03:19:14.770
And we did an episode about
how to develop a rational guide

03:19:14.770 --> 03:19:16.100
to supplementation.

03:19:16.100 --> 03:19:18.095
I highly recommend
listening to that episode.

03:19:18.095 --> 03:19:19.720
Again, it's timestamped,
available free

03:19:19.720 --> 03:19:22.030
at hubermanlab.com
in all formats.

03:19:22.030 --> 03:19:24.520
Because it talks about
which supplements

03:19:24.520 --> 03:19:26.320
are likely to be
"clean," quote, unquote,

03:19:26.320 --> 03:19:28.420
to contain the things that
you expect them to contain,

03:19:28.420 --> 03:19:30.337
there's more and more
evidence coming out that

03:19:30.337 --> 03:19:31.960
a lot of supplements,
including some--

03:19:31.960 --> 03:19:34.510
for instance,
supplements that contain

03:19:34.510 --> 03:19:36.850
testicle or the
extracts of testicles

03:19:36.850 --> 03:19:38.242
can contain testosterone.

03:19:38.242 --> 03:19:40.450
Whether or not they can shut
down your own endogenous

03:19:40.450 --> 03:19:42.293
testosterone
production isn't clear.

03:19:42.293 --> 03:19:43.960
No one's really
explored that in detail.

03:19:43.960 --> 03:19:45.970
But based on everything we
just talked about with TRT,

03:19:45.970 --> 03:19:48.560
it stands to reason that it
might either reduce it or shut

03:19:48.560 --> 03:19:49.060
it down.

03:19:49.060 --> 03:19:50.870
It's just never
been explored yet.

03:19:50.870 --> 03:19:53.672
So by all means, make sure
that what you're taking

03:19:53.672 --> 03:19:54.880
if you're taking supplements.

03:19:54.880 --> 03:19:57.250
But again, the
major point here is

03:19:57.250 --> 03:19:58.660
that, for both
females and males,

03:19:58.660 --> 03:20:01.240
taking supplements to
support healthy hormone

03:20:01.240 --> 03:20:04.630
production, including
things like tongkat ali,

03:20:04.630 --> 03:20:08.440
is not the same as taking
hormones or bioidentical

03:20:08.440 --> 03:20:12.010
hormones, which indeed can
shut down your own endogenous

03:20:12.010 --> 03:20:13.570
production of
hormones and thereby

03:20:13.570 --> 03:20:17.230
reduce both egg quality and
the chance of fertilization

03:20:17.230 --> 03:20:19.060
and healthy pregnancy
and sperm quality

03:20:19.060 --> 03:20:21.370
and the chance of fertilization
and healthy pregnancy.

03:20:21.370 --> 03:20:25.540
Any time there's a discussion
about fertility and pregnancy,

03:20:25.540 --> 03:20:27.700
there seems to also be
a parallel discussion

03:20:27.700 --> 03:20:29.470
about sex determination.

03:20:29.470 --> 03:20:32.830
That is, what factors can
influence whether or not

03:20:32.830 --> 03:20:35.410
the child that's born
is male or female.

03:20:35.410 --> 03:20:38.530
That is, whether or not it has
double X chromosomes-- so one X

03:20:38.530 --> 03:20:40.720
chromosome from mom, one
X chromosome from dad

03:20:40.720 --> 03:20:42.910
because the egg was
fertilized by a sperm that

03:20:42.910 --> 03:20:46.150
had an X sex chromosome,
that 23rd chromosome--

03:20:46.150 --> 03:20:48.910
or whether or not the offspring
is male, whether or not

03:20:48.910 --> 03:20:51.368
it has the X chromosome from
mom, because it's always going

03:20:51.368 --> 03:20:53.830
to be the X chromosome
in that egg,

03:20:53.830 --> 03:20:56.140
and a Y chromosome
from the sperm that

03:20:56.140 --> 03:20:57.815
fertilized that particular egg.

03:20:57.815 --> 03:20:59.440
Now, of course, there
are instances out

03:20:59.440 --> 03:21:04.870
there of people that have XXY
chromosomes or XYY chromosomes.

03:21:04.870 --> 03:21:07.900
But the vast majority
of people out there

03:21:07.900 --> 03:21:12.040
are going to have either
an XX chromosome-- so we

03:21:12.040 --> 03:21:14.740
call that a female karyotype.

03:21:14.740 --> 03:21:16.990
This is different than
genotype and phenotype,

03:21:16.990 --> 03:21:20.230
but a female karyotype
would be XX--

03:21:20.230 --> 03:21:24.760
or a male karyotype,
which would be XY.

03:21:24.760 --> 03:21:27.310
Now, despite the fact that
it is the egg and the sperm

03:21:27.310 --> 03:21:28.768
and the chromosomes
that they carry

03:21:28.768 --> 03:21:31.010
that are going to
determine the chromosomes,

03:21:31.010 --> 03:21:34.270
there's a lot of lore and
discussion about the factors

03:21:34.270 --> 03:21:38.140
that can bias which sperm
will fertilize the egg

03:21:38.140 --> 03:21:39.670
and thereby whether
or not you're

03:21:39.670 --> 03:21:43.270
going to get an XX, female,
or an XY, male, chromosome

03:21:43.270 --> 03:21:44.630
and therefore offspring.

03:21:44.630 --> 03:21:47.680
Now, not only is the lore
around this whole issue of sex

03:21:47.680 --> 03:21:52.330
determination rather prominent,
but it is also somewhat unusual

03:21:52.330 --> 03:21:53.860
and perhaps even interesting.

03:21:53.860 --> 03:21:57.580
So for instance,
Aristotle himself proposed

03:21:57.580 --> 03:22:02.440
that if a man is thinking about
himself and his own pleasure

03:22:02.440 --> 03:22:06.250
more than his partner
and her pleasure

03:22:06.250 --> 03:22:09.460
at the point of
ejaculation, then

03:22:09.460 --> 03:22:11.110
the offspring will be male.

03:22:11.110 --> 03:22:13.510
Aristotle also asserted
that if a man is thinking

03:22:13.510 --> 03:22:15.760
more about his partner
and her pleasure

03:22:15.760 --> 03:22:18.850
at the point in which he
ejaculates, well, then

03:22:18.850 --> 03:22:20.830
the offspring would be female.

03:22:20.830 --> 03:22:23.170
And of course, we
have zero reason

03:22:23.170 --> 03:22:26.110
to believe that there's any
truth to Aristotle's theory.

03:22:26.110 --> 03:22:27.693
There are no data
to support that.

03:22:27.693 --> 03:22:29.110
In fact, I'm not
even sure how you

03:22:29.110 --> 03:22:31.810
would run that experiment
because you can't really

03:22:31.810 --> 03:22:33.310
look at people's thoughts.

03:22:33.310 --> 03:22:36.310
You'd have to rely on
honest self-report.

03:22:36.310 --> 03:22:39.430
And even if people were
to faithfully report

03:22:39.430 --> 03:22:42.350
what they were thinking about
at the moment of ejaculation,

03:22:42.350 --> 03:22:44.267
this would involve, of
course, bringing people

03:22:44.267 --> 03:22:47.220
into the laboratory and
somehow measuring or analyzing

03:22:47.220 --> 03:22:48.970
their thoughts or
gathering their thoughts

03:22:48.970 --> 03:22:52.150
during the sexual intercourse
at the point of ejaculation,

03:22:52.150 --> 03:22:55.000
then figuring out which
biological sex was

03:22:55.000 --> 03:22:56.590
the offspring, et cetera.

03:22:56.590 --> 03:22:59.710
Just near impossible and
probably not the most important

03:22:59.710 --> 03:23:01.900
experiment to invest
our time doing.

03:23:01.900 --> 03:23:05.260
Nonetheless, there
continues to be

03:23:05.260 --> 03:23:07.668
a lot of lore about
what determines

03:23:07.668 --> 03:23:08.710
the sex of the offspring.

03:23:08.710 --> 03:23:11.170
Most notably, there's a
lot of lore and discussion

03:23:11.170 --> 03:23:15.310
and rumor about the idea that
particular sexual positions

03:23:15.310 --> 03:23:18.040
at the point of ejaculation
during intercourse

03:23:18.040 --> 03:23:22.030
can somehow bias the likelihood
that a pregnancy will

03:23:22.030 --> 03:23:26.430
be either resulting in
male or female offspring.

03:23:26.430 --> 03:23:28.790
Now, again, there are
zero data to support this,

03:23:28.790 --> 03:23:31.880
and yet this whole notion
of sex determination

03:23:31.880 --> 03:23:33.560
is a really interesting
one that people

03:23:33.560 --> 03:23:37.310
seem to be somewhat obsessed
by, so much so that, again,

03:23:37.310 --> 03:23:39.080
if you go online or
if you were to talk

03:23:39.080 --> 03:23:42.170
to people in the sort of
let's call it holistic

03:23:42.170 --> 03:23:46.260
or peripheral health spaces
related to fertility,

03:23:46.260 --> 03:23:47.960
there is discussion
about, OK, well,

03:23:47.960 --> 03:23:50.420
you take this sexual position
at the point of ejaculation

03:23:50.420 --> 03:23:52.337
to get a boy and you
take that sexual position

03:23:52.337 --> 03:23:54.050
at the point of
ejaculation to get a girl

03:23:54.050 --> 03:23:56.750
or you do this in the
early part of the day

03:23:56.750 --> 03:23:58.380
or the later part of the day.

03:23:58.380 --> 03:24:00.710
Again, all for
which there is zero

03:24:00.710 --> 03:24:04.340
data to support any kind
of systematic relationship

03:24:04.340 --> 03:24:06.530
between what I just discussed
and the biological sex

03:24:06.530 --> 03:24:07.370
of the offspring.

03:24:07.370 --> 03:24:11.210
That said, there are
now emerging methods

03:24:11.210 --> 03:24:17.000
that people are using in order
to separate out the sperm that

03:24:17.000 --> 03:24:20.360
will indeed give rise
to a male offspring

03:24:20.360 --> 03:24:21.870
versus a female offspring.

03:24:21.870 --> 03:24:23.720
Now, this, of course,
is done in the context

03:24:23.720 --> 03:24:25.437
of in-vitro fertilization.

03:24:25.437 --> 03:24:27.770
We haven't talked too much
about in-vitro fertilization.

03:24:27.770 --> 03:24:29.840
But in-vitro
fertilization involves,

03:24:29.840 --> 03:24:33.800
as the name suggests, taking
an egg and taking a sperm,

03:24:33.800 --> 03:24:35.180
pairing them in a dish.

03:24:35.180 --> 03:24:37.880
This can be done a
number of different ways.

03:24:37.880 --> 03:24:40.910
But just to briefly
describe the IVF procedure,

03:24:40.910 --> 03:24:44.620
IVF involves
administering supra--

03:24:44.620 --> 03:24:48.320
meaning greater than normal--
supraphysiological levels

03:24:48.320 --> 03:24:51.890
of follicle-stimulating
hormone and luteinizing hormone

03:24:51.890 --> 03:24:54.440
during the follicular
phase of a woman's cycle.

03:24:54.440 --> 03:24:58.310
What that causes is the
maturation of not just one

03:24:58.310 --> 03:25:03.630
egg that would be ovulated but
multiple follicles and eggs.

03:25:03.630 --> 03:25:07.250
And then ovulation
itself is suppressed also

03:25:07.250 --> 03:25:10.040
through the administration
of exogenous hormones.

03:25:10.040 --> 03:25:12.590
And then, under
ultrasound guidance,

03:25:12.590 --> 03:25:16.430
an OB/GYN goes in and collects
the mature eggs and follicles,

03:25:16.430 --> 03:25:18.337
puts them in a
dish, and then sperm

03:25:18.337 --> 03:25:20.420
are delivered to that dish,
and those could either

03:25:20.420 --> 03:25:22.700
be sperm that were
frozen previously,

03:25:22.700 --> 03:25:26.210
or more typically or ideally,
it would be live sperm collected

03:25:26.210 --> 03:25:29.270
that day that are
washed through a very

03:25:29.270 --> 03:25:31.040
straightforward procedure.

03:25:31.040 --> 03:25:33.230
And then those sperm
either are allowed

03:25:33.230 --> 03:25:35.870
to compete for those eggs
and fertilize those eggs

03:25:35.870 --> 03:25:39.710
and allow them to advance
to very early embryo stage

03:25:39.710 --> 03:25:42.200
before those embryos are
frozen and eventually implanted

03:25:42.200 --> 03:25:46.500
into a woman in order to have
them be carried to full term,

03:25:46.500 --> 03:25:47.180
ideally.

03:25:47.180 --> 03:25:51.260
Or there's a procedure in which
specific sperm are selected

03:25:51.260 --> 03:25:53.450
because they have the
best morphology, motility,

03:25:53.450 --> 03:25:54.260
and so forth.

03:25:54.260 --> 03:25:57.680
And in a process
called ICSI, I-C-S-I,

03:25:57.680 --> 03:26:01.790
in which the sperm themselves
are literally forced

03:26:01.790 --> 03:26:04.020
to fertilize that
particular egg.

03:26:04.020 --> 03:26:10.957
Now, under those conditions,
typically a couple or a woman,

03:26:10.957 --> 03:26:13.040
if she's doing this on her
own with a sperm donor,

03:26:13.040 --> 03:26:16.610
will get multiple
fertilized embryos

03:26:16.610 --> 03:26:20.180
that are carried to
a multicellular stage

03:26:20.180 --> 03:26:23.450
so that it's clear that
they could grow into a child

03:26:23.450 --> 03:26:26.507
if they were implanted
into a viable host--

03:26:26.507 --> 03:26:28.340
sometimes the surrogate,
sometimes the woman

03:26:28.340 --> 03:26:30.170
who wants the child herself.

03:26:30.170 --> 03:26:31.880
And under those
conditions, it is

03:26:31.880 --> 03:26:33.770
possible to look at
the genetic makeup,

03:26:33.770 --> 03:26:37.040
including the karyotype,
of those early nascent

03:26:37.040 --> 03:26:40.310
embryos, in which case
people really can select

03:26:40.310 --> 03:26:41.480
the sex of their offspring.

03:26:41.480 --> 03:26:45.260
That is, they will have
some embryos that are

03:26:45.260 --> 03:26:47.510
XX, some embryos that are XY.

03:26:47.510 --> 03:26:49.010
It's very likely,
also, that they

03:26:49.010 --> 03:26:53.240
will have some embryos that have
karyotypes or genotypes which

03:26:53.240 --> 03:26:56.330
are not ideal in that
they would potentially

03:26:56.330 --> 03:26:58.580
lead to a miscarriage or
some other genetic defect.

03:26:58.580 --> 03:27:01.400
And so, typically,
people do not select

03:27:01.400 --> 03:27:05.120
to implant those embryos
if they have the option

03:27:05.120 --> 03:27:10.490
to implant embryos that are
of either XX or XY karyotype

03:27:10.490 --> 03:27:13.670
and the normal
chromosomal arrangements

03:27:13.670 --> 03:27:16.070
for obvious reasons.

03:27:16.070 --> 03:27:20.030
So the whole point here is
that sex selection is possible,

03:27:20.030 --> 03:27:23.180
but only using
in-vitro fertilization.

03:27:23.180 --> 03:27:25.700
The other thing that
is becoming clear to us

03:27:25.700 --> 03:27:29.300
in more recent years is that
sex selection is actually

03:27:29.300 --> 03:27:31.970
possible at the level
of the sperm even prior

03:27:31.970 --> 03:27:33.210
to fertilization.

03:27:33.210 --> 03:27:36.470
This is an emerging data
set, and this is largely

03:27:36.470 --> 03:27:38.690
happening in clinics outside
of the United States.

03:27:38.690 --> 03:27:41.120
But there are some clinics
that have figured out methods

03:27:41.120 --> 03:27:43.190
in which they can
take a sperm sample

03:27:43.190 --> 03:27:46.700
and they can spin that
sperm sample in a centrifuge

03:27:46.700 --> 03:27:49.400
at a rate that separates
out the sperm into what

03:27:49.400 --> 03:27:50.850
are called different fractions.

03:27:50.850 --> 03:27:52.400
So for those of you who've
done a little bit of biology

03:27:52.400 --> 03:27:55.310
with centrifuge, it's when
you spin any kind of substance

03:27:55.310 --> 03:27:58.165
that includes multiple things
in it of different weights.

03:27:58.165 --> 03:28:00.290
When you spin them, the
things of different weights

03:28:00.290 --> 03:28:02.423
segregate out into
different fractions

03:28:02.423 --> 03:28:03.590
along the depth of the tube.

03:28:03.590 --> 03:28:05.810
And then you can take out
one fraction or the next

03:28:05.810 --> 03:28:06.860
simply with a little pipette.

03:28:06.860 --> 03:28:08.985
You take out the top
fraction, the middle fraction,

03:28:08.985 --> 03:28:09.600
and so forth.

03:28:09.600 --> 03:28:11.240
And what these clinics
have figured out

03:28:11.240 --> 03:28:16.070
is that if they spin the sperm
sample at the correct spin rate

03:28:16.070 --> 03:28:19.100
that the sperm
that will give rise

03:28:19.100 --> 03:28:22.670
to male offspring and the
sperm that will give rise

03:28:22.670 --> 03:28:25.730
to female offspring segregate
out into different fractions,

03:28:25.730 --> 03:28:29.690
allowing them to take each
of those fractions separately

03:28:29.690 --> 03:28:33.710
and to apply them to eggs, if
it's in-vitro fertilization,

03:28:33.710 --> 03:28:37.130
and give rise very reliably,
certainly much more

03:28:37.130 --> 03:28:41.390
than chance, to either
male or female embryos.

03:28:41.390 --> 03:28:43.760
They also, of course,
can choose to do

03:28:43.760 --> 03:28:46.200
this outside the context
of in-vitro fertilization.

03:28:46.200 --> 03:28:49.670
So some people are now opting
to have their sperm samples spun

03:28:49.670 --> 03:28:52.850
out in this way, separate
out the sperm that give rise

03:28:52.850 --> 03:28:54.590
to male or female
offspring, and then

03:28:54.590 --> 03:28:58.590
to only use the fraction
that they are interested in--

03:28:58.590 --> 03:29:00.590
so if they want a boy,
they'll use one fraction.

03:29:00.590 --> 03:29:03.020
If they want a girl, they'll
use different fraction--

03:29:03.020 --> 03:29:06.650
and then to use those fractions
in the context of what's

03:29:06.650 --> 03:29:09.980
called IUI, or intrauterine
insemination, which

03:29:09.980 --> 03:29:14.000
is, as the name suggests, rather
than having the man deliver

03:29:14.000 --> 03:29:16.460
the ejaculate with his penis
and the sperm with his penis,

03:29:16.460 --> 03:29:17.990
they have a device.

03:29:17.990 --> 03:29:19.890
The devices are now
commercially sold.

03:29:19.890 --> 03:29:21.890
Believe it or not, they're
sold over-the-counter

03:29:21.890 --> 03:29:24.210
and on the internet, so people
will even do this at home.

03:29:24.210 --> 03:29:26.377
And so what they're doing
is they'll take the sperm,

03:29:26.377 --> 03:29:31.100
and they'll do IUI in order
to bias the probability

03:29:31.100 --> 03:29:33.620
that they're going to get a
male or a female offspring.

03:29:33.620 --> 03:29:36.320
Again, this is something
that's now emerging.

03:29:36.320 --> 03:29:37.910
It's not commonplace.

03:29:37.910 --> 03:29:42.260
Most of the time, people simply
roll the dice, as it were,

03:29:42.260 --> 03:29:46.430
by having either intercourse
and just hoping for or not

03:29:46.430 --> 03:29:49.010
caring if they get a male
or a female offspring

03:29:49.010 --> 03:29:51.050
or, in the instance
of IVF, selecting

03:29:51.050 --> 03:29:53.180
male or female offspring,
sometimes largely

03:29:53.180 --> 03:29:55.100
on the basis of the
chromosomal arrangements.

03:29:55.100 --> 03:29:58.790
So of course, some
people might prefer

03:29:58.790 --> 03:30:01.100
to have one or the
other biological sex

03:30:01.100 --> 03:30:02.070
as their offspring.

03:30:02.070 --> 03:30:05.180
But of course, the healthy
chromosomal arrangements

03:30:05.180 --> 03:30:08.030
are going to be paramount
for getting a healthy child.

03:30:08.030 --> 03:30:11.240
And as I mentioned before,
unhealthy chromosomal

03:30:11.240 --> 03:30:13.340
arrangements or abnormal
chromosomal arrangements

03:30:13.340 --> 03:30:16.530
often lead to miscarriage
and/or birth defects.

03:30:16.530 --> 03:30:19.550
So selecting for healthy
chromosomal arrangements

03:30:19.550 --> 03:30:21.290
is always paramount,
but some people

03:30:21.290 --> 03:30:22.880
are selecting for
biological sex.

03:30:22.880 --> 03:30:27.410
And indeed, some couples
who can conceive naturally

03:30:27.410 --> 03:30:30.860
are opting for
IUI in order to be

03:30:30.860 --> 03:30:33.740
able to select biological
sex because of this ability

03:30:33.740 --> 03:30:37.040
to spin out the sperm samples
to different fractions

03:30:37.040 --> 03:30:39.980
and select the male
or female sperm.

03:30:39.980 --> 03:30:41.630
That is, the sperm
that would give rise

03:30:41.630 --> 03:30:43.020
to a male or female offspring.

03:30:43.020 --> 03:30:46.980
So this is a rapidly emerging
theme, believe it or not.

03:30:46.980 --> 03:30:48.170
Who knew?

03:30:48.170 --> 03:30:50.870
And of course, it has nothing to
do with Aristotle's assertions

03:30:50.870 --> 03:30:52.912
about what people are
thinking about at the point

03:30:52.912 --> 03:30:54.860
of ejaculation, nor
does it have anything

03:30:54.860 --> 03:30:57.860
to do with body position at
the point of ejaculation.

03:30:57.860 --> 03:30:59.510
But I do find it
rather interesting

03:30:59.510 --> 03:31:02.210
that, even in this
day and age, people

03:31:02.210 --> 03:31:05.870
seem to be continually
pursuing new and different ways

03:31:05.870 --> 03:31:08.570
to understand why one
sperm or another sperm

03:31:08.570 --> 03:31:11.550
happens to fertilize the egg.

03:31:11.550 --> 03:31:13.990
And when that information
is not available,

03:31:13.990 --> 03:31:15.740
because, frankly, it's
not available yet--

03:31:15.740 --> 03:31:17.960
we don't know why
a sperm containing

03:31:17.960 --> 03:31:20.420
a Y chromosome or a sperm
containing an X chromosome

03:31:20.420 --> 03:31:22.005
is more likely to
fertilize an egg.

03:31:22.005 --> 03:31:23.630
And there are some
ideas, for instance,

03:31:23.630 --> 03:31:26.150
that older fathers tend to
have more daughters as opposed

03:31:26.150 --> 03:31:26.767
to sons.

03:31:26.767 --> 03:31:29.100
But when you really look at
the data, it's pretty mixed.

03:31:29.100 --> 03:31:31.607
So if you've heard
that before, it

03:31:31.607 --> 03:31:33.440
has a particular nickname
that I'm not going

03:31:33.440 --> 03:31:34.637
to describe on the podcast.

03:31:34.637 --> 03:31:35.720
You can look it up online.

03:31:35.720 --> 03:31:39.800
But if any of you are aware
of any other kind of ideals

03:31:39.800 --> 03:31:42.328
or lore, no matter how
ridiculous or crazy, please

03:31:42.328 --> 03:31:44.120
put them in the comment
section on YouTube.

03:31:44.120 --> 03:31:47.090
I'd be very curious to learn
about those, mostly out

03:31:47.090 --> 03:31:49.430
of interest and curiosity.

03:31:49.430 --> 03:31:52.340
But, look, sometimes
these outrageous stories,

03:31:52.340 --> 03:31:55.905
such as notions of body
position and how they influence

03:31:55.905 --> 03:31:58.280
biological sex, even though
they turn out not to be true,

03:31:58.280 --> 03:32:00.327
turn out to be interesting
for other reasons.

03:32:00.327 --> 03:32:01.910
And in fact, next,
we're going to talk

03:32:01.910 --> 03:32:04.550
about how body position
during sexual intercourse

03:32:04.550 --> 03:32:08.640
can, in fact, influence
fertility and pregnancy.

03:32:08.640 --> 03:32:11.180
So another common theme
around fertility and pregnancy

03:32:11.180 --> 03:32:13.310
that you'll hear about
is that, for couples

03:32:13.310 --> 03:32:17.210
that are trying to get pregnant,
that during intercourse they

03:32:17.210 --> 03:32:19.640
should do whatever it
is that works for them,

03:32:19.640 --> 03:32:23.180
but then after
the man ejaculates

03:32:23.180 --> 03:32:25.310
that the woman should
try and position

03:32:25.310 --> 03:32:30.230
her ankles above her head
or somehow otherwise tilt

03:32:30.230 --> 03:32:34.190
her pelvis back in order
to increase the rate and/or

03:32:34.190 --> 03:32:37.590
probability that the
sperm swim toward the egg,

03:32:37.590 --> 03:32:39.380
as opposed to the
other direction.

03:32:39.380 --> 03:32:42.470
Now, I talked to a couple
of different OB/GYNs

03:32:42.470 --> 03:32:46.670
and urologists that are focused
on fertility about this topic,

03:32:46.670 --> 03:32:49.040
and it turns out you get
pretty mixed answers as to

03:32:49.040 --> 03:32:51.380
whether or not there's
any validity to this idea

03:32:51.380 --> 03:32:54.830
that the woman's body position
after the man ejaculates

03:32:54.830 --> 03:32:57.380
inside of her can
somehow influence

03:32:57.380 --> 03:32:58.850
the probability of pregnancy.

03:32:58.850 --> 03:33:01.160
One group of experts
told me that there

03:33:01.160 --> 03:33:03.560
is no reason for a woman
to need to continue

03:33:03.560 --> 03:33:07.040
to lie down, elevate the
ankles, or in any way

03:33:07.040 --> 03:33:09.650
tilt her pelvis back
in order to increase

03:33:09.650 --> 03:33:12.830
the probability of
successful fertilization.

03:33:12.830 --> 03:33:17.120
The other group suggested that
indeed there is a strong reason

03:33:17.120 --> 03:33:21.110
to believe that tilting the
pelvis back, maybe even keeping

03:33:21.110 --> 03:33:23.940
the ankles elevated,
and having a woman lie

03:33:23.940 --> 03:33:27.990
on her back for about 15 minutes
with the pelvis positioned

03:33:27.990 --> 03:33:33.210
at about 20 degrees back
is ideal for optimizing

03:33:33.210 --> 03:33:33.815
fertilization.

03:33:33.815 --> 03:33:35.190
I mean, they were
really specific

03:33:35.190 --> 03:33:36.273
about the recommendations.

03:33:36.273 --> 03:33:40.890
So I find this interesting that,
within the cohort of extremely

03:33:40.890 --> 03:33:45.510
well trained MDs, OB/GYNs
and urology fertility docs,

03:33:45.510 --> 03:33:47.580
and OB/GYNs, you see a split.

03:33:47.580 --> 03:33:49.290
It has nothing to do
with whether or not

03:33:49.290 --> 03:33:52.920
the physician was male or
female or their training

03:33:52.920 --> 03:33:54.590
or their institution,
none of that.

03:33:54.590 --> 03:33:56.740
There just seemed to be a sort
of even split between the two.

03:33:56.740 --> 03:33:58.500
Now, granted, it wasn't
the largest sample size

03:33:58.500 --> 03:33:59.625
that I could have obtained.

03:33:59.625 --> 03:34:02.090
And yet I do find it
interesting that there's

03:34:02.090 --> 03:34:05.040
this split in the
opinion about this.

03:34:05.040 --> 03:34:08.940
One group, the group that said,
no, pelvic position doesn't

03:34:08.940 --> 03:34:11.620
really matter, don't
worry about it,

03:34:11.620 --> 03:34:14.460
it's not going to influence
the rates of fertilization,

03:34:14.460 --> 03:34:17.595
argued that the sperm
swim very quickly

03:34:17.595 --> 03:34:19.470
and that if they are
released near the cervix

03:34:19.470 --> 03:34:22.080
they're going to swim very
quickly toward the egg

03:34:22.080 --> 03:34:25.860
in order to fertilize it
regardless of pelvic position.

03:34:25.860 --> 03:34:30.090
The other group said, well,
yes, sperm swim quickly

03:34:30.090 --> 03:34:32.910
and even if they're
released right at the entry

03:34:32.910 --> 03:34:36.580
to the cervix that the sperm
still have a long distance

03:34:36.580 --> 03:34:37.080
to go.

03:34:37.080 --> 03:34:39.360
Again, if you were to
scale this according

03:34:39.360 --> 03:34:42.570
to the size of the sperm versus
the size of a human body,

03:34:42.570 --> 03:34:45.090
an entire human body,
what you'd scale it to

03:34:45.090 --> 03:34:47.340
is the distance between Los
Angeles and San Francisco.

03:34:47.340 --> 03:34:49.770
And it needs to undergo that
basically within 24 hours

03:34:49.770 --> 03:34:50.040
or so.

03:34:50.040 --> 03:34:51.457
Although, as we
mentioned earlier,

03:34:51.457 --> 03:34:54.090
sperm can survive
quite a while inside

03:34:54.090 --> 03:34:57.850
of the woman's body-- maybe
three or five days at least.

03:34:57.850 --> 03:34:59.245
So in both cases
they acknowledge

03:34:59.245 --> 03:35:00.120
it's a long distance.

03:35:00.120 --> 03:35:01.830
But on the one hand,
you have a group

03:35:01.830 --> 03:35:04.315
of experts that are saying the
sperm more or less know what

03:35:04.315 --> 03:35:05.940
to do and are going
to do it regardless

03:35:05.940 --> 03:35:09.060
of the position of the woman
after ejaculation inside her

03:35:09.060 --> 03:35:11.060
and the other group
saying, no, we

03:35:11.060 --> 03:35:12.600
want to do everything
we can to bias

03:35:12.600 --> 03:35:16.170
the likelihood that the
sperm will fertilize the egg.

03:35:16.170 --> 03:35:19.920
Well, setting aside
the basic argument

03:35:19.920 --> 03:35:25.020
that tilting back at the pelvis
and lying stationary or so

03:35:25.020 --> 03:35:28.350
for about 15 minutes
after sexual intercourse

03:35:28.350 --> 03:35:33.690
and ejaculation is not
an expensive endeavor,

03:35:33.690 --> 03:35:36.210
although it requires
a little bit of time.

03:35:36.210 --> 03:35:39.420
And it forces people to
remain motionless or close

03:35:39.420 --> 03:35:42.690
to motionless, and they're not
up and around and moving about.

03:35:42.690 --> 03:35:45.400
Aside from that, it's a
relatively low investment.

03:35:45.400 --> 03:35:47.430
So one argument is,
well, if it could

03:35:47.430 --> 03:35:50.820
bias the likelihood of
fertilization at all

03:35:50.820 --> 03:35:54.807
and people want to get pregnant,
why wouldn't they do that?

03:35:54.807 --> 03:35:56.140
So that's a reasonable argument.

03:35:56.140 --> 03:35:58.410
But it doesn't really
point to the mechanism.

03:35:58.410 --> 03:36:01.518
The arguments that point to a
potential mechanism are that--

03:36:01.518 --> 03:36:03.810
if you recall what we were
talking about when we talked

03:36:03.810 --> 03:36:06.055
about sperm quality,
sperm quality

03:36:06.055 --> 03:36:07.680
involves a bunch of
different measures,

03:36:07.680 --> 03:36:11.250
like concentration of sperm
per milliliter of semen,

03:36:11.250 --> 03:36:14.610
morphology of those sperm,
how many are forward motile.

03:36:14.610 --> 03:36:17.880
It turns out that in any
one ejaculate sample,

03:36:17.880 --> 03:36:22.710
the total number of forward
motile and yet fast forward

03:36:22.710 --> 03:36:28.590
motile sperm that are also of
the highest quality morphology

03:36:28.590 --> 03:36:30.370
is actually quite low.

03:36:30.370 --> 03:36:33.000
And so the idea here
is that you want

03:36:33.000 --> 03:36:35.730
to get as many sperm
of the highest quality

03:36:35.730 --> 03:36:39.030
swimming toward the egg because
those sperm stand the highest

03:36:39.030 --> 03:36:40.682
probability of
fertilizing that egg.

03:36:40.682 --> 03:36:43.140
And in fact, this relates to
some of the discussion we were

03:36:43.140 --> 03:36:46.890
having earlier about behavioral
dos and don'ts for sake

03:36:46.890 --> 03:36:50.400
of increasing the
probability of fertilization.

03:36:50.400 --> 03:36:53.910
And the one that is most
important here is cannabis.

03:36:53.910 --> 03:36:55.740
It turns out that
the data on cannabis

03:36:55.740 --> 03:36:58.500
really do support the
idea that some of you

03:36:58.500 --> 03:37:00.930
may have heard from
parents and teachers--

03:37:00.930 --> 03:37:03.720
I don't know, I did hear this
from parents and teachers--

03:37:03.720 --> 03:37:08.700
that cannabis can disrupt
the swimming styles of sperm

03:37:08.700 --> 03:37:11.820
in ways that are not
supportive of fertilization,

03:37:11.820 --> 03:37:14.100
that it can turn more of
the sperm into twitchers.

03:37:14.100 --> 03:37:15.210
Although when I
learned about this,

03:37:15.210 --> 03:37:17.002
I was not informed of
the word "twitchers."

03:37:17.002 --> 03:37:20.100
What I was told is that,
if you use cannabis,

03:37:20.100 --> 03:37:22.440
that the sperm don't know
which direction to go,

03:37:22.440 --> 03:37:25.200
that they're confused,
almost implying

03:37:25.200 --> 03:37:27.870
that the sperm themselves
are high on cannabis.

03:37:27.870 --> 03:37:31.350
Well, that's certainly not the
argument that I'm making here.

03:37:31.350 --> 03:37:34.260
But it does seem to be
the case that people

03:37:34.260 --> 03:37:38.630
who use cannabis, even once,
the sperm that are generated

03:37:38.630 --> 03:37:43.700
during that particular month
or two months during which

03:37:43.700 --> 03:37:46.190
or after which they
use cannabis have

03:37:46.190 --> 03:37:50.870
less forward motility and
possibly altered morphology,

03:37:50.870 --> 03:37:51.560
as well.

03:37:51.560 --> 03:37:53.120
I want to be very
clear, I did not

03:37:53.120 --> 03:37:55.790
say that if you use cannabis
once you are forever

03:37:55.790 --> 03:37:59.360
disrupting the motility and
morphology of your sperm.

03:37:59.360 --> 03:38:00.170
I did not say that.

03:38:00.170 --> 03:38:02.750
What I said is that if
you use cannabis once,

03:38:02.750 --> 03:38:05.960
then the sperm that are
generated in the 60 days

03:38:05.960 --> 03:38:09.130
after that cannabis
use are going

03:38:09.130 --> 03:38:12.830
to have a higher incidence of
disrupted motility and perhaps

03:38:12.830 --> 03:38:14.840
morphology as well.

03:38:14.840 --> 03:38:19.900
Remember, sperm are continually
generated every 60 days or so.

03:38:19.900 --> 03:38:23.260
And so if you use cannabis
once, you are not forever

03:38:23.260 --> 03:38:24.280
disrupting your sperm.

03:38:24.280 --> 03:38:26.530
But if you are using
cannabis and then you

03:38:26.530 --> 03:38:28.870
are looking to conceive
in the next 60 days,

03:38:28.870 --> 03:38:32.950
you are going to be reducing,
we think significantly so,

03:38:32.950 --> 03:38:36.740
the number of quality
forwardly motile sperm.

03:38:36.740 --> 03:38:39.520
So the simple takeaway from
this is avoid cannabis use.

03:38:39.520 --> 03:38:41.950
Although if you are going
to use cannabis-- and again,

03:38:41.950 --> 03:38:44.170
there are medical
uses of cannabis

03:38:44.170 --> 03:38:46.600
and beneficial uses of cannabis
for certain populations.

03:38:46.600 --> 03:38:48.410
It can be bad for
other populations.

03:38:48.410 --> 03:38:50.530
We talked about that in
the Huberman Lab podcast

03:38:50.530 --> 03:38:51.460
all about cannabis.

03:38:51.460 --> 03:38:53.110
But if you're going
to use cannabis,

03:38:53.110 --> 03:38:56.770
you should try and abstain
from cannabis in the two months

03:38:56.770 --> 03:39:00.970
prior to the attempt to
fertilize and get pregnant.

03:39:00.970 --> 03:39:03.580
Now, I'm not aware
of any data on how

03:39:03.580 --> 03:39:07.000
cannabis use by the woman
can influence the likelihood

03:39:07.000 --> 03:39:08.590
of fertilization and pregnancy.

03:39:08.590 --> 03:39:11.052
And I want to couch this whole
discussion around cannabis

03:39:11.052 --> 03:39:13.510
under the umbrella of something
that came up in the episode

03:39:13.510 --> 03:39:16.930
that I did on cannabis,
which is that, for about half

03:39:16.930 --> 03:39:19.790
of people out there,
male and female--

03:39:19.790 --> 03:39:23.710
so here we're not distinguishing
by biological sex.

03:39:23.710 --> 03:39:25.630
About half of people
that use cannabis

03:39:25.630 --> 03:39:27.340
report it as an aphrodisiac.

03:39:27.340 --> 03:39:30.595
It makes them want to have
sexual intercourse more than

03:39:30.595 --> 03:39:31.720
if they don't use cannabis.

03:39:31.720 --> 03:39:33.640
And for the other
half, it actually

03:39:33.640 --> 03:39:36.490
has the opposite effect by way
of an influence on a hormone

03:39:36.490 --> 03:39:38.500
called prolactin,
which suppresses

03:39:38.500 --> 03:39:40.240
the dopamine system,
the testosterone,

03:39:40.240 --> 03:39:42.290
and the estrogenic system.

03:39:42.290 --> 03:39:45.190
And so this whole idea that
cannabis is an aphrodisiac

03:39:45.190 --> 03:39:48.250
seems to be true for about half
of the human population and not

03:39:48.250 --> 03:39:50.060
for the other half of
the human population.

03:39:50.060 --> 03:39:52.660
So I mention that because
I know a number of people

03:39:52.660 --> 03:39:55.720
use cannabis as an aphrodisiac.

03:39:55.720 --> 03:39:57.610
They like to use cannabis
before intercourse.

03:39:57.610 --> 03:40:00.070
It was actually very
surprising to me

03:40:00.070 --> 03:40:02.200
to discover when I
researched that cannabis

03:40:02.200 --> 03:40:07.660
episode that approximately
15% of women who are pregnant

03:40:07.660 --> 03:40:10.510
continue to use cannabis
during pregnancy.

03:40:10.510 --> 03:40:12.700
And that's a very
alarming statistic.

03:40:12.700 --> 03:40:16.330
And everything we know is
that the use of cannabis

03:40:16.330 --> 03:40:19.600
during pregnancy is detrimental
to the health and particularly

03:40:19.600 --> 03:40:21.350
the brain development
of the fetus.

03:40:21.350 --> 03:40:23.170
So that's a real concern.

03:40:23.170 --> 03:40:25.930
I highly recommend women
abstain from cannabis use

03:40:25.930 --> 03:40:27.490
during pregnancy.

03:40:27.490 --> 03:40:30.250
Talk to your OB/GYN about
it if you're using it all

03:40:30.250 --> 03:40:31.630
or considering using at all.

03:40:31.630 --> 03:40:33.790
So based on what I told
you earlier about the fact

03:40:33.790 --> 03:40:38.230
that cannabis use is not good
for egg quality and the fact

03:40:38.230 --> 03:40:40.930
that cannabis use can
disrupt the motility of sperm

03:40:40.930 --> 03:40:44.170
and therefore is not
good for sperm quality

03:40:44.170 --> 03:40:47.740
and it can disrupt the patterns
of swimming in sperm in ways

03:40:47.740 --> 03:40:49.942
that reduce the
likelihood of fertility,

03:40:49.942 --> 03:40:52.150
I think the take-home message
is clear, which is that

03:40:52.150 --> 03:40:55.030
whether or not you want
to be a cannabis user

03:40:55.030 --> 03:40:57.220
or not, if you are going
to try and conceive

03:40:57.220 --> 03:40:58.720
and certainly while
you're pregnant,

03:40:58.720 --> 03:41:00.970
you're going to want to
avoid the use of cannabis.

03:41:00.970 --> 03:41:03.970
And that is smoked cannabis
and vaped cannabis.

03:41:03.970 --> 03:41:07.390
And during pregnancy,
the consumption

03:41:07.390 --> 03:41:10.060
of cannabis even in edible
form or in tincture form

03:41:10.060 --> 03:41:12.880
is also going to be detrimental
to the developing fetus.

03:41:12.880 --> 03:41:15.070
But of course, we
started this conversation

03:41:15.070 --> 03:41:18.100
in the context of body
position, in particular

03:41:18.100 --> 03:41:20.200
at the point of
ejaculation, in determining

03:41:20.200 --> 03:41:24.610
the sex of the offspring and/or
the likelihood of getting

03:41:24.610 --> 03:41:26.750
a successful fertilization
in pregnancy.

03:41:26.750 --> 03:41:30.970
And I think that given that the
tilting back of the pelvis--

03:41:30.970 --> 03:41:34.330
so again, this is elevating the
pelvis by about 20 degrees--

03:41:34.330 --> 03:41:36.310
I don't think it has
to be exact, exact--

03:41:36.310 --> 03:41:40.120
but about 20 degrees for about
15 minutes post-ejaculation

03:41:40.120 --> 03:41:42.400
inside of the
woman-- or I suppose

03:41:42.400 --> 03:41:45.700
if people are using IUI,
intrauterine insemination.

03:41:45.700 --> 03:41:48.760
Since that seems to be the
consensus among those experts

03:41:48.760 --> 03:41:53.170
that believe that
pelvic tilt backward

03:41:53.170 --> 03:41:55.990
can be beneficial for
increasing the probability

03:41:55.990 --> 03:41:58.120
of fertilization and
given that it involves

03:41:58.120 --> 03:42:00.557
no cost but a little bit
of time seems to me that,

03:42:00.557 --> 03:42:02.140
if you want to get
pregnant, that that

03:42:02.140 --> 03:42:03.577
would be the right thing to do.

03:42:03.577 --> 03:42:05.410
And as far as I know,
there's no information

03:42:05.410 --> 03:42:08.980
nor was I able to obtain any
recommendations from experts

03:42:08.980 --> 03:42:11.770
about what the ideal
body position of the male

03:42:11.770 --> 03:42:14.320
is after ejaculation
if the goal is

03:42:14.320 --> 03:42:17.450
to increase the probability
of fertilization in pregnancy.

03:42:17.450 --> 03:42:19.660
So we've been talking about
behavioral interventions,

03:42:19.660 --> 03:42:21.952
some dos and some don'ts that
people can do to increase

03:42:21.952 --> 03:42:25.150
their fertility, and the
likelihood that any fertilized

03:42:25.150 --> 03:42:27.670
egg will be carried
to term successfully.

03:42:27.670 --> 03:42:29.680
And soon we'll also
talk about things

03:42:29.680 --> 03:42:32.230
that people can take to
improve their fertility.

03:42:32.230 --> 03:42:34.360
Now, keep in mind that
this entire discussion

03:42:34.360 --> 03:42:35.800
is about fertility.

03:42:35.800 --> 03:42:38.050
But also remember,
as we discussed

03:42:38.050 --> 03:42:40.720
at the beginning of
the episode, trying

03:42:40.720 --> 03:42:44.200
to increase your fertility
is one of the best ways

03:42:44.200 --> 03:42:47.290
to think about trying
to create and maintain

03:42:47.290 --> 03:42:49.392
optimal physical health.

03:42:49.392 --> 03:42:51.100
So for people that
are trying to conceive

03:42:51.100 --> 03:42:53.230
and for people who are
not trying to conceive,

03:42:53.230 --> 03:42:55.510
optimizing your fertility
status, whether or not

03:42:55.510 --> 03:42:58.030
you're male or female,
is one of the best ways

03:42:58.030 --> 03:42:59.710
to target those approaches.

03:42:59.710 --> 03:43:02.440
And there are now a lot of
data supporting the idea

03:43:02.440 --> 03:43:04.960
that acupuncture
of all things can

03:43:04.960 --> 03:43:08.740
be very beneficial for improving
both female and male fertility

03:43:08.740 --> 03:43:10.930
and, should a
woman get pregnant,

03:43:10.930 --> 03:43:13.570
for improving the quality
of outcomes-- that

03:43:13.570 --> 03:43:15.460
is, the likelihood
that there will

03:43:15.460 --> 03:43:19.600
be a successful pregnancy
that is carried to term,

03:43:19.600 --> 03:43:22.312
not premature, and
so on and so forth.

03:43:22.312 --> 03:43:23.770
Now, for some of
you out there, you

03:43:23.770 --> 03:43:25.270
might think, oh, of
course, acupuncture,

03:43:25.270 --> 03:43:27.687
acupuncture has been known to
work for thousands of years.

03:43:27.687 --> 03:43:30.250
And therefore,
it's not surprising

03:43:30.250 --> 03:43:33.310
that it would assist with
fertility and pregnancy.

03:43:33.310 --> 03:43:35.210
For many of you
out there, however,

03:43:35.210 --> 03:43:36.730
probably thinking,
acupuncture, that

03:43:36.730 --> 03:43:38.530
seems kind of like
fringe science.

03:43:38.530 --> 03:43:41.050
But what I can assure
you is that there are now

03:43:41.050 --> 03:43:43.420
quite a few clinical
trials funded

03:43:43.420 --> 03:43:46.720
by government agencies, like the
National Institutes of Health,

03:43:46.720 --> 03:43:49.450
showing that acupuncture is
a very effective treatment

03:43:49.450 --> 03:43:50.930
for a number of
different things,

03:43:50.930 --> 03:43:52.660
including fertility
and pregnancy,

03:43:52.660 --> 03:43:56.560
but for hormone status,
for stress relief,

03:43:56.560 --> 03:43:59.180
even for chronic illnesses
of different kinds,

03:43:59.180 --> 03:44:00.680
including autoimmune illnesses.

03:44:00.680 --> 03:44:03.020
So this is no longer
considered fringe science.

03:44:03.020 --> 03:44:05.050
In fact, one of the
best laboratories

03:44:05.050 --> 03:44:07.210
in the world working
on this is a laboratory

03:44:07.210 --> 03:44:10.900
out of Harvard Medical School
run by a guy named Qiufu Fu.

03:44:10.900 --> 03:44:14.740
Qiufu's lab has really been
exploring in a mechanistic way

03:44:14.740 --> 03:44:17.080
how the different
stimulation sites that

03:44:17.080 --> 03:44:19.210
are used in acupuncture--
so where the needles are

03:44:19.210 --> 03:44:21.850
inserted-- tap into
neural pathways that

03:44:21.850 --> 03:44:23.870
link the different
organs of the body.

03:44:23.870 --> 03:44:26.830
So for instance, they've
found that stimulation

03:44:26.830 --> 03:44:29.710
of a particular site
on the lower limb

03:44:29.710 --> 03:44:32.080
can reduce inflammation
dramatically

03:44:32.080 --> 03:44:35.170
throughout the body by
way of neural pathways

03:44:35.170 --> 03:44:37.660
that originate in the
lower limb and extend

03:44:37.660 --> 03:44:39.950
to areas such as the
kidney and the pancreas.

03:44:39.950 --> 03:44:42.790
So all these, quote,
unquote, "ancient maps"

03:44:42.790 --> 03:44:44.950
of the human body as they
relate to acupuncture

03:44:44.950 --> 03:44:47.530
are now being parsed at the
level of mechanism, which

03:44:47.530 --> 03:44:50.710
I think is wonderful because
it not only is showing us

03:44:50.710 --> 03:44:54.190
that so much of what has
been purported and reported

03:44:54.190 --> 03:44:56.740
in the landscape of
acupuncture actually

03:44:56.740 --> 03:44:58.720
has an underlying
mechanistic basis,

03:44:58.720 --> 03:45:01.550
and with additional mechanistic
understanding, of course,

03:45:01.550 --> 03:45:03.770
always arrive new
and better practices.

03:45:03.770 --> 03:45:06.880
That's the idea, to evolve
these fields of acupuncture,

03:45:06.880 --> 03:45:08.980
to evolve the fields of
mechanistic understanding

03:45:08.980 --> 03:45:10.610
of our biology and health.

03:45:10.610 --> 03:45:14.590
And so the issue of whether
or not acupuncture can assist

03:45:14.590 --> 03:45:18.490
in getting pregnant and in
carrying a child to term

03:45:18.490 --> 03:45:20.740
and for that child to
be healthy are really

03:45:20.740 --> 03:45:23.320
starting to emerge
in a major way.

03:45:23.320 --> 03:45:25.300
And rather than go
into all those data

03:45:25.300 --> 03:45:27.640
in detail, what I can
tell you is that there are

03:45:27.640 --> 03:45:29.890
clinical trials and data
supporting the fact that

03:45:29.890 --> 03:45:32.050
female fertility
itself can be supported

03:45:32.050 --> 03:45:36.250
by acupuncture through several
mechanisms, one of which

03:45:36.250 --> 03:45:39.335
is the balancing-- and I realize
that's a somewhat tricky term,

03:45:39.335 --> 03:45:40.960
and I'll define it
better in a moment--

03:45:40.960 --> 03:45:46.130
the balancing of hormones across
the ovulatory/menstrual cycle,

03:45:46.130 --> 03:45:48.190
including regulating
levels of FSH

03:45:48.190 --> 03:45:50.320
so that they're not
too high nor too low

03:45:50.320 --> 03:45:53.230
and restricting the
FSH to the follicular

03:45:53.230 --> 03:45:58.630
phase of the menstrual cycle,
as well as using acupuncture

03:45:58.630 --> 03:46:00.790
to improve things
like blood flow

03:46:00.790 --> 03:46:02.620
and the health of
the ovary itself

03:46:02.620 --> 03:46:05.710
and other aspects of the
female reproductive axis.

03:46:05.710 --> 03:46:09.680
So acupuncture can operate at
the chemical level, impacting

03:46:09.680 --> 03:46:10.180
hormones.

03:46:10.180 --> 03:46:12.460
It can act at the
mechanical level,

03:46:12.460 --> 03:46:15.460
impacting the different tissues
through which the egg has

03:46:15.460 --> 03:46:17.050
to pass and so on and so forth.

03:46:17.050 --> 03:46:19.630
Likewise, on the male
side, acupuncture

03:46:19.630 --> 03:46:24.400
has been shown to improve
semen volume, quality of sperm,

03:46:24.400 --> 03:46:28.030
sperm motility, et
cetera, and in large part

03:46:28.030 --> 03:46:30.760
through changes in the
neural pathways that

03:46:30.760 --> 03:46:35.920
innervate the very tissues and
vascular input to the scrotum

03:46:35.920 --> 03:46:38.770
and testicles, because,
as we learned earlier,

03:46:38.770 --> 03:46:40.900
temperature regulation of
the scrotum and testicles

03:46:40.900 --> 03:46:43.510
is so vital for
getting healthy sperm

03:46:43.510 --> 03:46:45.410
and increasing sperm quality.

03:46:45.410 --> 03:46:48.340
In addition, there are good
data to support the idea

03:46:48.340 --> 03:46:51.708
that acupuncture can increase
levels of testosterone,

03:46:51.708 --> 03:46:53.750
free testosterone, and
the sorts of hormones that

03:46:53.750 --> 03:46:57.200
are going to support healthy
hormone production and sperm

03:46:57.200 --> 03:46:59.180
production in males.

03:46:59.180 --> 03:47:03.290
And this is distinct from
applying testosterone

03:47:03.290 --> 03:47:04.610
from an exogenous source.

03:47:04.610 --> 03:47:06.860
So when we're talking about
acupuncture and increasing

03:47:06.860 --> 03:47:09.402
levels of testosterone, we're
talking about increasing levels

03:47:09.402 --> 03:47:11.030
of endogenous testosterone.

03:47:11.030 --> 03:47:13.700
So those Leydig cells can
support the Sertoli cells,

03:47:13.700 --> 03:47:16.340
and the Sertoli cells can make
that androgen-binding protein,

03:47:16.340 --> 03:47:18.620
and you get enhanced
spermatogenesis.

03:47:18.620 --> 03:47:21.080
You can find evidence for all
of these different features,

03:47:21.080 --> 03:47:22.850
both changes to the
chemical milieu-- that

03:47:22.850 --> 03:47:25.340
is, the hormones-- and changes
to the mechanical milieu,

03:47:25.340 --> 03:47:28.640
including, for instance,
improvement of the pathways

03:47:28.640 --> 03:47:31.160
leading from the seminiferous
tubules to the epididymis

03:47:31.160 --> 03:47:33.950
to the vas deferens, basically
clearing out the plumbing so

03:47:33.950 --> 03:47:36.140
that more quality
ejaculate can be delivered,

03:47:36.140 --> 03:47:38.390
which, of course, is going
to increase the probability

03:47:38.390 --> 03:47:39.840
of fertilization.

03:47:39.840 --> 03:47:41.450
So when you hear
that acupuncture

03:47:41.450 --> 03:47:43.940
can improve the
likelihood of pregnancy,

03:47:43.940 --> 03:47:46.670
that's an accurate statement for
which there are now increasing

03:47:46.670 --> 03:47:48.620
amounts of mechanistic data.

03:47:48.620 --> 03:47:50.900
If you want to learn more
about how acupuncture

03:47:50.900 --> 03:47:53.840
can be used to contribute
to improved fertilization

03:47:53.840 --> 03:47:55.580
and pregnancy,
there are a number

03:47:55.580 --> 03:47:57.650
of different excellent
reviews on this,

03:47:57.650 --> 03:48:01.530
both as it relates to females
and as it relates to males.

03:48:01.530 --> 03:48:03.980
One of the best papers
that I happen to like

03:48:03.980 --> 03:48:05.527
is one that we'll
provide a link to

03:48:05.527 --> 03:48:07.610
in the references entitled
"Acupuncture and Herbal

03:48:07.610 --> 03:48:10.580
Medicine for Female Fertility,
An Overview of Systematic

03:48:10.580 --> 03:48:13.400
Review," so a review of reviews.

03:48:13.400 --> 03:48:16.242
This was published
recently in 2021.

03:48:16.242 --> 03:48:17.450
We'll provide a link to that.

03:48:17.450 --> 03:48:21.080
And there's also going to
be a link to a review that

03:48:21.080 --> 03:48:24.110
relates to acupuncture for
male fertility and hormone

03:48:24.110 --> 03:48:25.100
augmentation.

03:48:25.100 --> 03:48:27.350
I should just mention
briefly that if you're

03:48:27.350 --> 03:48:29.510
going to look at
scientific papers,

03:48:29.510 --> 03:48:31.280
one thing that you'll
want to consider

03:48:31.280 --> 03:48:33.748
is also looking at the
references that they reference.

03:48:33.748 --> 03:48:36.290
Now, of course, papers tend to
reference a ton of references,

03:48:36.290 --> 03:48:37.435
in particular in reviews.

03:48:37.435 --> 03:48:38.810
So what you'll
want to do is look

03:48:38.810 --> 03:48:40.700
for the references
that are showing up

03:48:40.700 --> 03:48:42.770
most often in the introduction.

03:48:42.770 --> 03:48:44.900
Those references
often are going to be

03:48:44.900 --> 03:48:48.170
the most prominent recent
reviews or the most important

03:48:48.170 --> 03:48:49.520
findings in recent years.

03:48:49.520 --> 03:48:51.960
That's not always the case,
but that's often the case.

03:48:51.960 --> 03:48:54.585
So if you read the first couple
of paragraphs of these papers--

03:48:54.585 --> 03:48:57.180
and these are openly available
as full text, by the way,

03:48:57.180 --> 03:48:58.610
online if you go
to these links--

03:48:58.610 --> 03:49:02.000
you'll be able to access the
best papers, the most relevant

03:49:02.000 --> 03:49:04.940
papers, in the context
of acupuncture supporting

03:49:04.940 --> 03:49:08.630
female and acupuncture
supporting male fertility

03:49:08.630 --> 03:49:09.680
and hormone status.

03:49:09.680 --> 03:49:12.740
Now, I'd like to discuss things
that both men and women can

03:49:12.740 --> 03:49:15.320
take in order to
maximize their fertility.

03:49:15.320 --> 03:49:19.560
And again and again, when
we're talking about fertility,

03:49:19.560 --> 03:49:22.260
we're talking about people
who want to conceive and have

03:49:22.260 --> 03:49:26.580
children, but also we're
talking about a basic measure

03:49:26.580 --> 03:49:28.060
of overall health status.

03:49:28.060 --> 03:49:30.960
So if you're somebody who does
not want to conceive children,

03:49:30.960 --> 03:49:33.570
I still encourage you to
think about whether or not

03:49:33.570 --> 03:49:35.040
you would want to
do certain things

03:49:35.040 --> 03:49:37.110
or not do certain
things in order

03:49:37.110 --> 03:49:41.280
to maximize your fertility as a
means to maximize your vitality

03:49:41.280 --> 03:49:42.840
and longevity,
because that's really

03:49:42.840 --> 03:49:46.050
what maximizing fertility is
about for a lot of people.

03:49:46.050 --> 03:49:47.610
That said, I know
a lot of people

03:49:47.610 --> 03:49:49.990
would like to conceive
children, perhaps not right away

03:49:49.990 --> 03:49:50.850
but in the future.

03:49:50.850 --> 03:49:52.500
And what I'm about
to describe are

03:49:52.500 --> 03:49:55.110
some tools and
interventions that is things

03:49:55.110 --> 03:50:00.090
that one can take in order to
improve their hormone status

03:50:00.090 --> 03:50:03.150
but also, in particular,
the quality of their eggs

03:50:03.150 --> 03:50:06.520
and the quality of their sperm
in the short and long term.

03:50:06.520 --> 03:50:09.360
The first on the list of things
that people can take in order

03:50:09.360 --> 03:50:13.260
to improve egg quality or
sperm quality is L-carnitine.

03:50:13.260 --> 03:50:15.630
L-carnitine is present
in various foods,

03:50:15.630 --> 03:50:17.310
in particular in red meats.

03:50:17.310 --> 03:50:19.320
But again, it's going
to be very hard to get

03:50:19.320 --> 03:50:21.900
sufficient levels of L-carnitine
to improve egg quality

03:50:21.900 --> 03:50:23.670
and sperm quality, the
unless you're going

03:50:23.670 --> 03:50:25.050
to take it in supplement form.

03:50:25.050 --> 03:50:28.290
The typical recommendation,
based on peer-reviewed studies

03:50:28.290 --> 03:50:30.840
that have shown significant
improvements in egg quality--

03:50:30.840 --> 03:50:33.090
that is chromosomal
arrangements,

03:50:33.090 --> 03:50:35.910
that is the likelihood of
fertility-- or pregnancy,

03:50:35.910 --> 03:50:36.450
rather--

03:50:36.450 --> 03:50:39.300
the likelihood of
sperm being forward

03:50:39.300 --> 03:50:41.550
fast swimmers as opposed
to twitchers or immotile

03:50:41.550 --> 03:50:43.710
and having proper morphology--
all those measures

03:50:43.710 --> 03:50:47.370
has been demonstrated to
be significantly improved

03:50:47.370 --> 03:50:48.870
by the ingestion of L-carnitine.

03:50:48.870 --> 03:50:50.040
How much L-carnitine?

03:50:50.040 --> 03:50:52.530
Well, that depends on how you're
obtaining the L-carnitine.

03:50:52.530 --> 03:50:56.010
If you're obtaining
it in capsule form,

03:50:56.010 --> 03:51:00.360
1 to 3 grams per day of
capsule form L-carnitine

03:51:00.360 --> 03:51:03.390
is what's been suggested to
improve egg quality and sperm

03:51:03.390 --> 03:51:04.050
quality.

03:51:04.050 --> 03:51:07.290
Now, 1 to 3 grams per day
can be taken all at once

03:51:07.290 --> 03:51:09.330
or spread out throughout
the 24-hour cycle.

03:51:09.330 --> 03:51:11.865
It can be taken with
or without food.

03:51:11.865 --> 03:51:13.780
It does not seem to matter.

03:51:13.780 --> 03:51:17.610
And when taken for a
period of 30 to 60 days,

03:51:17.610 --> 03:51:19.560
it does seem to
significantly improve

03:51:19.560 --> 03:51:21.930
all the parameters that
have been discussed for egg

03:51:21.930 --> 03:51:23.640
quality and sperm quality.

03:51:23.640 --> 03:51:26.160
Now, the mechanism for that
effect is pretty clear.

03:51:26.160 --> 03:51:31.530
L-carnitine is involved in the
processing of lipids, fats,

03:51:31.530 --> 03:51:34.210
in terms of
mitochondrial function.

03:51:34.210 --> 03:51:36.420
And as we talked about
before, mitochondria

03:51:36.420 --> 03:51:40.560
are vital for the organization
and action of the spindle that

03:51:40.560 --> 03:51:42.210
pulls apart the
chromosomes, taking

03:51:42.210 --> 03:51:46.260
that cell within the female
from diploid to haploid,

03:51:46.260 --> 03:51:47.370
which is essential.

03:51:47.370 --> 03:51:51.120
You really want just the 23
individual chromosomal strands.

03:51:51.120 --> 03:51:53.640
You don't want
chromosomal repeats.

03:51:53.640 --> 03:51:56.790
It's also involved in the
actual fusion of the egg

03:51:56.790 --> 03:52:01.022
as it exits the ovary and
enters the ovulation cycle.

03:52:01.022 --> 03:52:03.480
Mitochondria are also important,
as we talked about before,

03:52:03.480 --> 03:52:05.220
for the forward motility
of sperm because

03:52:05.220 --> 03:52:06.595
of the enrichment
of mitochondria

03:52:06.595 --> 03:52:08.280
in that mid region
just behind the head.

03:52:08.280 --> 03:52:10.620
They cause the
whipping flagellation

03:52:10.620 --> 03:52:12.930
of the tail, allowing
for forward movement,

03:52:12.930 --> 03:52:15.310
as well as other aspects
of cellular morphology.

03:52:15.310 --> 03:52:18.847
So it makes a lot of sense as to
why L-carnitine supplementation

03:52:18.847 --> 03:52:19.680
would be beneficial.

03:52:19.680 --> 03:52:22.760
Again, it's 1 to 3 grams per
day over a period of about 30

03:52:22.760 --> 03:52:23.453
to 60 months.

03:52:23.453 --> 03:52:25.620
If you're hoping to conceive
in the upcoming months,

03:52:25.620 --> 03:52:29.310
recommend taking it for at
least 30 days prior to that.

03:52:29.310 --> 03:52:32.100
Of course, based on the data
we talked about before--

03:52:32.100 --> 03:52:34.080
cumulative probability,
fecundability,

03:52:34.080 --> 03:52:35.730
et cetera-- there's
no reason to not

03:52:35.730 --> 03:52:37.740
continue to try for
pregnancy before taking

03:52:37.740 --> 03:52:41.070
L-carnitine, but L-carnitine is
going to improve egg and sperm

03:52:41.070 --> 03:52:41.640
quality.

03:52:41.640 --> 03:52:45.660
And so you might actually
take the stance that,

03:52:45.660 --> 03:52:48.420
even if you don't have any
problem getting pregnant,

03:52:48.420 --> 03:52:50.940
wouldn't you want to
maximize the quality

03:52:50.940 --> 03:52:53.730
of the egg that gets fertilized
and the quality of the sperm

03:52:53.730 --> 03:52:55.270
that fertilizes that egg?

03:52:55.270 --> 03:52:58.290
So that's additional rationale
for taking L-carnitine.

03:52:58.290 --> 03:53:00.450
One important note--
if you are going

03:53:00.450 --> 03:53:03.660
to take L-carnitine in
oral form, in capsule form,

03:53:03.660 --> 03:53:06.030
it can increase
something called TMAO.

03:53:06.030 --> 03:53:08.430
TMAO can cause stiffening
of the arteries.

03:53:08.430 --> 03:53:10.800
You don't want TMAO
levels to go too high.

03:53:10.800 --> 03:53:13.680
One way to offset the
increases in TMAO caused

03:53:13.680 --> 03:53:16.950
by oral L-carnitine is
to take 600 milligrams

03:53:16.950 --> 03:53:18.602
of garlic per day.

03:53:18.602 --> 03:53:20.310
I suppose you could
eat cloves of garlic.

03:53:20.310 --> 03:53:22.260
That would work just as
well because garlic contains

03:53:22.260 --> 03:53:23.820
something called
allicin, which can

03:53:23.820 --> 03:53:26.010
offset the increase in TMAO.

03:53:26.010 --> 03:53:29.550
But 600 milligram capsules
of garlic are going to be--

03:53:29.550 --> 03:53:31.780
or garlic extract, rather--

03:53:31.780 --> 03:53:36.300
is going to be the most probably
cost effective and simplest way

03:53:36.300 --> 03:53:37.170
to do this.

03:53:37.170 --> 03:53:39.388
And also, they are going to
create that garlic smell.

03:53:39.388 --> 03:53:40.930
Some people like
the smell of garlic.

03:53:40.930 --> 03:53:41.680
Some people don't.

03:53:41.680 --> 03:53:43.620
So if you're going to
take oral L-carnitine,

03:53:43.620 --> 03:53:45.720
I suggest also
taking 600 milligrams

03:53:45.720 --> 03:53:47.985
a day of garlic extract.

03:53:47.985 --> 03:53:50.110
And you can do that at any
time throughout the day.

03:53:50.110 --> 03:53:52.442
It doesn't have to be
with the L-carnitine.

03:53:52.442 --> 03:53:54.900
The next item on the list of
compounds that have been shown

03:53:54.900 --> 03:53:57.030
to improve egg quality
and sperm quality--

03:53:57.030 --> 03:53:58.980
and quite robustly so--

03:53:58.980 --> 03:54:00.600
is coenzyme Q10.

03:54:00.600 --> 03:54:03.450
Coenzyme Q10 is something
that you can actually measure

03:54:03.450 --> 03:54:05.183
levels of in your blood.

03:54:05.183 --> 03:54:06.600
Most physicians
will say that they

03:54:06.600 --> 03:54:08.400
want to see your
levels of coenzyme Q10

03:54:08.400 --> 03:54:10.673
to be somewhere
between 0.5 and 2.5.

03:54:10.673 --> 03:54:12.090
It's going to
depend on the units.

03:54:12.090 --> 03:54:13.632
Most people, I
realize, are not going

03:54:13.632 --> 03:54:15.750
to run off and get
their CoQ10 measured.

03:54:15.750 --> 03:54:17.820
It's not included in most
standard blood tests.

03:54:17.820 --> 03:54:19.500
But if you were to
measure your CoQ10,

03:54:19.500 --> 03:54:21.630
that's the range that
you want to look for.

03:54:21.630 --> 03:54:25.080
That said, many people opt
to supplement with CoQ10.

03:54:25.080 --> 03:54:28.560
And you'll find that many
fertility docs, OB/GYNs,

03:54:28.560 --> 03:54:31.080
and urologists that are trying
to assist their male patients

03:54:31.080 --> 03:54:32.700
with fertility
will suggest CoQ10

03:54:32.700 --> 03:54:36.180
because, again, it supports
the health of mitochondria.

03:54:36.180 --> 03:54:40.530
Mitochondria are so vital to so
many aspects of the formation

03:54:40.530 --> 03:54:45.270
and fertilization of
the egg and sperm that,

03:54:45.270 --> 03:54:47.580
of course, fertilizes the egg.

03:54:47.580 --> 03:54:51.000
The coenzyme Q10 dosages
that are most often suggested

03:54:51.000 --> 03:54:54.150
and that you'll observe in
the peer-reviewed research

03:54:54.150 --> 03:54:56.130
literature-- on
humans, I should add--

03:54:56.130 --> 03:54:59.550
is 100 to 400
milligrams per day.

03:54:59.550 --> 03:55:02.490
And the coenzyme Q10
is taken generally

03:55:02.490 --> 03:55:05.610
with a meal and ideally
a meal that contains fat.

03:55:05.610 --> 03:55:08.820
And there's even some idea
that taking coenzyme Q10

03:55:08.820 --> 03:55:12.773
with your dinner, assuming that
dinner includes some fat-- you

03:55:12.773 --> 03:55:14.190
don't have to add
additional fat--

03:55:14.190 --> 03:55:17.850
is going to be more advantageous
than taking coenzyme Q10 early

03:55:17.850 --> 03:55:19.350
in the day, although
that's probably

03:55:19.350 --> 03:55:21.808
a detail that's getting a little
too far down in the weeds.

03:55:21.808 --> 03:55:24.900
So again, 100 to 400 milligrams
of coenzyme Q10 per day,

03:55:24.900 --> 03:55:26.610
whether or not you're
a man or a woman,

03:55:26.610 --> 03:55:29.310
for improving the
likelihood of fertility

03:55:29.310 --> 03:55:31.560
by way of improving
egg and sperm quality.

03:55:31.560 --> 03:55:33.685
And again, if you're somebody
who just doesn't have

03:55:33.685 --> 03:55:36.330
any problem getting pregnant
or if you're already producing

03:55:36.330 --> 03:55:38.467
many sperm of
quality morphology,

03:55:38.467 --> 03:55:40.800
this is another case in which
you could take a step back

03:55:40.800 --> 03:55:43.260
and say, well, why wouldn't
I want to further optimize

03:55:43.260 --> 03:55:44.550
the quality of the
egg and the sperm,

03:55:44.550 --> 03:55:45.960
because the quality of
the egg and the sperm

03:55:45.960 --> 03:55:47.640
ultimately are
going to determine

03:55:47.640 --> 03:55:49.950
not just whether or not you
have a successful pregnancy

03:55:49.950 --> 03:55:54.220
but are going to determine,
admittedly in ways that will

03:55:54.220 --> 03:55:56.620
forever remain cryptic
to you-- but nonetheless

03:55:56.620 --> 03:55:58.540
are going to be
important in determining

03:55:58.540 --> 03:56:01.210
the qualities of the
brain tissue and body

03:56:01.210 --> 03:56:02.710
tissue of your offspring.

03:56:02.710 --> 03:56:05.500
The third item on the list of
compounds which are commonly

03:56:05.500 --> 03:56:09.700
suggested or prescribed
by fertility docs

03:56:09.700 --> 03:56:11.230
nowadays for men
and women wishing

03:56:11.230 --> 03:56:13.480
to conceive and/or
optimize their fertility

03:56:13.480 --> 03:56:17.740
as a basis for general vitality
and health is inositol.

03:56:17.740 --> 03:56:19.850
Now, inositol has many uses.

03:56:19.850 --> 03:56:21.520
So you'll hear about
the use of inositol

03:56:21.520 --> 03:56:23.663
for reducing anxiety
or improving mood

03:56:23.663 --> 03:56:25.330
or even for the
treatment of depression.

03:56:25.330 --> 03:56:27.370
We talked about inositol
in previous episodes

03:56:27.370 --> 03:56:28.810
of this podcast.

03:56:28.810 --> 03:56:31.510
For instance, I
talked about inositol

03:56:31.510 --> 03:56:35.290
and in particular taking 900
milligrams of myo-inositol

03:56:35.290 --> 03:56:37.480
prior to sleep, which
is something that I do,

03:56:37.480 --> 03:56:40.330
along with the other supplements
that I take and recommend

03:56:40.330 --> 03:56:44.313
for sleep, such as magnesium 3
and 8, apigenin, and theanine.

03:56:44.313 --> 03:56:45.730
If you're curious
about those, you

03:56:45.730 --> 03:56:48.160
can see our newsletter on sleep
or our "Perfect Your Sleep"

03:56:48.160 --> 03:56:49.750
episode or the "Master
Your Sleep" episode.

03:56:49.750 --> 03:56:52.125
It talks about behavioral and
supplementation-based tools

03:56:52.125 --> 03:56:53.110
for improving sleep.

03:56:53.110 --> 03:56:58.210
But myo-inositol is not just
suggested for or prescribed

03:56:58.210 --> 03:57:01.210
for people that are
wishing to get pregnant

03:57:01.210 --> 03:57:02.590
and for general health.

03:57:02.590 --> 03:57:05.320
But myo-inositol is
often recommended

03:57:05.320 --> 03:57:09.490
for people that want to improve
egg and sperm quality because

03:57:09.490 --> 03:57:10.990
of the way that
it can positively

03:57:10.990 --> 03:57:12.850
impact insulin sensitivity.

03:57:12.850 --> 03:57:16.000
Insulin sensitivity might sound
like a bad thing to people

03:57:16.000 --> 03:57:16.580
out there.

03:57:16.580 --> 03:57:19.840
But it turns out that you
want to be insulin sensitive.

03:57:19.840 --> 03:57:22.480
The last thing you want is
to be insulin insensitive.

03:57:22.480 --> 03:57:24.550
Insulin insensitivity is
associated with type 2

03:57:24.550 --> 03:57:26.830
diabetes, with obesity,
and even for people

03:57:26.830 --> 03:57:29.530
who are not challenged
with obesity,

03:57:29.530 --> 03:57:31.867
you want your cells to
be insulin sensitive.

03:57:31.867 --> 03:57:34.450
You don't want a lot of insulin
floating around in your system

03:57:34.450 --> 03:57:37.870
with your cells unable
to use that insulin.

03:57:37.870 --> 03:57:40.150
That's really what insulin
insensitivity is about.

03:57:40.150 --> 03:57:45.342
Myo-inositol, at dosages
of 1 to 5 grams per day--

03:57:45.342 --> 03:57:47.050
that's pretty high,
1 to 5 grams per day,

03:57:47.050 --> 03:57:50.200
keeping in mind that 1,000
milligrams is 1 gram--

03:57:50.200 --> 03:57:53.830
has been suggested to improve
egg quality and sperm quality.

03:57:53.830 --> 03:57:55.630
Now, one point of--

03:57:55.630 --> 03:57:57.220
I wouldn't say
caution-- but of note

03:57:57.220 --> 03:57:59.927
is that myo-inositol
can reduce anxiety,

03:57:59.927 --> 03:58:01.510
and it can be a
slight sedative, which

03:58:01.510 --> 03:58:05.500
is why some folks, including
myself, take almost a gram, 900

03:58:05.500 --> 03:58:07.690
milligrams, prior to sleep.

03:58:07.690 --> 03:58:10.840
If you're going to take
5 grams of myo-inositol,

03:58:10.840 --> 03:58:13.315
you would want to restrict
that to the late evening

03:58:13.315 --> 03:58:14.440
or second half of your day.

03:58:14.440 --> 03:58:16.065
And I don't suggest
starting that high.

03:58:16.065 --> 03:58:17.950
I would start with 1
or 2 grams and then

03:58:17.950 --> 03:58:19.450
working your way
up, seeing what you

03:58:19.450 --> 03:58:23.500
can tolerate in terms of
the level of anti-anxiety

03:58:23.500 --> 03:58:26.260
and drowsiness that it produces.

03:58:26.260 --> 03:58:28.750
1 to 5 grams per
day of myo-inositol

03:58:28.750 --> 03:58:32.890
is what's suggested for both
men and women wishing to improve

03:58:32.890 --> 03:58:34.180
egg health and sperm health.

03:58:34.180 --> 03:58:39.040
But for women, it's also often
suggested to include also--

03:58:39.040 --> 03:58:43.600
so to take myo-inositol, but
to also take D-chiro inositol.

03:58:43.600 --> 03:58:46.690
D-chiro inositol
has elements in it

03:58:46.690 --> 03:58:50.110
that can be both pro
and anti-androgenic.

03:58:50.110 --> 03:58:52.420
Androgens are things like
testosterone and related

03:58:52.420 --> 03:58:53.440
molecules.

03:58:53.440 --> 03:58:56.350
There are a number of
different causes of infertility

03:58:56.350 --> 03:58:59.440
and disruption to egg
quality, age being the most

03:58:59.440 --> 03:59:00.550
significant factor.

03:59:00.550 --> 03:59:03.130
But another significant
and very common

03:59:03.130 --> 03:59:06.730
factor, even among young
women who are of fertile age,

03:59:06.730 --> 03:59:10.360
is having too many androgens
and as it relates to something

03:59:10.360 --> 03:59:12.370
called polycystic
ovarian syndrome.

03:59:12.370 --> 03:59:14.775
We'll do an entire episode
about menopause and PCOS

03:59:14.775 --> 03:59:16.150
and a number of
other things that

03:59:16.150 --> 03:59:19.780
relate to fertility because
it's an entire and very

03:59:19.780 --> 03:59:22.190
interesting other discussion
that we need to have.

03:59:22.190 --> 03:59:23.710
But the recommendation
is that women

03:59:23.710 --> 03:59:26.260
take 1 to 5 grams
of myo-inositol

03:59:26.260 --> 03:59:30.160
but also D-chiro inositol
because of the ways

03:59:30.160 --> 03:59:33.070
that it can balance
androgens and offset some

03:59:33.070 --> 03:59:36.310
of the negative effects of
polycystic ovarian syndrome

03:59:36.310 --> 03:59:38.920
or even for women who do
not have polycystic ovarian

03:59:38.920 --> 03:59:41.830
syndrome because of the ways
that D-chiro inositol can

03:59:41.830 --> 03:59:44.710
balance androgens in
ways that are beneficial.

03:59:44.710 --> 03:59:48.550
The dosages of D-chiro
inositol that are recommended

03:59:48.550 --> 03:59:53.010
tend to be 1/25 to 1/40
of the myo-inositol dose.

03:59:53.010 --> 03:59:54.760
So you'll have to get
out your calculator.

03:59:54.760 --> 03:59:56.950
Remember, 1,000
milligrams equals 1 gram.

03:59:56.950 --> 03:59:59.740
So figure out, if you're
taking 1 gram of myo-inositol

03:59:59.740 --> 04:00:02.110
per day or 2 grams,
you're going to want

04:00:02.110 --> 04:00:03.760
to convert that to milligrams.

04:00:03.760 --> 04:00:07.180
So let's say you're taking 2
grams of myo-inositol per day.

04:00:07.180 --> 04:00:08.380
That's 2,000 milligrams.

04:00:08.380 --> 04:00:10.750
Then you'd want to
divide that by 25.

04:00:10.750 --> 04:00:13.960
And that's how many
milligrams of D-chiro inositol

04:00:13.960 --> 04:00:15.590
you would want to take, as well.

04:00:15.590 --> 04:00:18.730
Or you could go with the lower
end dose and divide it by 40

04:00:18.730 --> 04:00:23.080
and take that number of
milligrams of D-chiro inositol

04:00:23.080 --> 04:00:24.310
along with the inositol.

04:00:24.310 --> 04:00:27.160
Again, probably taking it later
in the day is going to be good.

04:00:27.160 --> 04:00:29.373
And it's not clear
at all that taking it

04:00:29.373 --> 04:00:31.790
with food or without food makes
any difference whatsoever.

04:00:31.790 --> 04:00:33.670
So I would suggest
you do either.

04:00:33.670 --> 04:00:36.260
Keep in mind, as I'm discussing
these recommendations,

04:00:36.260 --> 04:00:37.510
I may call them prescriptions.

04:00:37.510 --> 04:00:39.218
But none of these are
prescription drugs.

04:00:39.218 --> 04:00:41.740
And of course, you should
always discuss any supplements

04:00:41.740 --> 04:00:44.800
that you're planning to take or
stop taking, for that matter,

04:00:44.800 --> 04:00:45.670
with your physician.

04:00:45.670 --> 04:00:46.962
I don't say that to protect me.

04:00:46.962 --> 04:00:48.107
I say that to protect you.

04:00:48.107 --> 04:00:49.690
Any time you're going
to add or change

04:00:49.690 --> 04:00:51.398
something in your
overall health regimen,

04:00:51.398 --> 04:00:54.200
you want to discuss that
with your trusted health care

04:00:54.200 --> 04:00:57.500
professional, typically, I would
hope, a board-certified MD.

04:00:57.500 --> 04:01:01.550
The fourth item in the list of
commonly suggested supplements

04:01:01.550 --> 04:01:05.360
for men and women wishing to
optimize egg and sperm quality,

04:01:05.360 --> 04:01:08.477
respectively, is
omega-3 fatty acids.

04:01:08.477 --> 04:01:10.310
And now, here, we're
talking about something

04:01:10.310 --> 04:01:12.935
that could be obtained from food
and can be obtained from food.

04:01:12.935 --> 04:01:15.890
So if you're consuming
fatty ocean fish, things

04:01:15.890 --> 04:01:19.190
like sardines, anchovies,
salmon with the skin,

04:01:19.190 --> 04:01:22.610
chances are you're going to
get some quality omega-3s.

04:01:22.610 --> 04:01:25.650
Omega-3s are also available
in plant-based sources.

04:01:25.650 --> 04:01:27.980
It's also available in
krill, for that matter.

04:01:27.980 --> 04:01:29.930
But most people find
it difficult to reach

04:01:29.930 --> 04:01:33.200
the threshold required
for optimizing

04:01:33.200 --> 04:01:34.610
mental health and
physical health

04:01:34.610 --> 04:01:37.830
that is the threshold of the
EPA essential fatty acids.

04:01:37.830 --> 04:01:40.070
And so for that
matter, I've suggested

04:01:40.070 --> 04:01:41.270
before on this podcast--

04:01:41.270 --> 04:01:43.310
and many fertility
docs will suggest--

04:01:43.310 --> 04:01:48.220
that their patients take omega-3
fatty acids in supplement form.

04:01:48.220 --> 04:01:50.560
It could be taken in liquid
form or in capsule form,

04:01:50.560 --> 04:01:53.950
but enough of those that you're
getting at least 1 gram per day

04:01:53.950 --> 04:01:57.820
of the EPA form of omega-3,
so at least 1 gram per day

04:01:57.820 --> 04:02:01.625
and as high as 2 or even 3
grams per day of the EPA form.

04:02:01.625 --> 04:02:03.250
So you'll need to
look at the packaging

04:02:03.250 --> 04:02:05.860
because oftentimes it'll
say high potency omega-3.

04:02:05.860 --> 04:02:10.060
It'll say 1,500
milligrams of omega-3s.

04:02:10.060 --> 04:02:13.028
But that's not 1,500
milligrams of the EPA form.

04:02:13.028 --> 04:02:15.070
You look on the back of
the label, and it'll say,

04:02:15.070 --> 04:02:18.880
each serving contains
750 milligrams of EPA.

04:02:18.880 --> 04:02:22.120
You want to get above
that 1 gram dosage per day

04:02:22.120 --> 04:02:25.060
and as high as 3 grams
per day of the EPAs.

04:02:25.060 --> 04:02:26.470
The most cost-effective
way to do

04:02:26.470 --> 04:02:28.652
that is going to be
liquid-form omegas,

04:02:28.652 --> 04:02:30.860
but that's a little bit
inconvenient for many people,

04:02:30.860 --> 04:02:32.402
and some people
don't like the taste.

04:02:32.402 --> 04:02:34.660
That's why they rely on
the capsule-form omegas.

04:02:34.660 --> 04:02:36.310
And of course,
there are compounds

04:02:36.310 --> 04:02:38.920
that can impact
fertility status, quality

04:02:38.920 --> 04:02:42.550
of eggs, quality of sperm,
not by adjusting mitochondria

04:02:42.550 --> 04:02:45.010
or insulin sensitivity
or creating

04:02:45.010 --> 04:02:48.460
a general milieu of support
for the egg and the sperm

04:02:48.460 --> 04:02:52.600
production and function, such
as the compounds that I just

04:02:52.600 --> 04:02:56.280
listed off do, but
rather compounds

04:02:56.280 --> 04:02:58.170
that influence the
hormones involved

04:02:58.170 --> 04:03:00.720
in the generation of sperm and
the generation of the eggs,

04:03:00.720 --> 04:03:04.020
involved in the ovulatory cycle
and the spermatogenesis cycle,

04:03:04.020 --> 04:03:04.740
that is.

04:03:04.740 --> 04:03:07.570
Now, these are going to
come in different forms.

04:03:07.570 --> 04:03:10.830
And I want to just emphasize
that the supplements that

04:03:10.830 --> 04:03:12.900
do this, that adjust
hormones in these ways that

04:03:12.900 --> 04:03:16.350
can be beneficial, are
distinct from hormone therapy

04:03:16.350 --> 04:03:19.733
or bioidentical hormones,
distinct from hormone therapy

04:03:19.733 --> 04:03:21.150
or bioidentical
hormones, because,

04:03:21.150 --> 04:03:23.880
as we discussed
earlier, when you take

04:03:23.880 --> 04:03:26.590
a hormone like testosterone or
even estrogen, for that matter,

04:03:26.590 --> 04:03:28.380
from an exogenous,
an outside source,

04:03:28.380 --> 04:03:30.797
you're going to disrupt
the feedback pathways

04:03:30.797 --> 04:03:32.880
inside of your body, and
you're going to shut down

04:03:32.880 --> 04:03:34.650
your own endogenous production.

04:03:34.650 --> 04:03:38.310
The supplements I'm about
to describe do not do that

04:03:38.310 --> 04:03:41.700
and yet can adjust levels of
hormones in more subtle ways

04:03:41.700 --> 04:03:46.290
that can be beneficial for the
process of maximizing fertility

04:03:46.290 --> 04:03:47.850
for males and for females.

04:03:47.850 --> 04:03:50.305
The first of which on this
list that I'd like to discuss

04:03:50.305 --> 04:03:51.930
has been discussed
in previous podcasts

04:03:51.930 --> 04:03:54.630
as well, which is a
substance called tongkat ali.

04:03:54.630 --> 04:03:57.420
Tongkat ali also
goes by other names.

04:03:57.420 --> 04:04:00.030
But when taken at 400
milligrams per day,

04:04:00.030 --> 04:04:01.590
sometimes separated
into two dosages

04:04:01.590 --> 04:04:04.920
but typically taken as
once a day early in the day

04:04:04.920 --> 04:04:08.280
because they can be a little
bit stimulating, although not

04:04:08.280 --> 04:04:09.120
anxiety provoking--

04:04:09.120 --> 04:04:10.362
I've never heard of that.

04:04:10.362 --> 04:04:11.820
It can be a little
bit stimulating.

04:04:11.820 --> 04:04:13.710
But 400 milligrams
a day of tongkat ali

04:04:13.710 --> 04:04:16.608
has been shown to
increase free testosterone

04:04:16.608 --> 04:04:18.900
by way of reducing something
called sex hormone binding

04:04:18.900 --> 04:04:19.400
globulin.

04:04:19.400 --> 04:04:21.900
It's also been shown to
increase luteinizing hormone,

04:04:21.900 --> 04:04:24.570
the net effect of which
has been described

04:04:24.570 --> 04:04:28.650
as a subtle but significant
increase in libido

04:04:28.650 --> 04:04:31.860
and some of the other parameters
associated with increased

04:04:31.860 --> 04:04:33.840
androgens, like free
testosterone in males

04:04:33.840 --> 04:04:34.350
and females.

04:04:34.350 --> 04:04:36.600
So a number of people out
there are taking tongkat ali

04:04:36.600 --> 04:04:37.142
in this way--

04:04:37.142 --> 04:04:38.610
400 milligrams per
day, restricted

04:04:38.610 --> 04:04:42.450
to the early part of the
day, with or without food.

04:04:42.450 --> 04:04:44.880
People always ask, do you
need to cycle tongkat ali?

04:04:44.880 --> 04:04:47.070
I'm not aware of any need
to cycle tongkat ali.

04:04:47.070 --> 04:04:48.750
In fact, it tends
to work better,

04:04:48.750 --> 04:04:52.110
meaning the effects on libido
and some other hormone profiles

04:04:52.110 --> 04:04:53.820
tend to increase over time.

04:04:53.820 --> 04:04:56.310
Again, tongkat ali is an option.

04:04:56.310 --> 04:04:58.440
Certainly, none of these
things are requirements.

04:04:58.440 --> 04:04:59.970
We're simply
listing off options.

04:04:59.970 --> 04:05:02.220
But many people, both
males and females,

04:05:02.220 --> 04:05:05.340
seem to benefit from
and like tongkat ali,

04:05:05.340 --> 04:05:07.530
even if they're not
seeking to conceive.

04:05:07.530 --> 04:05:09.900
There's no reason to think
that tongkat ali directly

04:05:09.900 --> 04:05:11.490
improves sperm quality.

04:05:11.490 --> 04:05:15.120
Except in males, the increase in
androgen created by tongkat ali

04:05:15.120 --> 04:05:18.930
supplementation can indeed lead
to improved spermatogenesis.

04:05:18.930 --> 04:05:21.627
So there's a growing amount
of data in the research

04:05:21.627 --> 04:05:22.710
literature on tongkat ali.

04:05:22.710 --> 04:05:24.340
Many people find it beneficial.

04:05:24.340 --> 04:05:26.610
And so it's something that
both men and women wishing

04:05:26.610 --> 04:05:29.010
to conceive and/or optimize
their fertility just

04:05:29.010 --> 04:05:31.860
as a general health parameter
might want to explore.

04:05:31.860 --> 04:05:35.640
The other supplement that's
been shown to improve both egg

04:05:35.640 --> 04:05:38.460
quality and sperm quality--

04:05:38.460 --> 04:05:39.937
and there I'm
referring to a number

04:05:39.937 --> 04:05:42.270
of different parameters related
to egg quality and sperm

04:05:42.270 --> 04:05:42.900
quality--

04:05:42.900 --> 04:05:46.920
as well as to increase
libido fairly substantially

04:05:46.920 --> 04:05:48.870
is a substance called Shilajit.

04:05:48.870 --> 04:05:53.550
Shilajit, spelled
S-H-I-L-A-G-I-T--

04:05:53.550 --> 04:05:57.180
Shilajit is actually
a compound that's

04:05:57.180 --> 04:05:59.040
used in ayurvedic
medicine, but there

04:05:59.040 --> 04:06:01.500
are some really good
research studies exploring

04:06:01.500 --> 04:06:05.340
the supplementation with
Shilajit at about 250

04:06:05.340 --> 04:06:07.120
milligrams twice per day.

04:06:07.120 --> 04:06:09.660
And this has been looked
at in males and in females.

04:06:09.660 --> 04:06:11.970
And it does seem to
significantly increase

04:06:11.970 --> 04:06:12.930
two hormones.

04:06:12.930 --> 04:06:15.120
One is testosterone,
and the other

04:06:15.120 --> 04:06:17.430
is follicle-stimulating hormone.

04:06:17.430 --> 04:06:21.060
And for that reason, Shilajit
is often considered a tonic

04:06:21.060 --> 04:06:25.530
that people use both as an
aphrodisiac to increase libido

04:06:25.530 --> 04:06:28.080
as well as to
increase fertility.

04:06:28.080 --> 04:06:30.990
Now, one note of caution,
if you're a woman

04:06:30.990 --> 04:06:32.983
and you're considering
taking Shilajit in order

04:06:32.983 --> 04:06:35.400
to increase testosterone and
follicle-stimulating hormone,

04:06:35.400 --> 04:06:37.080
keep in mind that
the ovulatory cycle

04:06:37.080 --> 04:06:41.280
is this very tightly
regulated cycle in which you

04:06:41.280 --> 04:06:45.300
want low but elevated levels
of follicle-stimulating hormone

04:06:45.300 --> 04:06:47.010
early in the
follicular phase, then

04:06:47.010 --> 04:06:50.087
it peaks right before
ovulation, and then low levels

04:06:50.087 --> 04:06:52.170
of follicle-stimulating
hormone in the second half

04:06:52.170 --> 04:06:52.770
of your cycle.

04:06:52.770 --> 04:06:55.800
For that reason, using
Shilajit chronically

04:06:55.800 --> 04:06:58.740
around the entire course
of your ovulatory cycle

04:06:58.740 --> 04:07:00.240
could be a little
bit risky, and I'd

04:07:00.240 --> 04:07:04.380
recommend that you talk to
your OB/GYN prior to doing that

04:07:04.380 --> 04:07:06.720
or if doing that at all.

04:07:06.720 --> 04:07:08.670
For males, it's a little
bit less of an issue,

04:07:08.670 --> 04:07:10.878
because, as I mentioned
earlier, sperm are constantly

04:07:10.878 --> 04:07:13.830
being generated, and
the presence of FSH

04:07:13.830 --> 04:07:16.320
is going to increase
spermatogenesis.

04:07:16.320 --> 04:07:19.230
Now, Shilajit is not FSH itself.

04:07:19.230 --> 04:07:22.260
Shilajit stimulates
the release of FSH.

04:07:22.260 --> 04:07:24.240
And it stimulates the
release of testosterone.

04:07:24.240 --> 04:07:25.740
So again, there's
no reason to think

04:07:25.740 --> 04:07:28.560
that it would shut down your
endogenous testosterone or FSH

04:07:28.560 --> 04:07:29.910
production.

04:07:29.910 --> 04:07:32.400
Although there are limited
amount of data that really

04:07:32.400 --> 04:07:33.780
explore that in detail.

04:07:33.780 --> 04:07:36.570
Many people use
Shilajit in order

04:07:36.570 --> 04:07:38.820
to increase their
testosterone, FSH,

04:07:38.820 --> 04:07:43.950
their libido, and various
aspects of sperm health.

04:07:43.950 --> 04:07:46.830
Again, the dosages of Shilajit
are about 250 milligrams,

04:07:46.830 --> 04:07:47.670
two times per day.

04:07:47.670 --> 04:07:49.140
One issue with
Shilajit is it often

04:07:49.140 --> 04:07:52.110
comes as a tar, which is a
little hard to measure out

04:07:52.110 --> 04:07:52.860
the dosages.

04:07:52.860 --> 04:07:53.940
Yes, a tar.

04:07:53.940 --> 04:07:56.040
It's this kind of
thick, gummy substance

04:07:56.040 --> 04:07:57.790
that you're supposed
to dissolve in water.

04:07:57.790 --> 04:07:59.873
And the recommendations
are you take a little bead

04:07:59.873 --> 04:08:01.040
and dissolve it in water.

04:08:01.040 --> 04:08:02.710
It is available in
capsule form where

04:08:02.710 --> 04:08:05.560
the ability to
control the dosage

04:08:05.560 --> 04:08:06.950
is made a little bit easier.

04:08:06.950 --> 04:08:08.650
But of course, as
with any supplement,

04:08:08.650 --> 04:08:11.080
I recommend starting with
the lowest possible dosage.

04:08:11.080 --> 04:08:14.800
So you might want to start with
a very small bead of Shilajit

04:08:14.800 --> 04:08:16.790
dissolved in water,
taken once per day,

04:08:16.790 --> 04:08:18.850
and then increase
the dosage as needed

04:08:18.850 --> 04:08:21.400
in order to obtain the
effects that you want.

04:08:21.400 --> 04:08:23.500
Things like Shilajit
start to bring us

04:08:23.500 --> 04:08:25.330
into the realm of
what can only be

04:08:25.330 --> 04:08:27.100
described as a little
bit unwieldy, right?

04:08:27.100 --> 04:08:28.990
Here we're saying you can't
really control the dosage.

04:08:28.990 --> 04:08:30.365
Now you're talking
about hormones

04:08:30.365 --> 04:08:32.770
that need to be tightly
regulated, at least for females

04:08:32.770 --> 04:08:33.910
across the ovarian cycle.

04:08:33.910 --> 04:08:35.590
For males, yes,
it has been shown

04:08:35.590 --> 04:08:37.720
to increase
testosterone and FSH,

04:08:37.720 --> 04:08:41.650
improve sperm motility and sperm
count pretty significantly.

04:08:41.650 --> 04:08:43.990
No reason to think that you
couldn't do that chronically

04:08:43.990 --> 04:08:44.650
with Shilajit.

04:08:44.650 --> 04:08:47.440
And yet, I do want to
acknowledge that Shilajit,

04:08:47.440 --> 04:08:49.990
as this black tar
substance, contains

04:08:49.990 --> 04:08:51.200
a lot of different things.

04:08:51.200 --> 04:08:53.140
In fact, it comes
from a mineral pitch.

04:08:53.140 --> 04:08:53.760
What is that?

04:08:53.760 --> 04:08:56.200
It comes from literally
the dirt and plants

04:08:56.200 --> 04:08:58.560
that have been compressed
by rocks in the Himalayas.

04:08:58.560 --> 04:09:00.622
So that's pretty esoteric
stuff when it really

04:09:00.622 --> 04:09:01.330
comes down to it.

04:09:01.330 --> 04:09:03.700
But the biological
effects of Shilajit,

04:09:03.700 --> 04:09:06.490
in both males and females,
seem to be related to the fact

04:09:06.490 --> 04:09:09.460
that it is highly enriched in
something called folic acid,

04:09:09.460 --> 04:09:11.170
and folic acid is
involved in a lot

04:09:11.170 --> 04:09:13.780
of different cellular processes,
not the least of which,

04:09:13.780 --> 04:09:17.920
at least in this context, is
the transport of molecules

04:09:17.920 --> 04:09:19.337
across cell membranes.

04:09:19.337 --> 04:09:20.920
And for hormones to
have their effect,

04:09:20.920 --> 04:09:22.920
they need to cross cell
membranes on the outside

04:09:22.920 --> 04:09:24.588
and the inside of the cell.

04:09:24.588 --> 04:09:26.380
So maybe that's how
it's having its effect.

04:09:26.380 --> 04:09:29.920
Again, the mechanisms of
exactly how Shilajit increases

04:09:29.920 --> 04:09:33.310
testosterone and FSH and
thereby libido, egg quality,

04:09:33.310 --> 04:09:35.320
and sperm quality
aren't entirely clear.

04:09:35.320 --> 04:09:38.068
But for the more
adventurous of you out there

04:09:38.068 --> 04:09:39.610
who want to experiment
with Shilajit,

04:09:39.610 --> 04:09:42.430
whether or not you're
trying to conceive or not,

04:09:42.430 --> 04:09:43.870
it might be something
to consider.

04:09:43.870 --> 04:09:45.700
But of course, do talk
to your physician.

04:09:45.700 --> 04:09:48.910
The next compound that I
want to discuss is zinc.

04:09:48.910 --> 04:09:51.310
And this discussion
mainly pertains to males,

04:09:51.310 --> 04:09:53.260
although I, of course,
should point out

04:09:53.260 --> 04:09:56.740
that females should get the
recommended daily allowance

04:09:56.740 --> 04:09:58.000
of zinc each day.

04:09:58.000 --> 04:10:00.580
Males, on the other
hand, seem to benefit

04:10:00.580 --> 04:10:04.163
from having additionally
high levels of zinc intake.

04:10:04.163 --> 04:10:05.830
Now, that can be
obtained through foods.

04:10:05.830 --> 04:10:08.620
You often hear, oh, oysters
are enriched in zinc,

04:10:08.620 --> 04:10:11.205
and oysters are an aphrodisiac.

04:10:11.205 --> 04:10:13.330
I don't know who's doing
the marketing for oysters,

04:10:13.330 --> 04:10:15.080
but it's really terrific.

04:10:15.080 --> 04:10:16.690
I think that seems
to have persisted.

04:10:16.690 --> 04:10:19.510
And maybe it's true.

04:10:19.510 --> 04:10:21.040
Oysters are enriched in zinc.

04:10:21.040 --> 04:10:23.870
What does zinc do for fertility?

04:10:23.870 --> 04:10:26.740
Well, in males, we know,
based on a really nice set

04:10:26.740 --> 04:10:29.230
of studies, that
zinc dosages that

04:10:29.230 --> 04:10:31.720
are pretty high of
about 120 milligrams

04:10:31.720 --> 04:10:33.730
taken twice per day--

04:10:33.730 --> 04:10:37.240
that's quite a lot-- with
meals can significantly

04:10:37.240 --> 04:10:40.540
increase testosterone
and dihydrotestosterone.

04:10:40.540 --> 04:10:42.860
And this probably shouldn't
come as a surprise to us.

04:10:42.860 --> 04:10:46.540
It turns out that zinc is
highly enriched in human testes

04:10:46.540 --> 04:10:48.200
and in the testes
of other animals,

04:10:48.200 --> 04:10:49.720
including fish
and other mammals.

04:10:49.720 --> 04:10:54.760
And it was actually in 1921
that it was observed in fish

04:10:54.760 --> 04:10:58.540
that zinc levels skyrocket
in the testes of fish

04:10:58.540 --> 04:11:00.020
during their breeding season.

04:11:00.020 --> 04:11:02.973
So zinc is correlated with
increases in breeding,

04:11:02.973 --> 04:11:04.390
but you never know
which direction

04:11:04.390 --> 04:11:05.770
that correlation is running.

04:11:05.770 --> 04:11:09.560
It turns out that
zinc in both animals,

04:11:09.560 --> 04:11:13.060
including fish, other mammals,
and in humans, strongly

04:11:13.060 --> 04:11:15.550
impacts the enzymatic
functions in the testes,

04:11:15.550 --> 04:11:18.800
including the function of
androgen-binding protein.

04:11:18.800 --> 04:11:20.380
So it seems that
high levels of zinc

04:11:20.380 --> 04:11:22.750
can increase spermatogenesis
and testosterone

04:11:22.750 --> 04:11:25.193
levels very significantly.

04:11:25.193 --> 04:11:26.860
This was explored in
a really nice study

04:11:26.860 --> 04:11:27.880
that I'll provide
a reference to.

04:11:27.880 --> 04:11:28.730
It's an older study.

04:11:28.730 --> 04:11:29.560
But I really like.

04:11:29.560 --> 04:11:31.310
It's called "Effect
of Zinc Administration

04:11:31.310 --> 04:11:33.550
on Plasma Testosterone,
Dihydrotestosterone,

04:11:33.550 --> 04:11:34.750
and Sperm Count."

04:11:34.750 --> 04:11:38.290
This is but just one
study among many now.

04:11:38.290 --> 04:11:41.410
This dates back to 1981,
but there have been studies

04:11:41.410 --> 04:11:43.810
subsequently that point to
the fact that supplementation

04:11:43.810 --> 04:11:45.518
with zinc at those
high levels can really

04:11:45.518 --> 04:11:48.400
be helpful in
terms of increasing

04:11:48.400 --> 04:11:51.040
sperm count,
testosterone, and even

04:11:51.040 --> 04:11:53.030
testicular size, of all things.

04:11:53.030 --> 04:11:55.750
So one important
point about taking

04:11:55.750 --> 04:11:59.225
zinc-- this 120 milligrams
of zinc two times daily

04:11:59.225 --> 04:12:00.850
definitely needs to
be done with meals.

04:12:00.850 --> 04:12:02.920
If you've ever taken
zinc on an empty stomach,

04:12:02.920 --> 04:12:05.590
even if you just take 15
or 30 milligrams of zinc,

04:12:05.590 --> 04:12:09.100
you can feel very nauseous,
not well, for a few hours.

04:12:09.100 --> 04:12:11.830
So make sure that you're
taking zinc with full meals.

04:12:11.830 --> 04:12:14.590
So this would mean that
you're taking in at least

04:12:14.590 --> 04:12:17.830
two full meals per day.

04:12:17.830 --> 04:12:20.260
I should also mention that
zinc supplementation did not

04:12:20.260 --> 04:12:23.200
appear to impact
gonadotropin-releasing hormone

04:12:23.200 --> 04:12:23.890
or prolactin.

04:12:23.890 --> 04:12:26.290
So it seems to be a
fairly targeted effect

04:12:26.290 --> 04:12:28.840
on the testosterone and
related pathways in males.

04:12:28.840 --> 04:12:32.080
As far as I know, there have
not been systematic explorations

04:12:32.080 --> 04:12:35.325
of the effects of high levels of
zinc administration on females.

04:12:35.325 --> 04:12:37.450
I would hope that those
studies would soon be done.

04:12:37.450 --> 04:12:39.280
But meanwhile, if
you're a male and you're

04:12:39.280 --> 04:12:40.930
interested in
improving sperm quality

04:12:40.930 --> 04:12:44.020
and your testosterone levels
overall for whatever reason,

04:12:44.020 --> 04:12:46.000
zinc likely is a good candidate.

04:12:46.000 --> 04:12:48.280
And that pretty much
summarizes the compounds

04:12:48.280 --> 04:12:50.350
that men and women
should take in order

04:12:50.350 --> 04:12:53.157
to maximize egg quality,
sperm quality, and fertility.

04:12:53.157 --> 04:12:54.740
And then, of course,
we start to enter

04:12:54.740 --> 04:12:57.500
the landscape of other things
that men and women can take

04:12:57.500 --> 04:13:00.260
in order to improve fertility,
and those other things

04:13:00.260 --> 04:13:02.390
generally are
prescription drugs.

04:13:02.390 --> 04:13:04.815
And so I just want to mention
what a few of those are.

04:13:04.815 --> 04:13:07.190
But of course, these are things
that you would absolutely

04:13:07.190 --> 04:13:11.030
have to obtain prescriptions
for from your MD,

04:13:11.030 --> 04:13:14.300
and your MD, without
question, would

04:13:14.300 --> 04:13:17.220
want to take blood tests prior
to prescribing these things.

04:13:17.220 --> 04:13:19.400
So for instance,
if men have been

04:13:19.400 --> 04:13:22.100
taking exogenous
testosterone through the use

04:13:22.100 --> 04:13:24.560
of anabolic steroids, like
performance-enhancing drugs

04:13:24.560 --> 04:13:26.540
or even testosterone
replacement therapy,

04:13:26.540 --> 04:13:28.190
their endogenous
testosterone levels

04:13:28.190 --> 04:13:30.193
are going to be very low,
and their sperm counts

04:13:30.193 --> 04:13:32.360
are going to be very low,
unless, for instance, they

04:13:32.360 --> 04:13:33.890
are prescribed and
taking something

04:13:33.890 --> 04:13:37.550
like hCG, human chorionic
gonadotropin, which

04:13:37.550 --> 04:13:40.160
mimics LH and would stimulate
the testes to produce

04:13:40.160 --> 04:13:43.400
testosterone and through
some indirect pathways rescue

04:13:43.400 --> 04:13:45.830
spermatogenesis, although
not to the same degree

04:13:45.830 --> 04:13:49.100
as if people are not
taking exogenous sources

04:13:49.100 --> 04:13:50.330
of testosterone.

04:13:50.330 --> 04:13:54.320
Some men, even if they've
never touched TRT or exogenous

04:13:54.320 --> 04:13:57.290
testosterone of any
kind, will be prescribed

04:13:57.290 --> 04:13:59.420
to take hCG because
of its ability

04:13:59.420 --> 04:14:01.310
to stimulate the
testes to produce

04:14:01.310 --> 04:14:02.700
more testosterone and sperm.

04:14:02.700 --> 04:14:04.610
So they're just
taking hCG alone.

04:14:04.610 --> 04:14:05.840
Other men will take--

04:14:05.840 --> 04:14:07.430
or will be prescribed, rather--

04:14:07.430 --> 04:14:10.640
FSH in order to stimulate
spermatogenesis, or hCG

04:14:10.640 --> 04:14:14.180
and FSH, or clomiphene,
which can regulate

04:14:14.180 --> 04:14:16.490
all sorts of things in
the both testosterone and

04:14:16.490 --> 04:14:20.810
estrogen-related pathways at
the level of brain and pituitary

04:14:20.810 --> 04:14:23.540
and gonad, testes.

04:14:23.540 --> 04:14:25.850
Likewise, for women,
if they're low in FSH,

04:14:25.850 --> 04:14:27.770
they might be prescribed FSH.

04:14:27.770 --> 04:14:30.680
If they are low in
luteinizing hormone,

04:14:30.680 --> 04:14:32.150
they might be prescribed hCG.

04:14:32.150 --> 04:14:33.710
If they're low in
testosterone, they might even

04:14:33.710 --> 04:14:34.850
be prescribed testosterone.

04:14:34.850 --> 04:14:36.410
And if their
testosterone is too high

04:14:36.410 --> 04:14:37.880
and they're dealing
with PCOS, they

04:14:37.880 --> 04:14:40.820
might be prescribed
anti-androgens and androgen

04:14:40.820 --> 04:14:43.320
blockers and on and on and on.

04:14:43.320 --> 04:14:45.260
There are so many
different hormones that

04:14:45.260 --> 04:14:47.600
can impact the different
aspects of the ovulatory

04:14:47.600 --> 04:14:51.950
and the spermatogenesis
cycle that the OB/GYNs

04:14:51.950 --> 04:14:55.040
and the urologists focused on
male fertility nowadays really

04:14:55.040 --> 04:14:57.830
have an excellent handle
on which levers and buttons

04:14:57.830 --> 04:15:00.590
and threads to pull and
push and so forth in order

04:15:00.590 --> 04:15:03.140
to set in motion
a proper ovulatory

04:15:03.140 --> 04:15:06.080
cycle and a proper
spermatogenesis cycle.

04:15:06.080 --> 04:15:08.305
Everything we talked
about up until now

04:15:08.305 --> 04:15:09.930
and in the early
phase of this episode,

04:15:09.930 --> 04:15:12.920
especially, about how
the brain commands

04:15:12.920 --> 04:15:15.890
the pituitary and the pituitary
commands the gonads and then

04:15:15.890 --> 04:15:17.720
the gonads, the
ovary, or the testes

04:15:17.720 --> 04:15:20.000
send feedback signals
to the pituitary

04:15:20.000 --> 04:15:21.980
to then influence
the pituitary, all

04:15:21.980 --> 04:15:24.440
of that incredible
orchestra, that dance,

04:15:24.440 --> 04:15:27.920
is so tightly regulated in
a way that really provides

04:15:27.920 --> 04:15:29.990
the OB/GYNs and
the fertility docs

04:15:29.990 --> 04:15:33.260
concerned with male fertility
exceptional tools to,

04:15:33.260 --> 04:15:36.860
for instance, figure out if a
man is not producing any sperm

04:15:36.860 --> 04:15:40.280
but his testosterone levels
are well within normal range,

04:15:40.280 --> 04:15:43.018
well, then there are some very
clear sets of explorations

04:15:43.018 --> 04:15:44.060
and potential treatments.

04:15:44.060 --> 04:15:45.768
Some of which are
mechanical, making sure

04:15:45.768 --> 04:15:47.690
the epididymis and vas
deferens are clear,

04:15:47.690 --> 04:15:49.790
allowing the sperm to
enter the ejaculate

04:15:49.790 --> 04:15:51.470
and the ejaculate
to enter the urethra

04:15:51.470 --> 04:15:55.930
and obviously to enter
the female, as well

04:15:55.930 --> 04:15:57.880
as for a woman
who's not ovulating

04:15:57.880 --> 04:16:02.650
to adjust her levels of FSH or
maybe even to apply acupuncture

04:16:02.650 --> 04:16:04.390
in conjunction with
supplementation

04:16:04.390 --> 04:16:07.870
and various prescription
hormone therapies to adjust

04:16:07.870 --> 04:16:10.060
fertility and ovulation
and the probability

04:16:10.060 --> 04:16:11.930
of successful pregnancy.

04:16:11.930 --> 04:16:14.560
So there's a vast landscape
of prescription drugs

04:16:14.560 --> 04:16:17.350
and surgical interventions
of varying degrees

04:16:17.350 --> 04:16:19.330
of invasiveness.

04:16:19.330 --> 04:16:23.140
And some are, for instance,
outpatient procedures.

04:16:23.140 --> 04:16:25.270
Some require general
anesthesia, et cetera,

04:16:25.270 --> 04:16:28.390
in order to maximize male
and female fertility.

04:16:28.390 --> 04:16:31.810
What I've tried to do
today is to provide you

04:16:31.810 --> 04:16:36.390
with a deep dive understanding
of the ovulatory and menstrual

04:16:36.390 --> 04:16:36.890
cycle.

04:16:36.890 --> 04:16:38.710
We talked about the brain,
the pituitary, the ovary,

04:16:38.710 --> 04:16:40.130
the Fallopian
tubes, and, in fact,

04:16:40.130 --> 04:16:41.770
the whole female
reproductive axis

04:16:41.770 --> 04:16:46.150
as it relates to
fertility and reproduction

04:16:46.150 --> 04:16:50.620
I also describe the male
reproductive axis as it relates

04:16:50.620 --> 04:16:53.200
to the brain, the pituitary,
the gonad, the testes,

04:16:53.200 --> 04:16:55.180
and the various
ducts, the pathways,

04:16:55.180 --> 04:16:59.800
out of the testes that allow
the sperm to be enriched

04:16:59.800 --> 04:17:02.290
within the semen and then
the semen and the ejaculate

04:17:02.290 --> 04:17:04.150
to exit through the urethra.

04:17:04.150 --> 04:17:06.850
I did all that as a way
to frame the various tools

04:17:06.850 --> 04:17:09.070
and interventions
that can really

04:17:09.070 --> 04:17:13.400
assist in increasing fertility,
egg quality, and sperm quality.

04:17:13.400 --> 04:17:15.580
So when we discuss
mitochondria in the context

04:17:15.580 --> 04:17:18.610
of the development of an egg
or the development of sperm

04:17:18.610 --> 04:17:21.700
and its ability to
swim quickly forward,

04:17:21.700 --> 04:17:23.620
now it should make
sense as to why

04:17:23.620 --> 04:17:25.120
give an intervention,
whether or not

04:17:25.120 --> 04:17:26.537
it's L-carnitine
or whether or not

04:17:26.537 --> 04:17:28.912
it's exercise or whether or
not it's getting enough sleep

04:17:28.912 --> 04:17:31.270
and limiting stress, why all
that should matter and why,

04:17:31.270 --> 04:17:34.765
in fact, mechanistically
those interventions can work.

04:17:34.765 --> 04:17:36.640
Because, indeed, there
are many interventions

04:17:36.640 --> 04:17:40.330
that we can all do and use
to support our fertility.

04:17:40.330 --> 04:17:42.520
And again, as a more
general theme today,

04:17:42.520 --> 04:17:44.710
I really wanted to,
A, teach you about

04:17:44.710 --> 04:17:46.600
the human reproductive axis--

04:17:46.600 --> 04:17:50.230
I do find the biology of the
ovulatory and menstrual cycle

04:17:50.230 --> 04:17:53.400
and spermatogenesis to be
absolutely fascinating to me.

04:17:53.400 --> 04:17:55.900
And again, if you're somebody
who's interested in conceiving

04:17:55.900 --> 04:17:57.730
or if you've already
conceived children

04:17:57.730 --> 04:17:59.650
and even if you don't
want more children,

04:17:59.650 --> 04:18:02.260
this is really the
aspect of our biology

04:18:02.260 --> 04:18:04.450
that allowed us to be here.

04:18:04.450 --> 04:18:07.840
It's the aspect of our biology
that determined whether or not

04:18:07.840 --> 04:18:09.100
we are male or female.

04:18:09.100 --> 04:18:11.740
It's the aspect of our biology
that determines so, so much,

04:18:11.740 --> 04:18:14.470
and yet I think that most
of us generally are not

04:18:14.470 --> 04:18:16.660
taught this in school or
at least not at the depth

04:18:16.660 --> 04:18:18.370
that we discussed it today.

04:18:18.370 --> 04:18:21.070
So hopefully that information
was in and of itself

04:18:21.070 --> 04:18:23.420
interesting and
perhaps useful as well.

04:18:23.420 --> 04:18:25.210
And I do think that
even if people are not

04:18:25.210 --> 04:18:28.060
wishing to conceive more
children that the information

04:18:28.060 --> 04:18:30.910
related to fertility and
optimizing egg and sperm health

04:18:30.910 --> 04:18:35.200
is of value in the sense that
optimizing egg and sperm health

04:18:35.200 --> 04:18:39.070
can be used as a proxy for
optimizing our body and brain

04:18:39.070 --> 04:18:39.820
health generally.

04:18:39.820 --> 04:18:44.050
In other words-- and here I'm
admittedly taking words out

04:18:44.050 --> 04:18:46.870
of the mouths of the
various wonderful doctors,

04:18:46.870 --> 04:18:50.350
the OB/GYNs and neurologists
that helped inform me

04:18:50.350 --> 04:18:52.900
in anticipation of this
episode-- what is good

04:18:52.900 --> 04:18:55.030
for the woman is
good for the egg

04:18:55.030 --> 04:18:57.100
and for fertility
and for pregnancy.

04:18:57.100 --> 04:19:01.420
And what's good for the
man is good for the quality

04:19:01.420 --> 04:19:05.560
and production of sperm and
for fertility and pregnancy.

04:19:05.560 --> 04:19:08.920
Put differently, whether or
not we are male or female,

04:19:08.920 --> 04:19:11.650
the things that we can do
to optimize our fertility

04:19:11.650 --> 04:19:14.140
are the exact same
things that we should all

04:19:14.140 --> 04:19:17.570
be doing to optimize our
vitality and our longevity.

04:19:17.570 --> 04:19:20.590
And I realize today's episode
